{"parentUuid":"bb5c7874-e306-4327-9950-3d1e7805ca35","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"048ce1b3-8891-4aae-bdd2-33b7fc094ee0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HxRm5rFk3syksgjUqAiynT","type":"tool_result","content":"3:**v13** — pour la tranche 3 du jalon 4 (encapsulation complète, `OB-C28`) : ajout des témoins W-GI et W-RX et des faits attendus sous l'encapsulation complète (§ 2 duodecies) ; les faits du § 2 undecies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`, § Passe finale). Aucun verdict de la v12 n'est modifié. **v12** — pour la passe finale de la couche R : ajout des faits attendus sous la rédaction finale de l'amendement de C22 point 4 et sous l'amendement proposé de C13 (§ 2 undecies) ; les verdicts et faits du § 2 decies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`, § Passe corrective). Deux faits du § 2 decies changent parce que le texte de l'amendement a changé : ils sont signalés au § 2 undecies. **v11** — pour la passe corrective de la couche R : ajout des faits attendus sous les deux amendements proposés, des jumeaux positifs des trois contre-exemples, du témoin `depend` et du témoin d'autorité W-NC (§ 2 decies) ; les verdicts et faits du § 2 nonies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`). Aucun verdict de la v10 n'est modifié. **v10** — pour la couche R (réalisation du mutex de référence) : ajout de la réalisation déclarée, du témoin d'autorité W-RC et des faits attendus sur les graphes du contrôleur (§ 2 nonies) ; les faits du § 2 octies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-events.md`, § Arête stricte du mutex). Aucun verdict de la v9 n'est modifié. **v9** — pour la correction de l'arête du mutex : ajout de l'arête stricte et des témoins W-RL₀, W-RL, W-RL-J, W-TR, W-TR-J (§ 2 octies) ; les faits du § 2 septies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-events.md`). Aucun verdict de la v8 n'est modifié. **v8** — pour la première passe sur les événements : ajout des jumeaux synchronisés des témoins de passation et des faits attendus au niveau du graphe d'événements (§ 2 septies). Aucun verdict de la v7 n'est modifié. **v7** — après l'extension aux droits sur les places (rapport `spec2-m4-handoff.md`, § Extension) : W-GS est confirmé par le modèle. Aucun verdict de la v6 n'est modifié. **v6** — après la mise à jour du rapport `spec2-m4-handoff.md` (test de `ChainExcl`) : statut de W-GC mis à jour ; ajout du témoin W-GS (§ 2 sexies). Aucun verdict de la v5 n'est modifié. **v5** — après le rapport `spec2-m4-handoff.md` : W-GR est confirmé par le modèle ; ajout du témoin W-GC (§ 2 quinquies) ; précision sur la mise en place de S10b. Aucun verdict de la v4 n'est modifié. **v4** — après le rapport de clôture `spec2-m3-close.md` : deux verdicts alignés sur le critère P7 (mise en place de S11, W-C22.2), ajout du témoin W-GR (§ 2 ter) et du cas S10b (§ 2 quater). Aucun autre verdict n'est modifié. **v3** — ajout des témoins de passation (§ 2 bis) ; aucun verdict de la v2 n'est modifié. **v2** — corrections après le rapport `spec2-m3.md` et sa revue ; chaque changement est listé en § 5. Les verdicts corrigés le sont depuis la Spec 1 et WC4, pas depuis le modèle.\n325:## 2 duodecies. Encapsulation complète — C22 point 6 (ajout v13)\n419:| § 2 duodecies (v13) | — | témoins W-GI et W-RX ; faits attendus sous l'encapsulation complète | WC5.2 C22 point 6, `OB-C28` ; Spec 1 §43, §77 ; rapport `spec2-m4-handoff.md`, § Extension aux droits sur les places |\n     421 corpus-spec2-m3.md\n1:# ERN — Concurrency Model Specification v0\n3:## Working Candidate 5.2 — Execution Contexts, Authority Transmission, and Concurrent Event Semantics **[WC5.2]**\n21:# I. Concurrent Execution Machine\n23:## C1. Execution Contexts\n33:## C2. Concurrent State and External Contracts\n53:## C3. Frame Ancestry — H1\n71:## C4. Context Creation — `spawn`\n96:## C5. Provisional By-Value Transmission at `spawn`\n124:## C6. Frame Exit and Reparenting\n141:## C7. Context Termination — `terminate`\n157:## C8. Reference Completion Operation — `join`\n169:## C9. Cross-Context Authorities and Dependencies\n185:## C10. External Contexts\n195:# II. Synchronized Authority Derivation\n197:## C11. Separation of Mechanisms\n209:## C12. Synchronization Registry\n230:## C13. Reference Construction — `newMutex`\n260:## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n282:## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\n303:## C16. Reference Acquisition — `acquire` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n329:## C17. Reference Unlock — `unlock` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n353:## C18. Abandoned Grants and Recovery **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n379:## C19. Synchronized Administration\n393:# III. Invariants and Correspondence\n395:## C20. Concurrent Frame and Authority Well-Formedness\n405:## C21. Synchronization Invariant — `SyncInv`\n421:## C22. Grant Discipline and Safe Abstraction Encapsulation **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C6 (item 4); WC5.1 (item 6)]**\n463:   Enforcement of the safe interface belongs to Specs 4 and 10. Complete physical-access and effect-footprint coverage, controller correspondence, and preservation remain obligations under C23, C25, C29, `OB-C05`, `OB-C20`, and `OB-C28`.\n470:   **Verification boundary [WC5.1]:** `ChainExcl` checks the direct-exercise fragment (`derive`, `split`, `read3`, `write3`, `writeShared`), and `PlaceExcl` checks selected `HasRight` premises; their conjunction is represented exploratorily by `Encap5R`. Both guard-exclusion witnesses and the normal mutex, arena and whole-mutex-transfer witnesses have been checked in that fragment. The complete coverage of all rights and composite phases, including the `resetLock` exception, remains `OB-C28`. A kernel-`ok` step that violates this requirement is excluded by the safe abstraction but does not alter its kernel outcome.\n478:## C23. Preservation of Ordinary and Concurrent Operations\n488:## C24. Sequential Conservativity\n502:## C25. Abstract-to-Concrete Realization Obligations\n514:# IV. Open Obligations\n545:| `OB-C28` | **[WC5.1/5.2] Full C22.6 coverage:** prove the guarded-chain exclusion for all rights not yet modeled in the exploratory rule: `issue` destination rights (§77.2, §77.6) and its internal phases; `newMutex` C13.2; `unlock` C17.2–C17.4; `newArena` §§76.1–76.2; the special `resetLock` C18.1 recovery rule (confirmed not enforced by any current `Encap5R` conjunct, although `ResetLockOk` admits a free lock with `grant = none`); and authorities grounding rights in `transfer` §63.4, `endUse` §69.2 and `free` §70.3 (including applicable `spawnVal` phases). Check other remaining compound rights and `reset` phases, enforce the restriction in the safe interface, prove relevant preservation, and test legitimate operations with a live mutex as well as the no-live-mutex case. |\n551:# V. Adversarial Corpus — Corrected Seed Cases\n581:### Guarded-Chain and Transfer Witnesses — Corpus §§ 2 ter–2 sexies and S10b **[WC5.1]**\n589:| **W-GS** — right on a place used by `store` | The mutex owner `c0` shares only the controller right with `c1`, then performs `store(z2,T)` **without** acquiring the grant; the kernel admits this operation. `c1 : acquire(e)` and `c1 : read3(T)` through its grant are also kernel-`ok`. | `Encap5C` still admits the unguarded `store`, because `ChainExcl` covers direct exercised authority arguments but not `HasRight(T)`. The tested `PlaceExcl` excludes this step, while `c0 : acquire(e); store(z2,T); unlock(e)` is admitted by `Encap5R`. Remaining `PlaceExcl` premise coverage is tracked by `OB-C28`. |\n592:### Handoff Witnesses — Corpus §§ 2 bis and 2 septies (authority and abstract-event verdicts proved) **[WC5.1 — M4]**\n617:### Finite Event-Model Witnesses — G1–G19 **[WC5.2 — M4]**\n637:### Controller Realization and Encapsulation Witnesses **[WC5.2 — M4]**\n660:# VI. Exploratory Verification Requirements\n664:## Milestone 1 — Abstract Model\n679:## Milestone 2 — Refinement\n685:## Milestone 3 — Adversarial Validation\n693:## Milestone 4 — Event Model, Handoff, and Data-Race-Freedom Validation\n707:**Still open [WC5.2 — M4]:** complete C22.6 premise coverage (`OB-C28`) and safe-interface enforcement; physical byte and within-step marker correspondence (`OB-C20`); all-context ordering of the non-atomic `newMutex` initialization; actual target `rf`/`mo` and full `LockOrder` refinement (`OB-C05`); failed-CAS retries and controller relocation; additional atomic units, global `seq_cst`, release sequences and the no-thin-air choice; complete DRF and safe-program soundness. `HandoffOrderedS` has been demonstrated on **six positive traces**, but has not been established for every safe program (`OB-C24`).\n714:4. **Authority handoff [WC5.1]:** retain the already proved `cap5_drop_own` (28 step kinds), `cap5_compat`, `cap5_sound_C` and `handoff_loss_exists_C` with their exact hypotheses and **`read3`/`write3`/`writeShared` scope**. Complete C22.6 premise coverage (`OB-C28`) and extend the access proof to physically realized operations (`OB-C20`); `lossStep_own` now establishes the strictly intervening, own-context loss step and `po(e1,r)` in the one-event-per-step graph; `handoffOrdered_no_raceS` proves the scoped composition if C46 ordering is supplied. Physical marker placement and protocol-wide C46 establishment remain open. Context-exclusive handoff for ordinary leaves and D-C9 mixed atomic/ordinary pairs remains an event/interface obligation. Do not confuse R4 simultaneous non-conflict with event ordering.\n731:# VII. Concurrent Event Model — Proposed Block C\n735:## C26. Executions, Abstract Steps, and Event Graphs\n751:## C27. Event Attributes and Realization Origin\n765:## C28. Program Order, Lifecycle Markers, and Within-Step Order\n786:## C29. Pure-Authority Erasure and Concrete-Access Coverage\n798:# VIII. Conflicts, Ordering, and Consistency — Proposed Block C\n800:## C30. Byte-Level Conflicts and Access Pairs\n808:## C31. Reads-From and Modification Order\n819:## C32. Synchronizes-With — `sw`\n831:## C33. Happens-Before and Data Races\n852:## C34. Admissible Event Graphs and Reference Memory Models\n881:# IX. Shared-Mutation Disciplines and Atomics — Proposed Block D\n883:## C35. Companion Shared-Mutation Contract — `SharedDiscipline`\n899:## C36. Classification of Inherited Accesses — D-C2\n911:## C37. Concurrent Atomic Read — `readShared`\n928:## C38. Atomic Units, Concrete Layouts, and Multi-Leaf Writes — D-C5\n938:## C39. Atomic Shared Writes and RMWs\n946:## C40. Memory Orders and Operation Legality — D-C7\n968:## C41. Atomic Protocol Obligations and Failure Paths\n976:## C42. Exclusive Ordinary Access to Atomic Storage — D-C9\n986:# X. Inter-Context Authority Handoff — Proposed Block D\n988:## C43. Context Capability and Current-Frame Exercise **[WC5.1]**\n1002:## C44. Scope of Exclusive Handoff Ordering\n1017:## C45. Loss Marker, L1 and L2 — Scoped Authority Proofs and Open Event Obligations **[WC5.1]**\n1033:## C46. HandoffOrdered — D-C10 **[WC5.1]**\n1049:# XI. Event Realization of Reference Protocols — Proposed Block D\n1051:## C47. Spawn, Completion, and Join Events\n1061:## C48. Reference Mutex: Acquire, Unlock, and Grant Events\n1075:## C49. LockOrder, Recovery, and Delegation\n1085:## C50. Realization, Visibility, and Physical Correspondence\n1095:# XII. Safe Executions and Data-Race Freedom — Proposed Block D\n1097:## C51. EncapsulatedTrace and SafeConcurrentTrace **[WC5.1]**\n1101:1. `EncapsulatedTrace`: the safe **reference-mutex** trace contract of C22, including the WC5 D-C6 restriction against ordinary `read3(ControlOf(entry))` and **[WC5.1]** the C22.6 restriction on all right-justification holder chains traversing a live `guarded` (subject to the specific C18.1 `resetLock` exception). This restricts the **public safe interface**, not O9/O10 or any inherited kernel operation. A kernel-`ok` `read3(lock)` or a kernel-`ok` access through live `guarded` without the required grant can be outside this contract without being a counterexample to Spec 1. The exploratory `Encap5R` checks a substantial but not complete subset of C22.6; `OB-C28` tracks the remainder.\n1108:## C52. Candidate Data-Race-Freedom Theorem and Proof Partition **[WC5.1]**\n1123:The generic `Synchronized` case is **not presented as a non-circular proof**. Likewise, assuming `HandoffOrdered` in a generic trace establishes only a composition theorem. **[WC5.1]** The former L1/L2 proof boundaries in the table now have **scoped authority-machine proofs** (`cap5_drop_own`, `cap5_compat`, `cap5_sound_C`, `handoff_loss_exists_C`) for directly modeled `read3`/`write3`/`writeShared` accesses under the tested chain restriction. They are **not** proofs for physical accesses generated by `store`, `transfer`, `issue`, allocation, or other compound operations; those require `OB-C20` and complete C22.6 coverage (`OB-C28`). **[WC5.1 — M4]** The abstract graph now proves the first own-context loss marker with step-level `po` (`lossStep_own`), the **conditional** composition `HandoffOrderedS → ¬ RaceS` (`handoffOrdered_no_raceS`), negative missing-`HBS` results for W-HO/W-HO′/W-HO″, and positive ordered counterparts W-HO-J/W-HO″-J/`lc_trace`. W-RL/W-TR show why the old mutex edge was overbroad; their strict-graph failures and join-based positive companions are proved. These are scoped **one-event-per-step** results, not concrete data-race-freedom for all realizations. The substantial remaining work is physical marker placement/byte-event coverage, concrete `rf`/`mo`/`sw` and controller `LockOrder`, safe-program/interface soundness, and proving C46 for every safe execution.\n1127:## C53. Proof Boundary, Conservativity, and No Freeze\n1141:# Drafting choices\n1155:10. **[WC5.1] Guarded-chain interpretation:** C22.6 is a proposed safe-interface trace restriction. It requires at least one valid holder-chain justification avoiding any live `guarded`, not all hypothetical derivations to avoid it; the full set of right premises and relevant pre/post/intermediate states must be covered. It does not alter Spec 1 §43. `resetLock` requires the narrowly scoped C18.1 own-`guarded` exception, with the `slot`-holder justification constrained against **other** live guards. Complete Lean coverage is `OB-C28`, not a silently assumed result.\nERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.1_to_WC5.2.diff\nERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.2.md\nERN_WC5.2_3_retouches_editoriales.diff\nERN_WC5_2_FINAL.txt\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"51a93e55-4f8e-4bb9-9a25-d181456cf71b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:25:27.972Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"3:**v13** — pour la tranche 3 du jalon 4 (encapsulation complète, `OB-C28`) : ajout des témoins W-GI et W-RX et des faits attendus sous l'encapsulation complète (§ 2 duodecies) ; les faits du § 2 undecies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`, § Passe finale). Aucun verdict de la v12 n'est modifié. **v12** — pour la passe finale de la couche R : ajout des faits attendus sous la rédaction finale de l'amendement de C22 point 4 et sous l'amendement proposé de C13 (§ 2 undecies) ; les verdicts et faits du § 2 decies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`, § Passe corrective). Deux faits du § 2 decies changent parce que le texte de l'amendement a changé : ils sont signalés au § 2 undecies. **v11** — pour la passe corrective de la couche R : ajout des faits attendus sous les deux amendements proposés, des jumeaux positifs des trois contre-exemples, du témoin `depend` et du témoin d'autorité W-NC (§ 2 decies) ; les verdicts et faits du § 2 nonies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`). Aucun verdict de la v10 n'est modifié. **v10** — pour la couche R (réalisation du mutex de référence) : ajout de la réalisation déclarée, du témoin d'autorité W-RC et des faits attendus sur les graphes du contrôleur (§ 2 nonies) ; les faits du § 2 octies sont obtenus par le modèle (rapport `spec2-m4-eve