{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","id":"09330834-08b3-42fb-aebf-e88c8eafe7f7","timestamp":"2026-11-12T17:01:30.632Z","version":"2.1.321","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"9f52ff250c3bf9a62496bf9c3c72b82c93ae96b1c01a28d5faa78501f67d1ec2","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"45c91c41-1729-4366-aabb-5fb95852ad3f","keep":218,"tail":["88b18b5e87bffa23b858808ae0090cd117aa727eac6eff47ac3b523924ca5058","5792eca7001fc687204a73604f53faf4b6af6b3c6e97d8fc96f6d658f643551d","a63e9c6d8e762f35549f2f2f15a2308e7a9b062e8cb3a0b8de5dd1827578b78c"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",218,"content",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",220,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"85a18a34ee87af6de75f4dda2c685c21390b3dfc335aec85ac45e2c791f6a709"}
{"parentUuid":"f035d148-f78b-4e43-8245-d0f60a4bddbd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyPkdLrgLcByqtXZHVdo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MBqFq8g37jzCfVDvbohE6p","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ResetException.lean","content":"import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Capacity\n\n/-!\n# The `resetLock` exception\n\nBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, task 6 (WC5.2 C22 item 6, `resetLock` exception; C18 items 1 and\n4): on a `RunFull` from the initial state, every `resetLock(e)` step has a right on the `slot` of\n`e`, and on its controller, whose holder chain contains the `guarded` of no live entry other than\n`e`.\n\nThe guard-free form of C18 item 1 (`ResetExerG`) poses the chain condition by definition; what is\nproved is that it yields a right on the `slot`: the `guarded` of a live entry is held by a usable\nplace (WC5.2 C21 item 1, `SyncInv`), so its exercise goes through the third clause of Spec 1 §43.\nThe controller right has a chain without any live `guarded` (`CtrlRight5`, the guard-free form of\nC18 item 4), a fortiori without that of another live entry.\n-/\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\n\n/-- `Exer5` is antitone in the registry: removing entries removes exclusions. -/\ntheorem exer5_of_sub {s : SC} {reg reg' : SyncReg} {c a : Nat} {m : Mode}\n    (hsub : ∀ e ∈ reg', e ∈ reg) (h : Exer5 s reg c a m) : Exer5 s reg' c a m := by\n  induction h with\n  | base hg hy ha hm hf => exact .base (fun e he => hg e (hsub e he)) hy ha hm hf\n  | held hg hy ha hm hp _ hc ih => exact .held (fun e he => hg e (hsub e he)) hy ha hm hp ih hc\n\n/-- The right of the step on the `slot` of entry `i` and on its controller, each by a holder chain\ncontaining the `guarded` of no live entry other than entry `i` (`Exer5` over the registry without\nentry `i`; WC5.2 C22 item 6, `resetLock` exception). -/\ndef ResetRights (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg) (c i : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (st.2[i]?) (fun e =>\n    OptP (slotOf st.1 e.guarded) (fun q => ∃ b ∈ List.range st.1.A.length,\n      Exer5 st.1 (st.2.eraseIdx i) c b .modify ∧\n        ∀ l ∈ footprint st.1.P q, Allows (effective st.1.flat b l) .modify) False ∧\n    OptP (ControlOf L st.1 e) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range st.1.A.length,\n      Exer5 st.1 (st.2.eraseIdx i) c a .observe ∧ effective st.1.flat a ctl ≠ none) False) False\n\n/-- Step form of task 6: under `SyncInv` (WC5.2 C21 item 1), the guard-free forms of C18 items 1\nand 4 give the rights of `ResetRights`. -/\ntheorem resetRights_of_premG {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {c i : Nat}\n    (hinv : SyncInv L st.1 st.2.1) (hp : PremG k L st (.resetLock c i)) :\n    ResetRights L (st.1, st.2.1) c i := by\n  obtain ⟨s, reg, ar⟩ := st\n  obtain ⟨hx, hc⟩ := hp\n  simp only [ResetExerG] at hx\n  show OptP (reg[i]?) _ False\n  revert hx hc\n  cases hi : reg[i]? with\n  | none => exact fun h _ => h\n  | some e =>\n    intro hx hc\n    have he : e ∈ reg := List.mem_of_getElem? hi\n    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩\n    · cases hx with\n      | @base _ _ y hg hy ha hm hf =>\n        have hl : e.Live s := ⟨y, hy, ha⟩\n        have hg' := hinv.guarded e he hl\n        rw [hy] at hg'\n        rw [hf] at hg'\n        exact hg'.2.elim\n      | @held _ q b _ y hg hy ha hm hq hb hall =>\n        have hs : slotOf s e.guarded = some q := by\n          unfold slotOf; rw [hy]; simp [hq]\n        rw [hs]\n        exact ⟨b, List.mem_range.2 hb.lt, hb, hall⟩\n    · unfold CtrlRight5 at hc\n      revert hc\n      cases ControlOf L s e with\n      | none => exact id\n      | some ctl =>\n        rintro ⟨a, ha, hx', he'⟩\n        exact ⟨a, ha, exer5_of_sub (fun x hx => List.mem_of_mem_eraseIdx hx) hx', he'⟩\n\n/-- Brief of slice 3, task 6: on a `RunFull` from the initial state, under `DDSound`, every step\n`resetLock(i)` by `c` has a right on the `slot` of entry `i` and on its controller whose holder\nchain contains the `guarded` of no live entry other than entry `i`. -/\ntheorem resetLock_rights {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {statics : Statics}\n    {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbls : List Label} (hdd : DDSound k)\n    (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], []))\n    (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {j : Nat} (hj : j < lbls.length) {c i : Nat}\n    (hl : lbls[j] = .resetLock c i) : ResetRights L ((σ j).1, (σ j).2.1) c i := by\n  have hinv := (runFull_inv hdd hstat h0 h (Nat.le_of_lt hj)).2.1.1\n  have hp := (h j hj).1.2\n  rw [hl] at hp\n  exact resetRights_of_premG hinv hp\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1519,"cache_read_input_tokens":507169,"output_tokens":2471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2471,"cache_read_input_tokens":507169,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1519},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":16576,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MBqFq8g37jzCfVDvbohE6p":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ResetException.lean","content":"import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Capacity\n\n/-!\n# The `resetLock` exception\n\nBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, task 6 (WC5.2 C22 item 6, `resetLock` exception; C18 items 1 and\n4): on a `RunFull` from the initial state, every `resetLock(e)` step has a right on the `slot` of\n`e`, and on its controller, whose holder chain contains the `guarded` of no live entry other than\n`e`.\n\nThe guard-free form of C18 item 1 (`ResetExerG`) poses the chain condition by definition; what is\nproved is that it yields a right on the `slot`: the `guarded` of a live entry is held by a usable\nplace (WC5.2 C21 item 1, `SyncInv`), so its exercise goes through the third clause of Spec 1 §43.\nThe controller right has a chain without any live `guarded` (`CtrlRight5`, the guard-free form of\nC18 item 4), a fortiori without that of another live entry.\n-/\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\n\n/-- `Exer5` is antitone in the registry: removing entries removes exclusions. -/\ntheorem exer5_of_sub {s : SC} {reg reg' : SyncReg} {c a : Nat} {m : Mode}\n    (hsub : ∀ e ∈ reg', e ∈ reg) (h : Exer5 s reg c a m) : Exer5 s reg' c a m := by\n  induction h with\n  | base hg hy ha hm hf => exact .base (fun e he => hg e (hsub e he)) hy ha hm hf\n  | held hg hy ha hm hp _ hc ih => exact .held (fun e he => hg e (hsub e he)) hy ha hm hp ih hc\n\n/-- The right of the step on the `slot` of entry `i` and on its controller, each by a holder chain\ncontaining the `guarded` of no live entry other than entry `i` (`Exer5` over the registry without\nentry `i`; WC5.2 C22 item 6, `resetLock` exception). -/\ndef ResetRights (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg) (c i : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (st.2[i]?) (fun e =>\n    OptP (slotOf st.1 e.guarded) (fun q => ∃ b ∈ List.range st.1.A.length,\n      Exer5 st.1 (st.2.eraseIdx i) c b .modify ∧\n        ∀ l ∈ footprint st.1.P q, Allows (effective st.1.flat b l) .modify) False ∧\n    OptP (ControlOf L st.1 e) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range st.1.A.length,\n      Exer5 st.1 (st.2.eraseIdx i) c a .observe ∧ effective st.1.flat a ctl ≠ none) False) False\n\n/-- Step form of task 6: under `SyncInv` (WC5.2 C21 item 1), the guard-free forms of C18 items 1\nand 4 give the rights of `ResetRights`. -/\ntheorem resetRights_of_premG {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {c i : Nat}\n    (hinv : SyncInv L st.1 st.2.1) (hp : PremG k L st (.resetLock c i)) :\n    ResetRights L (st.1, st.2.1) c i := by\n  obtain ⟨s, reg, ar⟩ := st\n  obtain ⟨hx, hc⟩ := hp\n  simp only [ResetExerG] at hx\n  show OptP (reg[i]?) _ False\n  revert hx hc\n  cases hi : reg[i]? with\n  | none => exact fun h _ => h\n  | some e =>\n    intro hx hc\n    have he : e ∈ reg := List.mem_of_getElem? hi\n    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩\n    · cases hx with\n      | @base _ _ y hg hy ha hm hf =>\n        have hl : e.Live s := ⟨y, hy, ha⟩\n        have hg' := hinv.guarded e he hl\n        rw [hy] at hg'\n        rw [hf] at hg'\n        exact hg'.2.elim\n      | @held _ q b _ y hg hy ha hm hq hb hall =>\n        have hs : slotOf s e.guarded = some q := by\n          unfold slotOf; rw [hy]; simp [hq]\n        rw [hs]\n        exact ⟨b, List.mem_range.2 hb.lt, hb, hall⟩\n    · unfold CtrlRight5 at hc\n      revert hc\n      cases ControlOf L s e with\n      | none => exact id\n      | some ctl =>\n        rintro ⟨a, ha, hx', he'⟩\n        exact ⟨a, ha, exer5_of_sub (fun x hx => List.mem_of_mem_eraseIdx hx) hx', he'⟩\n\n/-- Brief of slice 3, task 6: on a `RunFull` from the initial state, under `DDSound`, every step\n`resetLock(i)` by `c` has a right on the `slot` of entry `i` and on its controller whose holder\nchain contains the `guarded` of no live entry other than entry `i`. -/\ntheorem resetLock_rights {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {statics : Statics}\n    {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbls : List Label} (hdd : DDSound k)\n    (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], []))\n    (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {j : Nat} (hj : j < lbls.length) {c i : Nat}\n    (hl : lbls[j] = .resetLock c i) : ResetRights L ((σ j).1, (σ j).2.1) c i := by\n  have hinv := (runFull_inv hdd hstat h0 h (Nat.le_of_lt hj)).2.1.1\n  have hp := (h j hj).1.2\n  rw [hl] at hp\n  exact resetRights_of_premG hinv hp\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4c9ca37d-cd4c-4c89-a11e-232c676fda1d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgyPkbAtJA9BTqZzULh7D","requestRef":"09330834-08b3-42fb-aebf-e88c8eafe7f7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d85894a0-28bf-4a7a-ae43-245bfd92a79b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T17:01:49.154Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
