{"parentUuid":"3b646f83-1195-46f4-8e5b-4d9c8cb5b928","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"048ce1b3-8891-4aae-bdd2-33b7fc094ee0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RsBDZP8rttrAUXuVdu3UZD","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (29.9KB). Full output saved to: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6/tool-results/b7rifefcq.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n- MM-03.3 pass 6 (arbitrages F1-F7, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p6.md` with extra section (p) (F7 progress). Arenas by holder of `internal`, `store`, `callParams` ghost field. F6 (`call_protects_params_safe`) is false as stated (counterexamples kept); F7 (a) second store accepted.\n- MM-03.3 pass 7 (arbitrages G1-G5, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p7.md` with extra sections (p) verdict changes and (q) status of NoOrphan / F6. G1 clause in EnterPre (EnterPreBase = pass-6 text), G2 leaf store with arrival clause, G3 NoOrphan proved via auxiliary RootLive, G4 AnchorOrderHeld checked in arrival states. F6 still false (ancestor, unblock by releases, exit re-anchoring); G2 guard bypassed by a helper then release/endUse/free/exit.\n- MM-03.3 pass 8 (arbitrages J1-J2, 2026-10-30, closes jalon 1 again): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p8.md`, sections (a)-(o), (p) verdict changes, (q) closing balance in four classes. J1: `SameShape` (ordered isomorphism, open question), `corr`/`mvTo` move held authorities and owned places to corresponding parts, issue to a free leaf only, `newArena` needs the arena value Init, `init_only_by_writes` over a `Step` union. Open: J1 bullets 2/3 conflict (issue into a Moved leaf of the arena value).\n- Jalon 2 pass 1 (refinement MM-03 → MM-02, arbitrages K1-K5, 2026-10-31): branch `formal/refinement_0.1` cut from `formal/access_model_0.1`, new module `Ern.MM23` (`formal/Ern/MM23.lean`, imports MM02 and MM03 unchanged), report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` sections (a)-(f). Specs now `~/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md` and `~/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`. `Repr tok L s3 s2` is decidable (structure + `decidable_of_iff`, needs `set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096`). Axiom sweep by a Lean script walking module theorems with `collectAxioms` (grep-based sweep misses namespaced cases).\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c4de5a25-33d1-4449-9de5-2df275c7fc16","timestamp":"2026-11-12T17:13:19.297Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- MM-03.3 pass 6 (arbitrages F1-F7, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p6.md` with extra section (p) (F7 progress). Arenas by holder of `internal`, `store`, `callParams` ghost field. F6 (`call_protects_params_safe`) is false as stated (counterexamples kept); F7 (a) second store accepted.\n- MM-03.3 pass 7 (arbitrages G1-G5, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p7.md` with extra sections (p) verdict changes and (q) status of NoOrphan / F6. G1 clause in EnterPre (EnterPreBase = pass-6 text), G2 leaf store with arrival clause, G3 NoOrphan proved via auxiliary RootLive, G4 AnchorOrderHeld checked in arrival states. F6 still false (ancestor, unblock by releases, exit re-anchoring); G2 guard bypassed by a helper then release/endUse/free/exit.\n- MM-03.3 pass 8 (arbitrages J1-J2, 2026-10-30, closes jalon 1 again): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p8.md`, sections (a)-(o), (p) verdict changes, (q) closing balance in four classes. J1: `SameShape` (ordered isomorphism, open question), `corr`/`mvTo` move held authorities and owned places to corresponding parts, issue to a free leaf only, `newArena` needs the arena value Init, `init_only_by_writes` over a `Step` union. Open: J1 bullets 2/3 conflict (issue into a Moved leaf of the arena value).\n- Jalon 2 pass 1 (refinement MM-03 → MM-02, arbitrages K1-K5, 2026-10-31): branch `formal/refinement_0.1` cut from `formal/access_model_0.1`, new module `Ern.MM23` (`formal/Ern/MM23.lean`, imports MM02 and MM03 unchanged), report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` sections (a)-(f). Specs now `~/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md` and `~/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`. `Repr tok L s3 s2` is decidable (structure + `decidable_of_iff`, needs `set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096`). Axiom sweep by a Lean script walking module theorems with `collectAxioms` (grep-based sweep misses namespaced cases).\n- Jalon 2 pass 2 (arbitrages L1-L8, 2026-10-31): same branch `formal/refinement_0.1`, report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md` sections (a)-(f), (f) = `simulation` hypotheses classed spec 4 / spec 11 / bibliothèque / ouverte. `Repr` = decidable `ReprB` + `MM02.WF` (L3), ghost `provOf` updated by `provStep`, `simulation` over `SimRun` (per-run obligations, `Params` fixed once), `CaseSim` 18-step run. L7 literally false with zero-size leaves (counterexample kept).\n- Jalon 3 pass 1 (validation, 2026-11-01): branch `formal/validation_0.1` cut from `formal/refinement_0.1`, new modules `Ern/HandlePool.lean`, `Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean`, `Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean`, `Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean` (lake glob `Ern.*` picks nested modules), report `formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md` sections (a)-(g). Material `~/Downloads/ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` (cases, pool contract §4, NoLock §5). Executable runners with soundness proofs (`HandlePool.prun` -> `PReach`, `MM23.Horrors.srun` -> `SimRun`) let `decide` build reached states in seconds; the MM23 layout is computed from the run's final places (one allocation per root, 8-byte leaves).\n- Derivability pass 0.1 (2026-11-03): branch `formal/derivability_0.1` cut from `formal/validation_0.1`, modules `Ern/Derived/Arena.lean` (restricted issue/reset vs split|derive+store / derive+release, `ReachableNG` without the §56 guard) and `Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean` (library stack: push/mark/rewind/grow, runner `drun`), report `formal/reports/Derivability_v0.1.md` (a)-(f) + review. Spec: `~/Downloads/ERN_Spec1_Memory_Model_specification_normative_candidate_corrigee.md` (candidate Spec 1, sections §N, ops O1-O19). Two review rounds: 12/16 then 17/20 confirmed.\n- Reference pass (2026-11-05/06): branch `reference/memory-model-v0` from main, spec `specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md` (v0 kept), modules `Ern/MemoryModel/*`, `Ern/Lib/*`, `Ern/Corpus/*`; PR ernlang/ern#2 opened 2026-11-06 after arbitrations Q1-Q28. Progress log and briefs live in the scratchpad of session c986905c (`ref/log.md`, `ref/v01/*`): read them first when resuming. PR bodies: no \"Generated with Claude Code\" line.\n- Codex-review corrections (2026-11-06, commits df96b50..5ff52b5, PR kept draft): Q17 and H49 validated by the owner that day; Q3 `freeSlot` = kernel write of the pool value's leaves; Q17 (b) restated by the owner the same day (writes through the grounding authority are permitted re-initializations; `write_through_ground_accepted` is the positive witness), commits up to 13231ee; Q3 closed by the owner the same day: disjointness (`pool_entries_meta_disjoint` via `reachable_noSelfLock`) suffices, storage ownership by the pool value not required (external storage legitimate); the earlier \"owned storage\" wording must not be reused. Owner also settled: `metaLeaves` = every pool-value leaf is a safe over-approximation (disjointness), and (c) stays at leaf/init level because S3 has no values; value-level correspondence belongs to the concrete refinement, not an open question. StaticsOK (b) chosen by the owner as a full kernel bisimulation (`Access/Rename/*`, `Renumbered.*`), under `KExt` (Satisfiable invariant under footprint/anchor/pin-leaf permutation, owner-accepted). Current AGENTS.md allows `Classical.choice`. Design and API notes for Rename are in the scratchpad of session b714fc3e (`rename-design.md`, `rename-*-api.md`).\n- Spec 2 jalon 1 (2026-11-08): branch `formal/spec2-m1` from main, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC2.md` (never committed), modules `formal/Ern/Concurrency/*` (Context, Frames, Conservativity, Sync, SyncLib, Transfer, Traces, Preservation, Reparent, SyncPreserve, Reachable), report `formal/reports/spec2-m1.md` (French, sections a–f, problems D1–D9, proposals P1–P5). Brief's axiom rule is stricter than AGENTS.md: {propext, Quot.sound} only; audit script walks `Ern.Concurrency*` theorems with `collectAxioms` (theorem values via `ConstantInfo.thmInfo`, `value?` returns none for imported theorems). Theorems 2–4 were proved by three forked agents in worktrees (`.claude/worktrees/agent-*`, branches `worktree-agent-*`, `formal/spec2-m1-forkA`), merged by copying their single new file; a fact-check agent then caught five report errors. Extra Classical.choice sources: `List.getElem?_modify`, `List.filter_eq_nil_iff`, `by_cases` on `KernelOp` equality (no DecidableEq).\n- Spec 2 jalon 1, passe corrective WC3 (2026-11-09): same branch, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC3_corrige.md` (replaces WC2, never committed), report `formal/reports/spec2-m1-wc3.md`, new module `TransferPreserve.lean` (`spawnVal_preservesC`, via yield/transfer commutation). Finding W1: WC3 C21.4 controller uniqueness fails after an Encap-admitted `transfer(M, M′)` onto a live mutex whose `slot′` is an Uninit owner of its guarded root (`EncapTraces.transfer_merges_controllers`); theorem 4 is split into `SyncCore` (all other clauses) plus `lstep_ctlUnique` for labels other than transfer. Brief asked to keep `DeriveSyncPre.authorized` unchanged although C15.3 literally keeps the frame-held alternative (W2). Definition changes that alter signatures cannot be committed module by module: commit them with their downstream fixes.\n- Spec 2 jalon 1, passe WC3.1 (2026-11-09): same branch, amendments pasted in the brief (not a file), report `formal/reports/spec2-m1-wc3-1.md`, new module `SyncInit.lean` (full theorem 4). Finding: O12 `endUse` (Spec 1 §69, leaves become Uninit, only authorities held *within* the place are released) on `ctl` or on a strict part of `slot` breaks the WC3.1 C21 initialization invariant under `Encap`; theorem 4 is proved under the proposed clause `EndUseExcl` carried by `ProposedTrace`, never inside `Encap` (the brief forbids adding Encap clauses).\n- Spec 2 jalon 1, clôture sur WC4 (2026-11-09): same branch, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC4.md` (= WC3 + WC3.1 merged, plus C22.5, C21.7, S17a/b, S18; WC3 file no longer on disk, rebuilt from the transcript for a diff), report `formal/reports/spec2-m1-close.md` (part A pass, part B milestone index). The endUse clause is now inside `Encap` (C22.5); `EndUseExcl`/`ProposedTrace` removed; T4 proved on `EncapsulatedTrace`. Citation fix found: C21.4's guarded-identity uniqueness is the second clause of its first sentence, not its second sentence.\n- Spec 2 jalon 2, raffinement (2026-11-09): branch `formal/spec2-m2` from `d77f7a6`, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_WC4.md` (\"WC4 corrigée\": WC4 minus the three X1–X3 points), modules `Concurrency/Repr.lean` (`ReprC := Repr s.flat`), `Realize.lean` (`realize`, `StepOblC`, R1 `r1_lstep`, R5, `SimRunC`, R2 `simulationC`, R3, S4 run witness by `decide`), `NonConflict.lean` (R4, R4′), report `formal/reports/spec2-m2.md`. Re-indexed ops (transfer/depend/store/enter/exit) cannot use `Refinement.r6_*` (their S3 preconditions read `ancestor`): copy the proofs with only the clauses read. Composite transfers are proved on yielded states (`KBase` from `transfers_base`) since `Repr` ignores `A`. Finding: R4's `SharedMutable` conclusion is vacuous (write3 needs effective Modify, so the intersection is empty).\n- Spec 2 jalon 3, complétude et corpus (2026-11-09): branch `formal/spec2-m3` from `e30355f`, brief `~/Downloads/brief-spec2-m3.md`, corpus `~/Downloads/corpus-spec2-m3.md` (verdicts come from it, never from the model), WC4 file named `ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC4.md` in the brief is `~/Downloads/ERN_WC4.md` on disk. Library state is `SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg`; `Encap` unchanged, read on `(st.1, st.2.1)`; arena ops `NewArenaPreC`/`IssueStepC`/`ResetStepC` in `SyncLib.lean` (issue = split then store via `opStepC`, i.e. store re-indexed on `ancestorC`; literal `IssueD` on the view rejects corpus S3 step 8, witness `S3_8_view_literal`). Unified §56 guard needs invariant `AdminSep` (cross-registry), required by T4 only for issue/reset (conditional hypothesis keeps the m1 statement). New modules `ArenaPreserve`, `ArenaConservativity`, `RealizeSound`, `Corpus/{MX,AR,Frames,S10,Witness}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m3.md` (part B = consolidated index m1–m3). Open findings: S10 corpus `reject` vs model `ok` (§63.7 silent on frame-held authorities whose anchor moves), S11 setup needs a ceded observe derivative for C14.3. Proof tips: give `(E := …)` explicitly in `IssueStepC.ok` and define states with `s.A.length` (not literals) or `decide` unification times out; `akeep_of_A (s := …) (s' := …)` converts view/flat `AKeep`; `FramesC (s.set t)` needs `framesC_set`, not defeq. Review (4 parallel read-only agents, one per lens, then one targeted re-check) found W-C22.2 \"never enabled again\" refuted by an ordinary `release` (`W_C22_2_reenable`). Never auto-fix report line numbers by script: in `a, b (:N)` lists the number belongs to the last name; re-check each fix by opening the line.\n- Spec 2 jalon 3 clôture (2026-11-10): same branch `formal/spec2-m3`, corpus v3, report `formal/reports/spec2-m3-close.md`; owner kept the three extra theorems (`S10_2_ok`, `S10_3_ok`, `W_C22_2_cycle`). Corpus v4 then aligned S11 setup and W-C22.2 on the P7 criterion.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4 passe 1, passation (2026-11-10): branch `formal/spec2-m4` from `b4d18ce`, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.md` (C43–C46 L1/L2, OB-C17/18), corpus `~/Downloads/corpus-spec2-m3.md` v4. Modules `Cap`, `Encap5`, `CapPreserve`, `Corpus/{GuardedRead,CapValues,Encap5Witness,GuardedChain,S10b,L1Evidence}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-handoff.md`. Findings: L1 false for `cap` (W-GR acquire); `cap5_sound` and `handoff_loss_exists` false because `GuardedExcl` only checks the access argument while §43 is recursive along holder chains (z stored in T, exercised via guarded); `cap5_compat` proved (`attr_compat`); L1 `cap5_drop_own : DDSound k → Cap5DropOwn k L` proved for all 28 labels (2026-11-11; `CapPreserve` + `CapDrop`, transport restricted to authorities with some effective mode, exit/endUse/free via post-state `NoDangling`, spawnVal via `create_yield`/`yield_transfers` and `KBase`). GuardedExcl/CtlExcl play no role in L1 or state-form L2; `cap5` under-reports exercise (chains through guarded), so OB-C17 not discharged for real accesses. `auth_compat` duplicates `effective_exclusive`, `footprint_ne` duplicates `exists_mem_footprint` (disclosed, not refactored). Sequential helpers worth reusing: `EndFree.OnlyReleases`, `Frames.exitG_*`, `EndFree.chain_root_unique`, `rootHeldConv_active`, `TransferPreserveAux.transfer_base`. Test of the GuardedExcl fix (2026-11-11, `Encap5C.lean`, `Corpus/GuardedChainC.lean`): `Exer5` = ExercisableAt from the current frame with no live guarded on the holder chain, `ChainExcl` requires it for derive/split/read/write/writeShared, `Encap5C ⊆ Encap5`; `cap5_sound_C` and `handoff_loss_exists_C` proved; the locked variant of the counterexample is admitted and its marker is c1's unlock (`lc_handoff_marker`); mutex-free steps always satisfy ChainExcl. ChainExcl is my proposition, not WC5's: adoption is the owner's call. Extension to rights over places (2026-11-11, brief + corpus v6 §2 sexies W-GS, `Encap5R.lean`, `Corpus/{GuardedStore,PlaceExclWitness}.lean`, commits `960fb94`..`475e297`): `HasRight5` (HasRight with Exer5), `PlaceExcl k L st` (needs arena reg, layout, contract), `Encap5R ⊆ Encap5C`; W-GS step 1 (owner `store` into T without lock via guarded held by slot, partial sharing `o := derive(root_M, Observe, {lock})`) is admitted by Encap5C and excluded by PlaceExcl; twin, lc_trace, S2(=cycle_trace5), S3 to issue, S4, S10 admitted. `placeExcl_of_noLive` needs WC5 C21.6 RegBound (spawnVal creation phase can revive a dormant entry). Open choices reported: alloc disjunction mirrored with Exer5 on §68 branch; absent objects → True (MetaRight vs ResetD). Uncovered: Grounds clauses (§63.4, §69.2, §70.3), issue dst premises, newMutex C13.2, resetLock C18.1 (Exer5 impossible: arg is the live guarded), unlock, newArena.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, event pass (2026-11-11): same branch `formal/spec2-m4`, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.1.md` (replaces WC5), corpus v8 (§2 septies: hb facts for W-HO/W-HO′/W-HO″ and twins W-HO-J, W-HO″-J, lc_trace); owner accepted écarts 10–13 of the PlaceExcl pass. Modules `Events` (Run5R, Steps5R explicit-state runs, `Ev` step/start keyed by spawn position at 2i/2i+1, PO/SW/HB = TransGen, `reachList` one-pass decision so `decide` works on hb, ExclPair, Race, `lossStep` via `find?`, HandoffOrderedAt existential), `EventsCompose` (`lossStep_own`, `handoffOrdered_no_race` under exactly the hypotheses of `handoff_loss_exists_C`), `EventsProtocols` (`spawn_orders`, `join_orders`, `lock_orders` with hb-hypothesis form + holder corollary), `Corpus/HandoffEvents`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-events.md`, commits `3a5699a`..`7700b0d`, 1726 theorems (1225 non-internal). `lossStep_own` is not a corollary of `handoff_loss_exists_C` (its drop step need not cross the compat threshold). WC5.1 C4 only says identities are fresh; `|C|` is the model (`spawnEff`). Cite only clauses actually opened this session.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, herd pass (2026-11-11): same branch, `formal/herd/` (13 C litmus tests, `run.sh`, raw `results/`, README in English), report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-herd.md`, commits `3b5e7ce`..`c4c5d15`. herd7 7.58 is at `~/.opam/default/bin/herd7` (not on PATH); pass `-model rc11.cat` (C default is `c11_partialSC.cat`), `-skipcheck <name>` skips a check, races show as `Undef` / `Flag *undef*`. herd's C dialect rejects `&local` in CAS (use a shared pointer); `*x` is non-atomic whatever the type. The three-thread lock test takes ~6.5 min. The brief's exclusivity condition (\"never both r0 = 0\") is met by legal successive acquisitions; overlap shows only by skipping `atomicity` and `coherencermw` (plus `SC` for seq_cst). Complement (same day, commits `5c27f9b`..`8ab315d`): group D `XCHG+{acq,rlx,sc}` (my B7 renamed to `XCHG+acq`), group E `RS+rel+rlx` (rc11 `rs` includes a later same-thread non-RMW atomic write; WC5.1 C48 keeps the C++20 form, so that program races there; owner wants the term \"écriture atomique non-RMW\"), and the skip-check runs are in `run.sh` with outputs `results/<test>+skip-<checks>.txt`. In zsh, `$a` holding several options is not word-split: use `${=a}` or literal arguments.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, strict mutex edge (2026-11-11): corpus v9 §2 octies (prefix P, W-RL₀, W-RL, W-RL-J, W-TR, W-TR-J), modules `EventsStrict` (`ctlAt`, `MutexGap`, `SWS` copied from `SW`, `HBS`, `RaceS`, `HandoffOrderedS`, inclusion lemmas), `EventsStrictProtocols` (`*S` versions, `lock_ordersS_gaps` finer form), `RegIndex` (`reg_stable`: registry never shortens, guarded kept per index), `Corpus/{MutexEdge,MutexEdgeStrict}`; section added to `formal/reports/spec2-m4-events.md`; commits `358ce63`..`fa4d3ec`, 1801 theorems (1275 non-internal). Encap5R admits `resetLock` unchecked (no conjunct constrains it; C22.6 exception = OB-C28). WC5.1 C13 only says \"registers\"; append/in-place is the model. This project has autoImplicit on: an unopened name in a statement becomes a variable (caught only because `decide` failed).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, tranche 2, layer E (2026-11-11): `~/Downloads/ERN_WC5_1_FINAL.md` = « WC5.1 corrigé », replaces WC5.1 for citations; the three strict-edge decisions accepted. Autonomous event fragment in `formal/Ern/Concurrency/EventModel/` (`Closure`: generic TransGen decision by table rounds + counting, no edge-order assumption; `Graph`: init = event 0, po = listing order, rf/mo as pair lists, `EventConsistent` = 5 named conjuncts; `Lemmas`; `Witness` G1–G19), all with `set_option autoImplicit false`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-eventmodel.md`; commits `978ce1d`..; 1956 theorems (1348 non-internal). Results: all G1–G19 as expected; G12 (two unsynchronized RMWs reading init) passes coherence `hb;eco?`, only conjunct 3 rejects it (no `coherencermw` analogue); G18 has a race in the fragment vs none under rc11 (release sequences).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, tranche 2, layer R (2026-11-12): corpus v10 §2 nonies (declared realization of the reference mutex, W-RC, controller-graph facts); 7 hypotheses of the brief. Modules `EventModel/Complements` (G1 backward, `hb_trans`, `hb_closure`, `eco_irrefl` under conjuncts 1–3 via an mo-rank measure), `Corpus/ResetLockRight` (W-RC: step 4 resetLock `ok` without any right on lock), `MutexReal/{Graph,Coherence,Classify,ClassifyWitness,Bridge,Witness}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`; commits `4b719a3`..`83b6adf`; 2295 theorems (1521 non-internal). Graph: init = newMutex(e), events filterMap of acquire/unlock/resetLock on registry index e, mo = index order, rf (j, j+1) per RMW; invariant and coherence need only LStep + no taken grant initially (no Encap5R); bridge needs no hyp 3, converse needs `CtlFixed` (W-TR refutes it otherwise). Classification found 3 counterexamples admitted by Encap5R (store(z, lock), alloc(owner = lock), issue(..., lock2)): C22.4 only covers read3/write3/writeShared. Review lesson: an empty footprint \"by definition\" (free/exit/terminate) is a blocking pattern; add the dying leaves and prove via `SyncInv.control` after the step (`lstep_preserves`). Cite Spec 1 only after reading `specs/` (Lean comments' § numbers are not evidence).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, layer R corrective pass (2026-11-12): proposed amendments `~/Downloads/ERN_WC5_2_amendements_proposes.md` (C22 item 4 replacement, C18 item 4) tested, not validated; corpus v11 §2 decies; owner accepted `Touches` and the `release(guarded)` observation. Modules `MutexReal/{Amend,AmendWitness,NonRegression,Classify6,Classify6Witness,ResetAmend}`, `Corpus/NewMutexRight`; commits `866849f`..`c394671`; 2397 theorems (1592 non-internal). `TouchesX` = Touches + depend's `result` place itself; `CtlRestr` reads the post-state (dead-after exception), C22.3 exception literal (`TransferExcl`/`EncapVals`); `Run6`, `RunAm` (resetLock + `CtrlRight`). Results: 3 counterexamples refused, twins and all Run5R traces (+ W-GS twin, S3, S10 restated) are Run6; spawnVal under hyp 3 proved via the short route (source leaf → `Moved`, contradicts `ctlInit`); completeness without kind restriction proved; depend clause has no necessity witness; W-NC step 3 (`newMutex` from a frame without right on lock) is ok; `Run6` over-restricts `alloc(owner = M)` (leaf-level Touches). Count lesson: lazily realized equation lemmas (`Label.termOf.eq_1`) get re-attributed to a later module that also realizes them; count new theorems by name set difference against a saved baseline dump.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, layer R final pass (2026-11-12): second version of `ERN_WC5_2_amendements_proposes.md` (final C22.4, C18.4, proposed C13.11), corpus v12 §2 undecies; owner decisions: depend clause dropped, `alloc(owner = M)` admitted, provider counts by leaves. Modules `MutexReal/{Final,FinalWitness,FinalNonRegression,Classify7,Classify7Witness,FinalAuthority,FinalCorollaries}`; commits `d51ba8c`..`5148c22`; 2462 theorems (1642 non-internal). `TouchesF` = Touches with alloc owner counted as the place itself (`l = ow`, like store/issue); `CtlRestrF`, `Encap7`, `Run7`; `NewMutexRight` = Write3Pre fields exercisable + effectiveModify on `s.view c`; `RunAmF`. `Run6 → Run7` only under `SyncInv` (C21.3 leaf) or from init: unconditional left « inachevé ». All v12 facts obtained; `alloc(provider = M, owner = lock′)` kernel ok, refused only by definition (`allocEff` ignores the provider). Lesson: never `head`-truncate an enumeration grep (missed 4 newMutex steps in `Traces.lean`); `simp` on `isAtomic`/`relCap` realizes non-internal `eq_1` lemmas that count as new theorems.\n- Spec files live in `~/Downloads/` (`ERN_Memory_model.md` = v0.2 incl. MM-03.1/03.2, `ERN_Memory_Model_v0.3_consolidee.md`, `ERN_Memory_Model_0.3.3.md` = MM-03.3 v0.2), not in `specs/`.\n\n**Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions.\n\n**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_lt_range`): sweep `#print axioms` over every theorem and replace them with local lemmas. Mathlib tactics (`set`, `tauto`) are unavailable. Reviews keep catching report errors: quote old forms from the old commit, count declarations with a command, and base an evidence claim only on a check that would fail on the defect. After fixing review findings, run a second targeted review of the fixes: in MM-03 pass 2 a fix over-rejected legitimate programs. Before calling a clause \"missing\" from an arbitrage, re-read every earlier arbitrage still in force: in pass 3 the clause needed for exitFrame_no_dangling was A4's root-holder rule, which A1 puts in WF3 and pass 2 had left out. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac: run `lake build` directly (about 2.5 min). When an arbitrage enlarges a definition used in hypotheses (pass 4: `Inv3` gained `NoDangling`), theorems whose text is unchanged silently narrow: give them only the conjunct they use. Before retiring a counterexample whose witness breaks a new invariant clause, look for another witness: pass-4 review found one and flagged the weakening as major. Check obligations against the initial state: the base frame of `S3.init` owns no place, so an obligation about it can be vacuous on reached states. A review fix can itself pick a semantic reading (pass 5: the kind conjunct of `IsInternalFor` rejected a `newArena` that D3 leaves undecided): check every fix for verdicts it changes on cases the text is silent on. Module docstrings must cite the report's own numbering, not the review's decision numbers. Arbiter-supplied theorems can be false: check them on small reached states (owned storage, a parameter that is the ancestor of another) before trying a proof. Every factual claim in the report needs a module witness, or reviewers flag it; never say \"blocked until X\" without checking escape sequences such as ending the owner value. When a precondition gains clauses, lemmas taking it as a hypothesis narrow silently: name the old precondition (pass 7: `EnterPreBase`) and give the lemmas only what they use. A guard on one operation (G2 on `store`) is usually bypassable through another (a helper authority then `release`/`endUse`/`free`/exit): look for such bypasses before claiming a configuration is excluded. A new check on an operation with a defined failure (`issue` → `fail`) must not turn that failure into `reject`. Use one adversarial reviewer per arbitrage lens; each found distinct real issues in pass 7. When a restriction rejects an old counterexample, try to rebuild a witness that satisfies the new clause before restating it as a rejection (pass 8: a same-shape destination restored `transfer_not_inv3_preserving`). Drop hypotheses a proof does not use. When cases disappear because their state is no longer reached, replay their verdicts on a new reachable state and list the drops. Machine-check every changed verdict the report lists, including the old witnesses' rejected steps. Never state \"only clause X fails\" as `X → Pre` next to `¬ X`: that is vacuous; name the other clauses (pass 8: `TransferPreBase` with an iff) and state them. Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form. `omega` proving a conjunction goal pulls `Classical.choice`: split the goal first; `omega` closing a non-arithmetic goal (e.g. `∃ l, …` from contradictory hypotheses) does too: write `exact absurd h (by omega)`. `meta` is a keyword in this Lean: never name a hypothesis `meta`. `set` (Mathlib) is unavailable: use `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩`. `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated: use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`. When `S3.Usable.mono` is applied with `rfl` for `hP`, give `(s := …) (s' := …)` explicitly or it unifies the wrong way. Simulation theorems: never quantify obligations over all translations (vacuous); put them as per-step premises of the run with parameters fixed once, and give a concrete multi-step run as witness. A universal encoding obligation (`∀ addr, decode (enc addr) = addr`) is unsatisfiable by a finite computable decode: state it per value. `lake env lean` uses the last built olean: rebuild the module before a scratch file uses new declarations. Never use an unquoted heredoc for Lean or docstrings: backticks run as shell commands; use `<<'EOF'` and pass paths by environment variable. `example`s escape a `collectAxioms` sweep: rename them to theorems in a scratch copy to check their axioms. `awk length` counts bytes, not characters: count line length in Python. Each check round finds errors in the previous round's wording: when a sentence is fixed in a docstring, grep the report for the same claim; quote arbitrages exactly (L2 said \"hypothèse des énoncés\", not \"hors langage\"); classify every item a deliverable asks to classify instead of moving it aside; a summary must not present a hypothesis restated in a conclusion as a result. Count theorem constants with internal ones (`isInternal`) and say which count you give. A callee cannot move a value out of a parameter's footprint (`ActiveDerivedOutside` counts the parameter itself): build values to transfer as callee locals. Authority ids shift with every alloc/issue/split: check them with `#eval` of `prun` prefixes before writing a case. A literal invariant from the material can fail under the full kernel extension: keep the literal statement with counterexamples and prove the parts that hold, under their own names. A runner's fallback state must be unreachable (e.g. no frame) or a statement \"the run's state is reached\" is vacuous when the run fails; give a lemma deriving success from reachability. Projecting `.2` out of an existential passes the elaborator but fails in the kernel: use `obtain`. When `step_ok_of`-style lemmas time out at `whnf`, pass the contract `k` and statics explicitly. Jalon 3 took four check rounds (11/9/9/4 confirmed): each round's fixes need their own narrow check. The list `Sublist` notation `<+` is scoped: write `List.Sublist`; `List.take_add` pulls `Classical.choice`. `omit … in` goes before the docstring. A `def` in a `variable (k : K)` section takes `k` only if it uses it: check call sites. In a multi-line `{ st with … }`, put each field on its own line at one column. Theorems stated for registered arenas (`ar ∈ s.arenas`) do not carry over to library instances: never cite them for one. Before writing \"the only effect of X is Y\", look for a witness in the other direction (derivability: the missing guard also turned a `fail` into an `ok`).\n- Spec 1 v0.1 validated and frozen by the owner on 2026-11-06: file stays `specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md` (project convention: version in the file name; an unversioned rename in 3f9fee2 was reverted by 9b33c26 on 2026-11-07); v0 file deleted, owner tags `memory-model-v0` on main. PR ernlang/ern#2 ready for review, not merged. Inter-spec boundaries: KExt (§42), §86 typing → Spec 4, MM3-H H16 → Spec 3, MM23-H16 → Spec 8 (address) + Spec 11 (width/encoding); the lowest-address rule is a non-normative reference realization, not §82.3. Next-revision note: §81 omits Spec 8. Owner rule: Lean comments carry no decision history (dates, validations, restatements).\n- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — Frenc","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6/tool-results/b7rifefcq.txt","persistedOutputSize":30653},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1a55436b-663f-4784-bd8d-826cf6b7875a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b646f83-1195-46f4-8e5b-4d9c8cb5b928","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
