{"parentUuid":"7228db31-f98d-4f35-a768-4799bd653e82","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyQwLr6biEHU6bJn4y3h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ApV1EiT9jfcira1MN5HNdk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 493,511p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; sed -n 545,566p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; sed -n 589,596p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; sed -n 981,996p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; grep -n \"§2 \\|§2)\" formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/*.lean | head","description":"Read Spec 1 §42, §46, §47, §50, §80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":582977,"output_tokens":287,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":408,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":287,"cache_read_input_tokens":582977,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":408},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":1845,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ApV1EiT9jfcira1MN5HNdk":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern && sed -n 493,511p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; sed -n 545,566p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; sed -n 589,596p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; sed -n 981,996p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; grep -n \"§2 \\|§2)\" formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/*.lean | head","description":"Read Spec 1 §42, §46, §47, §50, §80"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01ApV1EiT9jfcira1MN5HNdk":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8c225d84-897b-4e99-9666-5aa8a7cb486c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgyQwLZUvuEGTgLve3txh","requestRef":"49d1e62e-afa7-4d80-a658-2bfd9de7283e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3bef243-c6b6-42d4-a921-5de5875a7ea9","timestamp":"2026-11-12T17:17:06.482Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"c3bef243-c6b6-42d4-a921-5de5875a7ea9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"048ce1b3-8891-4aae-bdd2-33b7fc094ee0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ApV1EiT9jfcira1MN5HNdk","type":"tool_result","content":"## 42. Authorities, Modes, Holders, and Origins\n\nAn authority conceptually has the following fields:\n\n```text\nAuthority {\n    id\n    mode: Observe | Modify\n    origin?: AuthorityId\n    footprint: Set<Leaf>\n    holder: Frame | Place\n    active: Bool\n}\n```\n\n`origin` links a derived authority to its current origin. Authorities have fresh identities and well-formed origin chains. A root authority has no origin; a derived authority has one. Creating derived rights does not increase the scope or permitted mode of the origin.\n\nThe **holder** (`holder`) is not the **owner** (`owner`). An authority derived by `derive` or `split` is initially held by the current frame; `store` or a permitted transfer may make it held by a place. The derived `issue` operation proceeds through `split` followed by `store`. `release` does not release a root. There is no persistent `Suspended` field: suspension of rights is inferred from active descendants and applies leaf by leaf.\n\n## 46. Arenas as Library Administration States\n\nEach entry belongs to the library's abstract state, **separate from kernel state `S₃`**. It has the following fields:\n\n```text\nArenaEntry {\n    storage: PlaceId\n    internal: AuthorityId\n    available: Set<Leaf>\n    issued: Set<(Region, AuthorityId)>\n}\n```\n\nA region is **available if and only if each of its leaves belongs to `available`**; the empty region is always available. Issuance removes the leaves of the issued region from `available`. Reset restores all leaves of the administered storage to that set. The registry and its updates belong to the abstraction contract and create no kernel permissions.\n\nThe arena is **live** if `internal` is active. The **arena value** is the place holding `internal`, distinct from the possible owner of `storage`. Administered storage may be local, static, allocated, or issued by another arena, under `newArena` preconditions and applicable invariants. `available` and `issued` remain **in the library's arena entry**.\n\n## 47. Initial State\n\nThe kernel's initial state contains only base frame 0 and the declared static storage. Every static leaf has its declared initial state, `Init` or `Uninit`. The roots of static places directly owned by frame 0 have a root `Modify` authority held by that frame; a static may also be owned by another static, in which case its root authority is held by the latter. The ownership graph of statics is acyclic: no static is owned, directly or transitively, by itself. The initial state invents no dynamic allocation, derived authority, or implicit anchor. The initial arena registry belongs to library state and is empty. The initial frame does not exit.\n\n## 48. External Parametric Contract\n## 50. I1 — Structural Exclusivity\n\nFor two active authorities **unrelated by derivation** covering the same leaf, their own modes must both be `Observe`. This rule also applies to leaves identified as `SharedMutable`; their particular mutation is governed by the `writeShared` contract and creates no exception to I1.\n\nExclusivity of **effective** modes (`effective_exclusive`) is a consequence of I1 and the definition of `effective`, not the definition of I1. On a leaf, two incompatible authorities cannot simultaneously possess incompatible effective rights. The only permitted independent ordinary coexistence is `Observe` / `Observe`.\n\n## 51. I2 — Conservation of Rights\n\n## 80. Parametric Contracts of the Access Discipline\n\nA contract `K` parameterizes rules of the access discipline without fabricating permissions. A safe abstraction using part of `K` must prove or fulfill the corresponding obligation; an unestablished precondition is not a language guarantee.\n\n| Contract | External obligation |\n|---|---|\n| `DeclaredDisjoint` | `DDSound(K)`: no falsely declared disjoint region when leaves can overlap |\n| `Pinned` | I5, prohibition of incompatible physical moves; `StaticPinnedBottom` for pinned statics |\n| `SharedMutable` | Applicable shared-mutation discipline, with correct rights and synchronization |\n| `ExternalDone` | External use of storage has ended when `unpin` is permitted |\n| `Deallocable` | The place belongs to a unit that can actually be freed |\n| `FreeCompat` | Opaque deallocation authority is compatible with the unit being freed |\n| `Satisfiable` | The provider can satisfy the requested shape **in the current state** |\n\nStructural conditions of `free`, dependencies, and the derived library `reset` carry the relevant invalidation obligations. Physical justification of `DDSound` must be established by a realization consistent with memory layouts and Section 82.\n\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/NonRegression.lean:7:Brief of milestone 4, slice 3, task 3 (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies, \"Usages\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Inventory.lean:6:Brief of milestone 4, slice 3 (WC5.2 C22 item 6, `OB-C28`; `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies).\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ResetException.lean:106:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-RX: in twin B, the `resetLock(e_n)` step has both\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:8:`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies. One theorem per expected fact, preconditions by `decide`;\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:108:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, step 1, `ok` (Spec 1 §77.1: `MetaRight` over\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:116:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, step 2, `ok` (WC5.2 C14 items 1–3 through `o`,\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:121:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, step 3, `ok` (O9): `read3(t)` via `g₁` by\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:143:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, \"sous l'encapsulation actuelle\": steps 1 to 3 are\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:149:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, \"sous l'encapsulation complète\": step 1 is\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:186:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, twin: `c0 : acquire(e)`, `c0 : issue(arena0, R1,","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"73b5e147-50cc-489b-b577-673b15f646e9","timestamp":"2026-11-12T17:17:07.122Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 42. Authorities, Modes, Holders, and Origins\n\nAn authority conceptually has the following fields:\n\n```text\nAuthority {\n    id\n    mode: Observe | Modify\n    origin?: AuthorityId\n    footprint: Set<Leaf>\n    holder: Frame | Place\n    active: Bool\n}\n```\n\n`origin` links a derived authority to its current origin. Authorities have fresh identities and well-formed origin chains. A root authority has no origin; a derived authority has one. Creating derived rights does not increase the scope or permitted mode of the origin.\n\nThe **holder** (`holder`) is not the **owner** (`owner`). An authority derived by `derive` or `split` is initially held by the current frame; `store` or a permitted transfer may make it held by a place. The derived `issue` operation proceeds through `split` followed by `store`. `release` does not release a root. There is no persistent `Suspended` field: suspension of rights is inferred from active descendants and applies leaf by leaf.\n\n## 46. Arenas as Library Administration States\n\nEach entry belongs to the library's abstract state, **separate from kernel state `S₃`**. It has the following fields:\n\n```text\nArenaEntry {\n    storage: PlaceId\n    internal: AuthorityId\n    available: Set<Leaf>\n    issued: Set<(Region, AuthorityId)>\n}\n```\n\nA region is **available if and only if each of its leaves belongs to `available`**; the empty region is always available. Issuance removes the leaves of the issued region from `available`. Reset restores all leaves of the administered storage to that set. The registry and its updates belong to the abstraction contract and create no kernel permissions.\n\nThe arena is **live** if `internal` is active. The **arena value** is the place holding `internal`, distinct from the possible owner of `storage`. Administered storage may be local, static, allocated, or issued by another arena, under `newArena` preconditions and applicable invariants. `available` and `issued` remain **in the library's arena entry**.\n\n## 47. Initial State\n\nThe kernel's initial state contains only base frame 0 and the declared static storage. Every static leaf has its declared initial state, `Init` or `Uninit`. The roots of static places directly owned by frame 0 have a root `Modify` authority held by that frame; a static may also be owned by another static, in which case its root authority is held by the latter. The ownership graph of statics is acyclic: no static is owned, directly or transitively, by itself. The initial state invents no dynamic allocation, derived authority, or implicit anchor. The initial arena registry belongs to library state and is empty. The initial frame does not exit.\n\n## 48. External Parametric Contract\n## 50. I1 — Structural Exclusivity\n\nFor two active authorities **unrelated by derivation** covering the same leaf, their own modes must both be `Observe`. This rule also applies to leaves identified as `SharedMutable`; their particular mutation is governed by the `writeShared` contract and creates no exception to I1.\n\nExclusivity of **effective** modes (`effective_exclusive`) is a consequence of I1 and the definition of `effective`, not the definition of I1. On a leaf, two incompatible authorities cannot simultaneously possess incompatible effective rights. The only permitted independent ordinary coexistence is `Observe` / `Observe`.\n\n## 51. I2 — Conservation of Rights\n\n## 80. Parametric Contracts of the Access Discipline\n\nA contract `K` parameterizes rules of the access discipline without fabricating permissions. A safe abstraction using part of `K` must prove or fulfill the corresponding obligation; an unestablished precondition is not a language guarantee.\n\n| Contract | External obligation |\n|---|---|\n| `DeclaredDisjoint` | `DDSound(K)`: no falsely declared disjoint region when leaves can overlap |\n| `Pinned` | I5, prohibition of incompatible physical moves; `StaticPinnedBottom` for pinned statics |\n| `SharedMutable` | Applicable shared-mutation discipline, with correct rights and synchronization |\n| `ExternalDone` | External use of storage has ended when `unpin` is permitted |\n| `Deallocable` | The place belongs to a unit that can actually be freed |\n| `FreeCompat` | Opaque deallocation authority is compatible with the unit being freed |\n| `Satisfiable` | The provider can satisfy the requested shape **in the current state** |\n\nStructural conditions of `free`, dependencies, and the derived library `reset` carry the relevant invalidation obligations. Physical justification of `DDSound` must be established by a realization consistent with memory layouts and Section 82.\n\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/NonRegression.lean:7:Brief of milestone 4, slice 3, task 3 (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies, \"Usages\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Inventory.lean:6:Brief of milestone 4, slice 3 (WC5.2 C22 item 6, `OB-C28`; `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies).\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ResetException.lean:106:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-RX: in twin B, the `resetLock(e_n)` step has both\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:8:`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies. One theorem per expected fact, preconditions by `decide`;\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:108:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, step 1, `ok` (Spec 1 §77.1: `MetaRight` over\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:116:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, step 2, `ok` (WC5.2 C14 items 1–3 through `o`,\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:121:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, step 3, `ok` (O9): `read3(t)` via `g₁` by\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:143:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, \"sous l'encapsulation actuelle\": steps 1 to 3 are\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:149:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, \"sous l'encapsulation complète\": step 1 is\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Witness.lean:186:/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v13 §2 duodecies W-GI, twin: `c0 : acquire(e)`, `c0 : issue(arena0, R1,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8c225d84-897b-4e99-9666-5aa8a7cb486c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c3bef243-c6b6-42d4-a921-5de5875a7ea9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
