{"parentUuid":"78465fe6-c540-42f5-8914-0c289883ddf5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018gtNxsr7mEy27BJWXHpmxG","type":"tool_result","content":"/-! ## On `Run7`: W-GI -/\n\n/-- Brief of slice 3, task 5, \"faux sur `Run7`\": W-GI is a final amended execution (`Run7`) from\nthe initial state whose step 1, `c0 : issue(arena0, R1, t)`, touches the protected leaf `t` of the\nlive entry `e` without the lock: no grant is recorded and `c0` has no `cap5` on `t`. On the twin,\nunder the grant of `c0`, the same step satisfies the corollary. -/\ntheorem protected_run7_refuted : Run7 KM L0 giσ giLbls ∧\n    ¬ ProtectedOK L0 (giσ 8) (.issue 0 0 [5] 3) (giσ 9) ∧ cap5 gi6 giReg 0 3 = none ∧\n    ProtectedOK L0 (gtσ 9) (.issue 0 0 [5] 3) (gtσ 10) :=\n  ⟨W_GI_current.2.1, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ## On `RunFull`: an abandoned grant -/\n\n/-- `o := derive(root_M, Observe, {lock})`, authority 4 (O1). -/\ndef ab3 : SC := x2.set (deriveEff (x2.view 0) 0 [2] .observe)\n/-- `c0 : enterFrame([o], [])` (O6): frame 1 holds `o`. -/\ndef ab4 : SC := enterEffC ab3 0 [4] []\n/-- `c0 : acquire(e)`: grant `g`, authority 5, held by frame 1 (WC5.2 C16). -/\ndef ab5 : SC := deriveSyncEff ab4 0 3\n/-- The registry with `g` recorded. -/\ndef abReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 5⟩]\n/-- `x := derive(g, Modify, {T})`, authority 6, held by frame 1 (O1). -/\ndef ab6 : SC := ab5.set (deriveEff (ab5.view 0) 5 [3] .modify)\n/-- `c0 : spawn([x])` (WC5.2 C4): context 1, initial frame 2 holds `x`. -/\ndef ab7 : SC := spawnEff ab6 0 [6] []\n/-- `c0 : exitFrame` (O7; WC5.2 C6): frame 1 ends; `g` and `o` are released, `x` survives in\ncontext 1 and is reanchored to `guarded`. -/\ndef ab8 : SC := exitEffC ab7 0\n/-- `c1 : write3(T)` via `x` (O10). -/\ndef ab9 : SC := ab8.set (write3Eff (ab8.view 1) [3])\n\n/-- The labels of the abandoned-grant trace. -/\ndef abLbls : List Label :=\n  ClassifyWitness.mx3Lbls ++ [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [2] .observe), .kernel 0 (.enter [4] []),\n    .acquire 0 0, .kernel 0 (.derive 5 [3] .modify), .spawn 0 [6] [], .kernel 0 .exit,\n    .kernel 1 (.write 6 [3])]\n\n/-- The named states of the abandoned-grant trace. -/\ndef abσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (ab3, regX, []), (ab4, regX, []),\n    (ab5, abReg, []), (ab6, abReg, []), (ab7, abReg, []), (ab8, abReg, []),\n    (ab9, abReg, [])].getD i (ab9, abReg, [])\n\n/-- Brief of slice 3, task 5, on `RunFull`: refuted. From `MX₃`, `c0` enters a frame with the\ncontroller right `o`, acquires `e` (grant `g` held by that frame), derives `x` from `g`, yields `x`\nto a new context `c1`, and exits the frame without `unlock` (WC5.2 C18: the grant becomes inactive\nby frame exit; `x` survives in `c1` and its origin becomes `guarded`, Spec 1 §73). Then\n`c1 : write3(T)` via `x` touches the protected leaf `T` of entry `e`, live before and after, whose\nrecorded grant `g` is inactive: the capacity of `c1` comes from `x`, whose origin chain is now\n`[guarded, root_T]`, outside the subtree of `g`. Every step is admitted by the complete\n72:def x0 : SC := SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst)\n74:def x1 : SC := x0.set (deriveEff (x0.view 0) 1 [3] .modify)\n76:def x2 : SC := storeEffC x1 0 3 1\n78:def regX : SyncReg := [⟨3, none⟩]\n200:def x10 : SC := enterEffC x9 1 [6] []\n202:def x11 : SC := x10.set (write3Eff (x10.view 1) [3])\n238:def x12 : SC := exitEffC x11 1\n240:def x13 : SC := x12.set (releaseEff (x12.view 1) 5)\n319:def x2w : SC := x2.set (write3Eff (x2.view 0) [2])\n329:def x2a : SC := deriveSyncEff x2 0 3\n331:def x2u : SC := x2a.set (releaseEff (x2a.view 0) 4)\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/Encap5Witness.lean:20:theorem W_GR_1_guardedExcl : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 x4 (.ok gr1) ∧\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:26:theorem W_GR_1_ok : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 x4 (.ok gr1) := ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:30:theorem W_GR_2_ok : AcquireOk KM L0 gr1 regX 0 0 (gr2, regG) :=\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:34:theorem W_GR_3_ok : opStepC KM (.write 5 [3]) 0 gr2 (.ok gr3) :=\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:40:theorem W_GR_4_reject : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 gr2 .reject ∧ effective gr2.flat 3 3 = none :=\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedChainC.lean:26:theorem W_GR_1_excluded : ¬ ChainExcl (x4, regX) (.kernel 1 (.read 3 [3])) := by decide\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/MX.lean:136:theorem S2_3_ok : UnlockOk L0 x6 regG 1 0 (x7, regX) :=","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"570aaed9-4024-4255-9590-39d79cd194d9","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:59:44.528Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/-! ## On `Run7`: W-GI -/\n\n/-- Brief of slice 3, task 5, \"faux sur `Run7`\": W-GI is a final amended execution (`Run7`) from\nthe initial state whose step 1, `c0 : issue(arena0, R1, t)`, touches the protected leaf `t` of the\nlive entry `e` without the lock: no grant is recorded and `c0` has no `cap5` on `t`. On the twin,\nunder the grant of `c0`, the same step satisfies the corollary. -/\ntheorem protected_run7_refuted : Run7 KM L0 giσ giLbls ∧\n    ¬ ProtectedOK L0 (giσ 8) (.issue 0 0 [5] 3) (giσ 9) ∧ cap5 gi6 giReg 0 3 = none ∧\n    ProtectedOK L0 (gtσ 9) (.issue 0 0 [5] 3) (gtσ 10) :=\n  ⟨W_GI_current.2.1, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ## On `RunFull`: an abandoned grant -/\n\n/-- `o := derive(root_M, Observe, {lock})`, authority 4 (O1). -/\ndef ab3 : SC := x2.set (deriveEff (x2.view 0) 0 [2] .observe)\n/-- `c0 : enterFrame([o], [])` (O6): frame 1 holds `o`. -/\ndef ab4 : SC := enterEffC ab3 0 [4] []\n/-- `c0 : acquire(e)`: grant `g`, authority 5, held by frame 1 (WC5.2 C16). -/\ndef ab5 : SC := deriveSyncEff ab4 0 3\n/-- The registry with `g` recorded. -/\ndef abReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 5⟩]\n/-- `x := derive(g, Modify, {T})`, authority 6, held by frame 1 (O1). -/\ndef ab6 : SC := ab5.set (deriveEff (ab5.view 0) 5 [3] .modify)\n/-- `c0 : spawn([x])` (WC5.2 C4): context 1, initial frame 2 holds `x`. -/\ndef ab7 : SC := spawnEff ab6 0 [6] []\n/-- `c0 : exitFrame` (O7; WC5.2 C6): frame 1 ends; `g` and `o` are released, `x` survives in\ncontext 1 and is reanchored to `guarded`. -/\ndef ab8 : SC := exitEffC ab7 0\n/-- `c1 : write3(T)` via `x` (O10). -/\ndef ab9 : SC := ab8.set (write3Eff (ab8.view 1) [3])\n\n/-- The labels of the abandoned-grant trace. -/\ndef abLbls : List Label :=\n  ClassifyWitness.mx3Lbls ++ [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [2] .observe), .kernel 0 (.enter [4] []),\n    .acquire 0 0, .kernel 0 (.derive 5 [3] .modify), .spawn 0 [6] [], .kernel 0 .exit,\n    .kernel 1 (.write 6 [3])]\n\n/-- The named states of the abandoned-grant trace. -/\ndef abσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (ab3, regX, []), (ab4, regX, []),\n    (ab5, abReg, []), (ab6, abReg, []), (ab7, abReg, []), (ab8, abReg, []),\n    (ab9, abReg, [])].getD i (ab9, abReg, [])\n\n/-- Brief of slice 3, task 5, on `RunFull`: refuted. From `MX₃`, `c0` enters a frame with the\ncontroller right `o`, acquires `e` (grant `g` held by that frame), derives `x` from `g`, yields `x`\nto a new context `c1`, and exits the frame without `unlock` (WC5.2 C18: the grant becomes inactive\nby frame exit; `x` survives in `c1` and its origin becomes `guarded`, Spec 1 §73). Then\n`c1 : write3(T)` via `x` touches the protected leaf `T` of entry `e`, live before and after, whose\nrecorded grant `g` is inactive: the capacity of `c1` comes from `x`, whose origin chain is now\n`[guarded, root_T]`, outside the subtree of `g`. Every step is admitted by the complete\n72:def x0 : SC := SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst)\n74:def x1 : SC := x0.set (deriveEff (x0.view 0) 1 [3] .modify)\n76:def x2 : SC := storeEffC x1 0 3 1\n78:def regX : SyncReg := [⟨3, none⟩]\n200:def x10 : SC := enterEffC x9 1 [6] []\n202:def x11 : SC := x10.set (write3Eff (x10.view 1) [3])\n238:def x12 : SC := exitEffC x11 1\n240:def x13 : SC := x12.set (releaseEff (x12.view 1) 5)\n319:def x2w : SC := x2.set (write3Eff (x2.view 0) [2])\n329:def x2a : SC := deriveSyncEff x2 0 3\n331:def x2u : SC := x2a.set (releaseEff (x2a.view 0) 4)\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/Encap5Witness.lean:20:theorem W_GR_1_guardedExcl : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 x4 (.ok gr1) ∧\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:26:theorem W_GR_1_ok : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 x4 (.ok gr1) := ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:30:theorem W_GR_2_ok : AcquireOk KM L0 gr1 regX 0 0 (gr2, regG) :=\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:34:theorem W_GR_3_ok : opStepC KM (.write 5 [3]) 0 gr2 (.ok gr3) :=\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedRead.lean:40:theorem W_GR_4_reject : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 gr2 .reject ∧ effective gr2.flat 3 3 = none :=\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/GuardedChainC.lean:26:theorem W_GR_1_excluded : ¬ ChainExcl (x4, regX) (.kernel 1 (.read 3 [3])) := by decide\nErn/Concurrency/Corpus/MX.lean:136:theorem S2_3_ok : UnlockOk L0 x6 regG 1 0 (x7, regX) :=","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0d4d2c43-b169-4fe6-b87c-f8fe430b7a7d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"78465fe6-c540-42f5-8914-0c289883ddf5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classif