t try to resolve this typeclass instance problem because the second type argument to `GetElem?` is a metavariable. This argument must be fully determined before Lean will try to resolve the typeclass.\n\nHint: Adding type annotations and supplying implicit arguments to functions can give Lean more information for typeclass resolution. For example, if you have a variable `x` that you intend to be a `Nat`, but Lean reports it as having an unresolved type like `?m`, replacing `x` with `(x : Nat)` can get typeclass resolution un-stuck.\nErn/Concurrency/FullEncap/Closure.lean:190:36: error: Application type mismatch: The argument\n  fun x => ?m.14\nhas type\n  (x : ?m.12) → ?m.15 x\nbut is expected to have type\n  Decidable\n    (SyncEntry.Live st'.fst e →\n      ∀ (j : Nat),\n        j ∈ List.range st'.fst.A.length →\n          CoveringDesc st'.fst e.guarded j →\n            CoveringDesc st.fst e.guarded j ∨\n              (st.fst.A.length ≤ j ∧ ∃ o, st'.fst.flat.org j = some o ∧ CoveringDesc st.fst e.guarded o) ∨\n                ∃ c i e',\n                  lbl = Label.acquire c i ∧ st.snd.fst[i]? = some e' ∧ e'.guarded = e.guarded ∧ j = st.fst.A.length)\nin the application\n  @instDecidableForall (SyncEntry.Live st.fst e)\n    (SyncEntry.Live st'.fst e →\n      ∀ (j : Nat),\n        j ∈ List.range st'.fst.A.length →\n          CoveringDesc st'.fst e.guarded j →\n            CoveringDesc st.fst e.guarded j ∨\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Closure.lean 2>&1  0.30s user 0.28s system 36% cpu 1.617 total\nhead -70  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 1.605 total","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"01443d37-1c32-4480-b1b3-83eef03ac67c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untrack