{"parentUuid":"25060942-3a30-4c1d-b249-c0ded67a19c4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018QHfoCTSGg8RXtjxWnAQmq","type":"tool_result","content":"structure WF3 (s : S3) : Prop where\n  /-- §49.1: the stack is nonempty and duplicate-free, every frame below `nF`. -/\n  frames : s.F ≠ [] ∧ s.F.Nodup ∧ ∀ f ∈ s.F, f < s.nF\n  /-- §49.2: parent links are valid and acyclic (the parent precedes the child); a part shares\n  its parent's owner and death marker. -/\n  places : ∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (r : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.parent = some r →\n    ∃ pr : Place, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ r < q ∧ pr.owner = pl.owner ∧ s.dead r = s.dead q\n  /-- §49.3: owner frames are below `nF`; owner places exist; the ownership chain of every usable\n  place is finite and reaches a live frame. -/\n  owners : (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (f : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .frame f →\n      f < s.nF) ∧\n    (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (o : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .place o →\n      o < s.P.length) ∧\n    ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∃ f, FrameOf s q f ∧ f ∈ s.F\n  /-- §49.4: footprints consist of leaves of existing places. -/\n  footprints : ∀ (a : Nat) (x : Authority), s.A[a]? = some x → ∀ l ∈ x.footprint,\n    l < s.P.length ∧ isLeaf s.P l\n  /-- §49.5: an existing origin precedes the authority, so origin chains are acyclic and end at a\n  root authority. -/\n  origins : ∀ (b : Nat) (y : Authority) (a : Nat), s.A[b]? = some y → y.origin = some a → a < b\n  /-- §49.6: `RootChain`. -/\n  rootChain : RootChain s\n  /-- §49.7: `RootHeld`. -/\n  rootHeld : RootHeld s\n  /-- §49.8: every active authority is held by a frame of the stack or by a usable place. -/\n  holders : ∀ (a : Nat) (y : Authority), s.A[a]? = some y → y.active = true →\n    HolderLive s y.holder\n\n/-! ## `I1`–`I4`, `NoDangling`, `Inv3` (§50–§54, §57) -/\n\n/-- `I1` (§50): two distinct active authorities unrelated by derivation covering a common leaf\nboth have own mode `Observe`. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean:752:theorem usable_of_partOf {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) :\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-753-    ∀ n r q, r < n → partOf s.P r q → s.Usable q → s.Usable r\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-754-  | 0, _, _, h, _, _ => absurd h (Nat.not_lt_zero _)\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-755-  | n + 1, r, q, hr, ⟨hlen, hrq⟩, hu => by\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-756-    rcases hrq with rfl | hc\n--\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean:776:theorem usable_of_part {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {l r : Nat} (h : partOf s.P l r)\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-777-    (hu : s.Usable l) : s.Usable r := by\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-778-  obtain ⟨pl, pr, hpl, hpr, ho⟩ := hw.ownerOf h\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-779-  exact hu.of_same hpl hpr ho.symm (hw.deadOf h).symm\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-780-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"77d3e837-a8a1-4f53-abe5-d656eba0721e","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:10:33.045Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"structure WF3 (s : S3) : Prop where\n  /-- §49.1: the stack is nonempty and duplicate-free, every frame below `nF`. -/\n  frames : s.F ≠ [] ∧ s.F.Nodup ∧ ∀ f ∈ s.F, f < s.nF\n  /-- §49.2: parent links are valid and acyclic (the parent precedes the child); a part shares\n  its parent's owner and death marker. -/\n  places : ∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (r : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.parent = some r →\n    ∃ pr : Place, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ r < q ∧ pr.owner = pl.owner ∧ s.dead r = s.dead q\n  /-- §49.3: owner frames are below `nF`; owner places exist; the ownership chain of every usable\n  place is finite and reaches a live frame. -/\n  owners : (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (f : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .frame f →\n      f < s.nF) ∧\n    (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (o : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .place o →\n      o < s.P.length) ∧\n    ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∃ f, FrameOf s q f ∧ f ∈ s.F\n  /-- §49.4: footprints consist of leaves of existing places. -/\n  footprints : ∀ (a : Nat) (x : Authority), s.A[a]? = some x → ∀ l ∈ x.footprint,\n    l < s.P.length ∧ isLeaf s.P l\n  /-- §49.5: an existing origin precedes the authority, so origin chains are acyclic and end at a\n  root authority. -/\n  origins : ∀ (b : Nat) (y : Authority) (a : Nat), s.A[b]? = some y → y.origin = some a → a < b\n  /-- §49.6: `RootChain`. -/\n  rootChain : RootChain s\n  /-- §49.7: `RootHeld`. -/\n  rootHeld : RootHeld s\n  /-- §49.8: every active authority is held by a frame of the stack or by a usable place. -/\n  holders : ∀ (a : Nat) (y : Authority), s.A[a]? = some y → y.active = true →\n    HolderLive s y.holder\n\n/-! ## `I1`–`I4`, `NoDangling`, `Inv3` (§50–§54, §57) -/\n\n/-- `I1` (§50): two distinct active authorities unrelated by derivation covering a common leaf\nboth have own mode `Observe`. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean:752:theorem usable_of_partOf {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) :\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-753-    ∀ n r q, r < n → partOf s.P r q → s.Usable q → s.Usable r\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-754-  | 0, _, _, h, _, _ => absurd h (Nat.not_lt_zero _)\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-755-  | n + 1, r, q, hr, ⟨hlen, hrq⟩, hu => by\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-756-    rcases hrq with rfl | hc\n--\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean:776:theorem usable_of_part {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {l r : Nat} (h : partOf s.P l r)\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-777-    (hu : s.Usable l) : s.Usable r := by\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-778-  obtain ⟨pl, pr, hpl, hpr, ho⟩ := hw.ownerOf h\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-779-  exact hu.of_same hpl hpr ho.symm (hw.deadOf h).symm\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Lemmas.lean-780-","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"83b7bfc3-6844-427a-a76b-d093b0daa07f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlan