{"parentUuid":"c8bd1dbd-dbff-4718-ac17-4f395575df36","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, SubagentHandback, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, advisor, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Current brief: « tranche 3 : encapsulation complète, complément ».**\n   - Branch `formal/spec2-m4`; exploratory and never merged.\n   - Attachments: `ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.2.md` (unchanged); corpus v14, with §2 terdecies and the v14 wording of the « Donnée protégée » fact: « vivante avant et après le pas ».\n   - Owner decisions:\n     1. Task 5 of slice 3 is replaced by a statement in three cases (a disjunction, not an added hypothesis), complemented by the closure of the descendance.\n     2. C22 point 1: reanchoring is not an issuance.\n     3. « Entrée vivante » means live before and after the step.\n     4. The open points (spawnVal pre-state, dying leaves, unreplayed traces) are taken up in this pass.\n\n   **Tasks:**\n   1. Witnesses by `decide`:\n      - W-AG: steps 1–11 `ok` and admitted; 4 facts on step 6; refusals a–d with their failing clauses.\n      - W-AG-J: `ok` and admitted.\n      - Strict graph: W-AG has a race and no HBS; W-AG-J has a path via join.\n      - W-AG′: A1–A4, covering-descendants column, the negative.\n   2. Closure of the covering descendants on RunFull: cases (1)/(2)/(3); 28-kind table with three columns; check (2′) for composites.\n   3. Dying leaves:\n      - (i) a protected leaf doesn't die if e is live before and after;\n      - (ii) in the pre-state, no other context has cap5 on a dying leaf;\n      - which kinds kill leaves; which invariants serve; check on the exc_* witnesses.\n   4. spawnVal capacity in the pre-state (prove or find a counterexample).\n   5. Empty set without grant (is GrantDiscipline established?); last acquire (induction, no history in the state); three cases; the corpus fact as a separate theorem for the 28 kinds; which invariants serve; check on all RunFull traces, with W-AG step 7 in the third case.\n   6. Replay W-GR, W-GC, W-GS: the local verdict for the excluded step, separate from the positive RunFull suite. Replay S4, S9 and the WC4 traces (S9 expected admitted); report any refused trace.\n\n   **Report:** update `formal/reports/spec2-m4-encap.md` with a section « Complément », in French, containing:\n   - definitions and deviations from the brief;\n   - per witness: expected, obtained, clause, theorem (module:ligne);\n   - the 28-kind table of task 2 (three columns);\n   - the status of every statement of tasks 2–5 with exact hypotheses;\n   - the updated capacity table (spawnVal and dying leaves);\n   - the replayed traces, separating local verdicts from RunFull executions;\n   - what task 5 establishes (provenance) and what it doesn't (order, C46);\n   - refused ok steps and counterexamples;\n   - what OB-C28 leaves open;\n   - an axiom audit with a count that sums exactly.\n\n   **Order:** 1→6, one commit per compiling task.\n\n   **Constraints (verbatim):**\n   - « Formalisation exploratoire, jamais mergée. Pas de push sur `main`, pas de PR. »\n   - « Ne modifie ni `specs/`, ni `AGENTS.md`, ni `CLAUDE.md`, ni `formal/DESIGN.md`, ni aucun fichier de `formal/Ern/MemoryModel/`. »\n   - « N'ajoute aucune hypothèse pour obtenir un énoncé. Les hypothèses admises sont celles de `capacity_run` : `DDSound`, `StaticsOK`, état initial, `RunFull`. Toute hypothèse de plus est un écart à rapporter, avec ce qui la rend nécessaire. »\n   - « Définitions existantes. Aucune n'est modifiée ni affaiblie … `protected_runFull_refuted` compris. Tout est ajouté à côté. »\n   - Lean rules unchanged:\n     - no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide` or `noncomputable`;\n     - axioms `{propext, Quot.sound}`;\n     - `lake build` with no new warning;\n     - the `grep` of AGENTS.md is empty;\n     - docstrings in English citing WC5.2, Spec 1, corpus v14 or this brief;\n     - the verdict or expected fact comes from the corpus or the brief, never from the model;\n     - Conventional Commits **without Co-Authored-By** (memory rule; it overrides the system reminder).\n   - Out of scope:\n     - any modification of WC5.2;\n     - forbidding a derivative to outlive the grant;\n     - reject vs non-habilité classification of acquire (D-C1);\n     - physical events (OB-C20);\n     - realization conformance;\n     - a general proof of race freedom.\n   - Reports are in French; committed Lean is in English.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Lean 4 v4.35.0, no Mathlib. Build with `~/.elan/bin/lake build` in `formal/`; check a file with `lake env lean <file>`; `set_option autoImplicit false`.\n   - **No Mathlib tactics:**\n     - use `Decidable.byContradiction` for `by_contra`;\n     - use `congr (congrArg ..) ..` for `congrArg₂`.\n   - **Avoid deprecated lemmas and `omega` on conjunctions:**\n     - `if_pos`/`if_neg` are deprecated; use `List.getElem?_set_self` / `List.getElem?_set_ne` or `simp only [.., ↓reduceIte]`;\n     - `omega` on a conjunction goal may introduce `Classical.choice`; prove it explicitly.\n   - **Skel** (SyncPreserve.lean:134): `len`, `old`, `ancsSub`, `ancsKeep`, `new`.\n     - Lemmas: `Skel.active`, `Skel.afp`, `Skel.covering`, `Skel.covering_new`, `skel_append`, `skel_set`, `skel_map`, `skel_sameA`, `same_deact`, `Same`.\n     - StepFacts: `opStep_facts`, `spawnEff_facts`, `spawn_facts`, `term_facts`, `join_facts`, `src_none`.\n     - `PSkel`, `PSkel.isLeaf`, `pskel_refl`, `pskel_shapeP`.\n   - **CoveringDesc s g j** := `g ∈ ancs j ∧ Active j ∧ ∃ l ∈ afp j, l ∈ afp g`.\n     - `NoCoveringDesc`.\n     - SyncInv fields: `guarded`, `grant`, `control`, `ctlUnique`, `unique`, `grantSubtree`, `regBound`, `slotInit`, `ctlInit`.\n     - `GrantDiscipline` = `hlib.1.2` from `runFull_inv`; SyncInv = `hlib.1.1`; AdminSep = `hlib.2.1`.\n   - **KInvCA** (`hk`):\n     - `hk.parts` = FramesC ∧ WF3 ∧ I1;\n     - NoDangling = `hk.1.2.1.2.2`;\n     - WF3 fields: `footprints`, `holders`, `parent_lt`; `usable_of_part`; `exists_mem_footprint`; `footprint_ne` (CapPreserve).\n   - **cap5 / Attr5 / CapAt5 / Exer5:**\n     - `Exer5.attr5 hne`, `cap5_of`, `eff_present` (CapPreserve:135), `mem_descModes` (CapPreserve function form), `effective_of_A`, `SameSkel.effective`;\n     - `transfer_A_get`, `transfer_parentOf`, `transfer_len`, `transfer_footprint`;\n     - `Frames.enter_lt`, `Frames.enter_get`, `Arena.footprint_shapeP`, `mapI_id`, `length_mapI`;\n     - `stk_spawnCreate`, `view_top_mem`, `spawn_base` (TransferPreserveAux), `yield_get`, `yieldF` (TransferPreserveAux).\n   - **L1:** `cap5_drop_own (hdd) : Cap5DropOwn k L` (CapDrop.lean:1332). Cap5DropOwn (CapPreserve.lean:70):\n     ```\n     ∀ statics lbls st st' lbl c l, StaticsOK statics → EncapsulatedTrace5 k L (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], []) lbls st → Encap5 L (st.1, st.2.1) lbl → LStep k L lbl st st' → capRank (cap5 st'.1 st'.2.1 c l) < capRank (cap5 st.1 st.2.1 c l) → lbl.ctx = c\n     ```\n     - capRank: none 0, observe 1, modify 2.\n     - Conversions: `run5R_trace` (Events.lean:34) gives Run5R → EncapsulatedTrace5R (σ 0) lbls (σ lbls.length); `encapsulatedTrace5R_imp` (5R → 5C); `encapsulatedTrace5C_imp` (5C → 5); `chainExcl_guardedExcl`.\n     - `run7_run5R`, `runFull_run7`.\n   - **Steps5R** pattern for witnesses:\n     ```\n     .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <| ...\n     ```\n     then `runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide)`.\n     - Local Decidable instances `instDecidableEncap5R` in Witness.lean.\n     - `ClassifyWitness.mx3_steps`.\n   - Scratchpad: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6/scratchpad/`, containing Audit2.lean (axioms and per-module counts — copy it with the module list), dumpnames.lean (env OUT), names_finalpass.txt, names_encap.txt (2666 lines-1 baseline after slice 3) and ScanRights.lean.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/`, all imported in `formal/Ern.lean` after `MutexReal.FinalCorollaries`). Slice-3 files (Inventory, Witness, NonRegression, Capacity, CapacityWitness, Protected, ResetException) are unchanged in this pass.\n\n   - **AbandonedGrant.lean** (task 1, commit 857972e)\n     - Definitions: `covSet s g` (filter of CoveringDesc); `ag10` (release x), `ag11` (acquire → g′ = 7), `agReg [⟨3, some 7⟩]`, `ag12`; `agLbls := abLbls ++ [release 6, resetLock 0 0, acquire 0 0, write 7 [3]]`; `agσ`.\n     - Corpus step k is label index k+2.\n     - Theorems:\n       - `ag_steps`; `W_AG_run`;\n       - `W_AG_6_facts` (length equal, org 6: 5 → 3, afp/mode equal, covSet ab7 3 = [5,6], covSet ab8 3 = [6], live, ¬Active 5, root_M Modify on 1, 2);\n       - `W_AG_a` (∀ st', ¬AcquireOk; live; CtrlRight; ¬modeOK; ¬exclusive);\n       - `W_AG_b` (¬UnlockOk; ¬Active 5);\n       - `W_AG_c` (¬ResetLockOk; ¬NoCoveringDesc; CoveringDesc ab9 3 6; ExercisableAt 3);\n       - `W_AG_d` (read 3 [3] reject; effective = none).\n     - W-AG-J: aj11 (termEffC ag10 1), aj12, aj13, ajLbls, ajσ; `W_AGJ_run`.\n     - `W_AG_strict`: ExclPair 9 13 3, ¬HBS, ¬HandoffOrderedAtS, ¬HandoffOrderedS, RaceS.\n     - `W_AGJ_strict`: PO 9→11, SWS 11→12, PO 12→15, HBS 9 15, HandoffOrderedS, ¬RaceS.\n     - W-AG′: ap1..ap4, apLbls, apσ; `W_AGp_run` (RunFull + covSets [6], [6,7], org 7 = 6, [6,7], [7], length equal, org 7: 6 → 3, [7]); `W_AGp_neg`.\n\n   - **Closure.lean** (task 2, commit cca140c)\n     - `Skel.comp (h1) (h2) (hlen : s₂.A.length = s₁.A.length) (horg : ∀ i, s₂.flat.org i = s₁.flat.org i) : Skel s s₂`; `skel_refl`.\n     - `store_org`, `release_org`, `transfer_skel` (FullEncap version: Skel ∧ len ∧ org), `transfers_skel`, `yield_skel'`.\n     - `GrantOf st e j lbl` (acquire case: `OptP (st.2.1[i]?) (fun e' => e'.guarded = e.guarded ∧ j = st.1.A.length) False`).\n     - ClosureStep:\n       ```\n       ∀ e ∈ st.2.1, e.Live st.1 → e.Live st'.1 → ∀ j ∈ List.range st'.1.A.length, CoveringDesc st'.1 e.guarded j → CoveringDesc st.1 e.guarded j ∨ (st.1.A.length ≤ j ∧ ∃ o, st'.1.flat.org j = some o ∧ CoveringDesc st.1 e.guarded o) ∨ GrantOf st e j lbl\n       ```\n       It is decidable.\n     - `cover_of_skel`, `closure_of_skel`, `src_carry`, `store_skel'`, `release_skel'`.\n     - `closure_step (hk : KInvCA st.1) (hsep : AdminSep ..) (he : Encap ..) (hs : LStep ..)`.\n     - `closure_run (hdd hstat h0 h) (hi) : ClosureStep (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i+1))`.\n\n   - **Dying.lean** (task 3 partial, commit 2a92c48)\n     - `PSkel.comp`, `pskel_transferC`, `pskel_transfers`.\n     - `shape_step (hk hsep he hs) : Skel st.1 st'.1 ∧ PSkel st.1.P st'.1.P`.\n     - `protected_not_dying (hsk hP hnd ha hg hl) : ¬ Dying s s' l`.\n     - `protected_not_dying_run (hdd hstat h0 h hi hl hl' hfp)`.\n     - OtherCapFree:\n       ```\n       ∀ c' ∈ List.range st.1.C.length, c' ≠ lbl.ctx → ∀ l ∈ List.range st.1.P.length, Dying st.1 st'.1 l → cap5 st.1 st.2.1 c' l = none\n       ```\n       It is decidable.\n     - `exc_dying_facts` (decide on ce, fr, ex, tm; plus `cap5 tm4 exReg 0 4 = none`).\n\n   - **SpawnValCap.lean** (task 4, commit 88f099c)\n     - `corrF_ge` (`N ≤ x ∧ x < P.length`), `mvTo_ge`.\n     - `PhaseRel s c t` fields: lenP, lenA, parentLt, fpOld (iff), fpNew, holdLt, aOld, aNew, eff, top.\n     - `PhaseRel.active`, `ne_none_of_allows`, `exer5_back`, `fp_ge`, `effective_append_none`, `view_top_eq`.\n     - `phaseRel_create (hw₀ : WF3 (spawnCreate s c ls).flat) (hsh) (hl) (hne)`, `phaseRel_transfer (h) (hd : s.P.length ≤ dst) (hdl : dst < t.P.length)`.\n     - `phases_cap`, `spawnVal_pre`.\n     - `spawnVal_cap_pre (hdd hstat h0 h hi) (hl : lbls[i] = .spawnVal c ps ls vs) : ∀ v ∈ vs, ∀ l ∈ footprint (σ i).1.P v.1, (∃ x ∈ range, Attr5 .. c x .modify ∧ Allows (effective ..) .modify) ∧ Allows (cap5 ..) .modify`.\n\n   - **LastAcquire.lean** (task 5, commit 28312c0)\n     - `allows_mono`, `Mode.le_trans'`, `attr5_mono`, `cap5_attained`, `ProvCap st S c l m`.\n     - `CapFrom k st S` mirrors CapReq with ProvCap; spawnVal clause: `(∃ v ∈ vs, l ∈ footprint st.1.P v.1) → ProvCap .. .modify`.\n     - `prov_of`, `some_of_prov`, `capFrom_step (hs hS hlt hcap hnd hsv ht)`, `cov_of_attr (hi1 hinv he hl hng hfp hex) : CoveringDesc s e.guarded x`.\n     - `three_cases (hdd hstat h0 h hi he hl hl' hfp ht)`: (grant none → False) ∧ (some g active → CapFrom (x = g ∨ g ∈ ancs x)) ∧ (some g inactive → CapFrom CoveringDesc).\n     - `protected_cap_run (hdd hstat h0 h hi hl hl' hfp ht) : cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 lbls[i].ctx l ≠ none` (no `e ∈ reg` hypothesis).\n     - `empty_without_grant`.\n     - `reg_step`.\n     - `last_acquire`: ∀ n ≤ len, ∀ i e, (σ n).2.1[i]? = some e → Live → ∀ g, grant = some g → ∃ kk < n, an acquire of i at kk, no later acquire of i before n, g = |A(σ kk)|, and every covering descendant j = g or was created at k' ∈ (kk, n) with origin a covering descendant at k'.\n\n   - **ComplementSweep.lean**\n     - Local Decidable instance for ProvCap.\n     - `ThreeOK L st lbl st'` (at Observe), `SweepOK` (ClosureStep ∧ ThreeOK ∧ OtherCapFree at every step).\n     - `sweep` covers 33 traces: the 24 + lvσ, gtσ, rxbσ, frσ, exσ, tmσ, agσ, ajσ, apσ.\n     - `W_AG_7_third`.\n\n   - **Replay.lean** (task 6, commit 7384238)\n     - Opens `Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)`.\n     - `RunFull.take`.\n     - `W_GR_full`: W_GR_1_ok ∧ ¬PremG at (x4, regX) ∧ suite RunFull wrσ wrLbls (mx4 + c0 acquire + c0 write 5 [3]).\n     - `W_GC_full`: gc_read.2 ∧ ¬PremG at (gc6, greg) ∧ suite cgσ cgLbls (glbls.take 7 + acquire 0 0, write 3 [4], read 3 [4]); states cg7..cg9, cgReg [⟨4, some 6⟩].\n     - `W_GS_full`: W_GS_1_ok ∧ ¬PremG at (gs5, sreg) ∧ suite sgσ sgLbls (setupLbls + acquire 1 0 + read 6 [3] from gs5); sg6, sg7.\n     - `S2_full` (prefix of rl0, take 8), `S10_full` (prefix of s10, take 7), `S3_full` (s3fσ, 13 labels), `S4_full` (q0..q6, K0), `S9_full` (n0..n6, K9), `mutex_full`, `distinct_full`, `wc4_full` (traceA, traceB, traceMutex = take 3).\n     - Docstrings currently cite \"WC4 C13, C16, C17\", \"WC4 S18\" (to fix to WC5.2), and claim \"step 1 changes no state\" (to back with rfl or drop).\n\n   - **formal/reports/spec2-m4-encap.md**: slice-3 report, already committed. The « Complément » section is not yet written.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Classical.choice from `omega` on a conjunction goal: replaced with an explicit Nat term (found by bisecting in scratch).\n   - `by_contra` and `congrArg₂` are unknown (no Mathlib): used `Decidable.byContradiction` and `congr (congrArg (· ++ ·) _) _`.\n   - Deprecated `if_pos`/`if_neg`: replaced with `getElem?_set_self`/`getElem?_set_ne` or `simp only [.., ↓reduceIte]`.\n   - Dependent elimination failures: used `Outcome3.ok.inj ho`, `Holder.frame.inj`, `rw [he₂]`.\n   - The filterMap rewrite hit the wrong occurrence: used a congr-based split.\n   - Restated match lambdas don't match syntactically: inlined the proof.\n   - `mem_descModes` ambiguity: used the CapPreserve function form with `(t := s.flat)`.\n   - Unknown K0: opened `Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)`.\n   - Metavariable σ default in `hA.run _`: gave the explicit default and type ascription.\n   - Unused variables (`he` in protected_cap_run, `hw` in phaseRel_create): removed.\n   - `-` in match patterns: replaced with `_`.\n   - Binder types needed in PhaseRel fields: added explicit `(a : Nat) (y : Authority)`.\n   - The PSkel `rfl` for ≤ failed: used `Nat.le_refl`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Task 1:** all expected facts obtained.\n     - W-AG and W-AG-J: RunFull.\n     - Refusal a: no ok outcome. C14.2 fails; C15.4/C15.5 fail; C14.1/C14.3 hold.\n     - Refusal b: no ok outcome (the corpus says reject); C17.2, g inactive.\n     - Refusal c: no ok outcome; C18.2, x covers T.\n     - Refusal d: reject; O9.2.\n     - Strict graph: as the corpus expects.\n     - W-AG′: as the corpus expects.\n   - **Task 2:** the closure is proved for all kinds via Skel. (2′) is not needed: composites create only in their first phase.\n   - **Task 3:**\n     - (i) proved.\n     - (ii) checked on the witnesses and in the sweep; the general proof is pending (see Current Work).\n     - \"Which kinds kill leaves\" is not proved (relecture + sweep pending).\n   - **Task 4:** proved; no counterexample.\n   - **Task 5:**\n     - Empty set: GrantDiscipline is established on reached states by `runFull_inv` (trace_inv; hypotheses DDSound, StaticsOK, init, RunFull).\n     - `last_acquire` is proved.\n     - The three cases are proved; they use tasks 3(i) and 4, `capacity_run`, I1, C21.1, GrantSubtree and GrantDiscipline.\n     - The corpus fact is proved for 28 kinds.\n     - The sweep passes, and W-AG step 7 falls in the third case.\n   - **Task 6:** all replays are RunFull; no trace is refused; S9 is admitted.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1 (start of this session): brief « tranche 3 : encapsulation complète (C22 point 6) » with corpus v13 and WC5.2. Completed earlier.\n   - Message 2 (current): the brief « Brief Claude Code — ERN Spec 2, jalon 4, tranche 3 : encapsulation complète, complément ».\n     - Attachments: corpus-spec2-m3.md v14 and ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.2.md.\n     - Decisions 1–4, Objet, tasks 1–6, Hors de portée, Règles Lean, Rapport and Ordre: see section 1, including the verbatim constraints.\n     - It ends with « Ordre 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5 → 6. Commit à chaque tâche compilant. »\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Task 3(ii), general proof via `cap5_drop_own`:**\n     - Show that after the step no context has cap5 on a dying leaf: an attaining authority would be active and cover an unusable leaf, contradicting NoDangling after, with isLeaf via PSkel.\n     - Conclude that a strict drop for c′ ≠ ctx contradicts L1.\n     - Build the bridge RunFull → EncapsulatedTrace5 prefix: `run5R_trace` on the prefix, then `encapsulatedTrace5R_imp`, then `encapsulatedTrace5C_imp`. Get Encap5 from Encap5R (`⟨he.1.1, chainExcl_guardedExcl he.1.2.1, he.1.2.2⟩`).\n     - If the signature doesn't fit, report « inachevé » with the goal.\n   - **Advisor's cheap gaps:**\n     - extend the sweep with the Replay traces;\n     - add a decidable \"only endUse/free/exit/terminate kill leaves\" check to the sweep;\n     - grep the trace list untruncated (Run5, Run5C, Run5R, Run6, LRun, EncapsulatedTrace*) and classify every trace;\n     - add W-GS local verdicts at gs6/gs7;\n     - back \"step 1 changes no state\" with `gr1 = x4` / `gc7 = gc6` by rfl, or drop it;\n     - read Spec 1 §40 and §56 or remove those citations;\n     - replace the WC4 citations in Replay.lean with WC5.2.\n   - **Report « Complément »** in spec2-m4-encap.md, in French, with all required items. It must also state:\n     - refusals b and c show « no ok outcome »;\n     - the sweep's three cases are at Observe;\n     - last_acquire identifies the entry by registry index, while closure case 3 identifies it by guarded identity;\n     - provenance vs order (C46: W-AG has a race; W-AG-J is ordered via join);\n     - what OB-C28 leaves open.\n   - **Audit:**\n     - axioms of all new theorems;\n     - name diff against names_encap.txt;\n     - per-file warning counts with `lake env lean`;\n     - the AGENTS.md grep;\n     - line lengths ≤ 100, checked in Python.\n   - Commit each, update memory, then call wrap_up and write the French closing message.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   I was starting the general proof of task 3(ii), after the advisor's advice: « First check whether it is a short corollary of `cap5_drop_own` (L1, WC5.2 C45) ». I had just read:\n   - `Cap5DropOwn` (CapPreserve.lean:70);\n   - `cap5_drop_own (hdd) : Cap5DropOwn k L` (CapDrop.lean:1332), dispatching all kinds;\n   - `run5R_trace` (Events.lean:34): `Run5R k L σ lbls → EncapsulatedTrace5R k L (σ 0) lbls (σ lbls.length)`;\n   - `Run5R` (Events.lean:24): `∀ i (h : i < lbls.length), Encap5R k L (σ i) lbls[i] ∧ LStep k L lbls[i] (σ i) (σ (i + 1))`.\n\n   The signature fits. The intended theorem (to add in Dying.lean or a new module):\n   ```\n   theorem other_cap_free_run (hdd hstat h0 h) (hi : i < lbls.length) : OtherCapFree (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i+1))\n   ```\n   Proof plan:\n   - **After the step:** for a dying l, `cap5 (σ (i+1)).1 (σ (i+1)).2.1 c' l = none`. Otherwise:\n     1. `cap5_attained` gives x with Allows (effective x l), so x is active and covers l (eff_present);\n     2. NoDangling at i+1 (`(runFull_inv .. hi).1.1.2.1.2.2`), with q = l, isLeaf at i+1 via `shape_step`'s PSkel and l unusable after, gives a contradiction.\n   - **Before the step:** if cap5 at i is not none, the capRank drops strictly (> 0 down to 0). `cap5_drop_own hdd statics (lbls.take i) (σ i) (σ (i+1)) lbls[i] c' l hstat htr he5 hs hd` then gives `lbls[i].ctx = c'`, contradicting c′ ≠ ctx.\n   - **Inputs:**\n     - `htr`: EncapsulatedTrace5 from init to (σ i), from `run5R_trace` applied to Run5R of `lbls.take i` (from `run7_run5R (runFull_run7 h)` restricted) with `h0`, then `encapsulatedTrace5C_imp (encapsulatedTrace5R_imp ..)`. Alternatively via `RunFull.take` and the length of `take`.\n     - `he5`: Encap5 from `(h i hi).1.1.1` (Encap5R) via `⟨he.1.1, chainExcl_guardedExcl he.1.2.1, he.1.2.2⟩`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Implement and compile `other_cap_free_run` as a corollary of `cap5_drop_own`, per the advisor's latest instruction: « First check whether it is a short corollary of `cap5_drop_own` (L1, WC5.2 C45). … This would cover every kind, including `free`, with no per-kind work. You still need a bridge from `RunFull` to the trace form L1 expects (`run5R_trace`, `encapsulatedTrace5R_imp`, `encapsulatedTrace5C_imp`). If the signature doesn't fit, record \"inachevé\" with the goal and move on. »\n\n   Then commit it (task 3 completion) and continue with:\n   1. the cheap gaps (sweep extension with the Replay traces and the dying-kinds check, exhaustive trace classification, W-GS local verdicts at gs6/gs7, the rfl backing or dropped claims, citation fixes);\n   2. the « Complément » report section;\n   3. the audit;\n   4. the memory update, wrap_up and the French closing message.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"65e67ac7-5516-414b-b293-99b9c76a32e6","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:37:03.574Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":27,"turnIndex":34},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["42de7458-b66a-403f-87e8-636698feb511"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"65e67ac7-5516-414b-b293-99b9c76a32e6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/DyingCap.lean","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/DyingCap.lean","content":"import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.LastAcquire\n\n/-!\n# No other context has a capacity on a dying leaf\n\nBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, complement, task 3, second fact (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14\n§2 terdecies, \"Feuilles qui meurent\"): in the state before a step of a context `c`, no context\nother than `c` has a `cap5` (WC5.2 C43) on a leaf that dies in the step.\n\nAfter the step, no context has a `cap5` on such a leaf: an attaining authority would be active\nand cover it, against `NoDangling` (Spec 1 §54) after the step. A context other than `c` with a\n`cap5` before the step would then have lost it in a step of `c`, which L1 forbids\n(`cap5_drop_own`, WC5.2 C45, proved for the 28 kinds on `EncapsulatedTrace5`, which every prefix\nof a `RunFull` is).\n-/\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen SyncPreserveAux SyncInitAux TransferPreserveAux\n\n/-- After a step, no context has a `cap5` on a leaf that died in it, when `NoDangling` holds after\nthe step (Spec 1 §54) and the step keeps leaves leaves (`PSkel`). -/\ntheorem cap5_none_after {s s' : SC} {reg : SyncReg} {c l : Nat} (hP : PSkel s.P s'.P)\n    (hnd : NoDangling s'.flat) (hd : Dying s s' l) : cap5 s' reg c l = none := by\n  cases hc : cap5 s' reg c l with\n  | none => rfl\n  | some m =>\n    exfalso\n    have hal : Allows (cap5 s' reg c l) .observe := by rw [hc]; exact Or.inl rfl\n    obtain ⟨x, -, -, hex⟩ := cap5_attained hal\n    obtain ⟨z, hz, za, hlz, -⟩ := eff_present (ne_none_of_allows hex)\n    obtain ⟨hleaf, hu, hu'⟩ := hd\n    have hlt := hu.lt\n    have hleaf' : isLeaf s'.P l := (hP.isLeaf hlt).2 hleaf\n    have hmem : l ∈ footprint s'.flat.P l :=\n      (Arena.mem_footprint_leaf hleaf' (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt hP.1)).2 rfl\n    exact hnd x z hz za l hu' l hmem hlz\n\n/-- A prefix of a `RunFull` is a `Run5R`. -/\ntheorem run5R_take {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\n    {lbls : List Label} (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) (n : Nat) : Run5R k L σ (lbls.take n) :=\n  fun i hi => by\n    have hi' : i < lbls.length := by simp at hi; omega\n    have e : (lbls.take n)[i] = lbls[i] := List.getElem_take\n    rw [e]\n    exact ⟨(h i hi').1.1.1, (h i hi').2⟩\n\n/-- Brief of the complement, task 3, second fact: on a `RunFull` from the initial state, under\n`DDSound`, in the state before a step, no context other than the acting one has a `cap5` on a\nleaf that dies in the step. Invariants and results used: `NoDangling` after the step (Spec 1\n§54), `PSkel` of the step, and L1 (`cap5_drop_own`, WC5.2 C45). -/\ntheorem other_cap_dying_run {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {statics : Statics}\n    {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbls : List Label} (hdd : DDSound k)\n    (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], []))\n    (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {i : Nat} (hi : i < lbls.length) {c' l : Nat}\n    (hc' : c' ≠ lbls[i].ctx) (hd : Dying (σ i).1 (σ (i + 1)).1 l) :\n    cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 c' l = none := by\n  obtain ⟨hk, hlib⟩ := runFull_inv hdd hstat h0 h (Nat.le_of_lt hi)\n  obtain ⟨hk', -⟩ := runFull_inv hdd hstat h0 h hi\n  obtain ⟨-, hP⟩ := shape_step hk hlib.2.1 (h i hi).1.1.1.1.1 (h i hi).2\n  have hafter := cap5_none_after (reg := (σ (i + 1)).2.1) (c := c') hP hk'.1.2.1.2.2 hd\n  cases hb : cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 c' l with\n  | none => rfl\n  | some m =>\n    exfalso\n    have htr5R := run5R_trace (run5R_take h i)\n    have hlen : (lbls.take i).length = i := by simp; omega\n    rw [hlen, h0] at htr5R\n    have htr := encapsulatedTrace5C_imp (encapsulatedTrace5R_imp htr5R)\n    have he5C := (h i hi).1.1.1.1\n    have he5 : Encap5 L ((σ i).1, (σ i).2.1) lbls[i] :=\n      ⟨he5C.1, chainExcl_guardedExcl he5C.2.1, he5C.2.2⟩\n    have hdrop : capRank (cap5 (σ (i + 1)).1 (σ (i + 1)).2.1 c' l) <\n        capRank (cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 c' l) := by\n      rw [hafter, hb]; cases m <;> decide\n    exact hc' (cap5_drop_own hdd statics (lbls.take i) (σ i) (σ (i + 1)) lbls[i] c' l hstat htr\n      he5 (h i hi).2 hdrop).symm\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n","numLines":83,"startLine":1,"totalLines":83}},"displayPath":"Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/DyingCap.lean","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fe013c73-0611-4b46-ba6e-152ca07408a3","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:37:03.782Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/DyingCap.lean\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.LastAcquire\n2\t\n3\t/-!\n4\t# No other context has a capacity on a dying leaf\n5\t\n6\tBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, complement, task 3, second fact (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14\n7\t§2 terdecies, \"Feuilles qui meurent\"): in the state before a step of a context `c`, no context\n8\tother than `c` has a `cap5` (WC5.2 C43) on a leaf that dies in the step.\n9\t\n10\tAfter the step, no context has a `cap5` on such a leaf: an attaining authority would be active\n11\tand cover it, against `NoDangling` (Spec 1 §54) after the step. A context other than `c` with a\n12\t`cap5` before the step would then have lost it in a step of `c`, which L1 forbids\n13\t(`cap5_drop_own`, WC5.2 C45, proved for the 28 kinds on `EncapsulatedTrace5`, which every prefix\n14\tof a `RunFull` is).\n15\t-/\n16\t\n17\tset_option autoImplicit false\n18\t\n19\tnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n20\t\n21\topen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\n22\topen SyncPreserveAux SyncInitAux TransferPreserveAux\n23\t\n24\t/-- After a step, no context has a `cap5` on a leaf that died in it, when `NoDangling` holds after\n25\tthe step (Spec 1 §54) and the step keeps leaves leaves (`PSkel`). -/\n26\ttheorem cap5_none_after {s s' : SC} {reg : SyncReg} {c l : Nat} (hP : PSkel s.P s'.P)\n27\t    (hnd : NoDangling s'.flat) (hd : Dying s s' l) : cap5 s' reg c l = none := by\n28\t  cases hc : cap5 s' reg c l with\n29\t  | none => rfl\n30\t  | some m =>\n31\t    exfalso\n32\t    have hal : Allows (cap5 s' reg c l) .observe := by rw [hc]; exact Or.inl rfl\n33\t    obtain ⟨x, -, -, hex⟩ := cap5_attained hal\n34\t    obtain ⟨z, hz, za, hlz, -⟩ := eff_present (ne_none_of_allows hex)\n35\t    obtain ⟨hleaf, hu, hu'⟩ := hd\n36\t    have hlt := hu.lt\n37\t    have hleaf' : isLeaf s'.P l := (hP.isLeaf hlt).2 hleaf\n38\t    have hmem : l ∈ footprint s'.flat.P l :=\n39\t      (Arena.mem_footprint_leaf hleaf' (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt hP.1)).2 rfl\n40\t    exact hnd x z hz za l hu' l hmem hlz\n41\t\n42\t/-- A prefix of a `RunFull` is a `Run5R`. -/\n43\ttheorem run5R_take {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\n44\t    {lbls : List Label} (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) (n : Nat) : Run5R k L σ (lbls.take n) :=\n45\t  fun i hi => by\n46\t    have hi' : i < lbls.length := by simp at hi; omega\n47\t    have e : (lbls.take n)[i] = lbls[i] := List.getElem_take\n48\t    rw [e]\n49\t    exact ⟨(h i hi').1.1.1, (h i hi').2⟩\n50\t\n51\t/-- Brief of the complement, task 3, second fact: on a `RunFull` from the initial state, under\n52\t`DDSound`, in the state before a step, no context other than the acting one has a `cap5` on a\n53\tleaf that dies in the step. Invariants and results used: `NoDangling` after the step (Spec 1\n54\t§54), `PSkel` of the step, and L1 (`cap5_drop_own`, WC5.2 C45). -/\n55\ttheorem other_cap_dying_run {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {statics : Statics}\n56\t    {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbls : List Label} (hdd : DDSound k)\n57\t    (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], []))\n58\t    (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {i : Nat} (hi : i < lbls.length) {c' l : Nat}\n59\t    (hc' : c' ≠ lbls[i].ctx) (hd : Dying (σ i).1 (σ (i + 1)).1 l) :\n60\t    cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 c' l = none := by\n61\t  obtain ⟨hk, hlib⟩ := runFull_inv hdd hstat h0 h (Nat.le_of_lt hi)\n62\t  obtain ⟨hk', -⟩ := runFull_inv hdd hstat h0 h hi\n63\t  obtain ⟨-, hP⟩ := shape_step hk hlib.2.1 (h i hi).1.1.1.1.1 (h i hi).2\n64\t  have hafter := cap5_none_after (reg := (σ (i + 1)).2.1) (c := c') hP hk'.1.2.1.2.2 hd\n65\t  cases hb : cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 c' l with\n66\t  | none => rfl\n67\t  | some m =>\n68\t    exfalso\n69\t    have htr5R := run5R_trace (run5R_take h i)\n70\t    have hlen : (lbls.take i).length = i := by simp; omega\n71\t    rw [hlen, h0] at htr5R\n72\t    have htr := encapsulatedTrace5C_imp (encapsulatedTrace5R_imp htr5R)\n73\t    have he5C := (h i hi).1.1.1.1\n74\t    have he5 : Encap5 L ((σ i).1, (σ i).2.1) lbls[i] :=\n75\t      ⟨he5C.1, chainExcl_guardedExcl he5C.2.1, he5C.2.2⟩\n76\t    have hdrop : capRank (cap5 (σ (i + 1)).1 (σ (i + 1)).2.1 c' l) <\n77\t        capRank (cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 c' l) := by\n78\t      rw [hafter, hb]; cases m <;> decide\n79\t    exact hc' (cap5_drop_own hdd statics (lbls.take i) (σ i) (σ (i + 1)) lbls[i] c' l hstat htr\n80\t      he5 (h i hi).2 hdrop).symm\n81\t\n82\tend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap\n83\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"fe013c73-0611-4b46-ba6e-152ca07408a3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Replay.lean","displayPath":"Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Replay.lean"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"93e64d37-4f96-4203-9078-480a0bebfa22","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:37:03.782Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Replay.lean was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"93e64d37-4f96-4203-9078-480a0bebfa22","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ComplementSweep.lean","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ComplementSweep.lean","content":"import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.LastAcquire\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.AbandonedGrant\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.NonRegression\n\n/-!\n# Sweep of the complement on the `RunFull` traces\n\nBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, complement, tasks 2, 3 and 5: the closure (`ClosureStep`), the\nthree cases of the protected data (`ThreeOK`, at mode `Observe`) and the absence of another\ncontext's capacity on a dying leaf (`OtherCapFree`) are checked by `decide` at every step of the\n`RunFull` traces of the repository, W-AG, W-AG-J and W-AG′ included. Step 7 of W-AG falls in the\nthird case (`W_AG_7_third`).\n-/\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Sweep\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.HandoffEvents Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.MutexEdge\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.ResetLockRight Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.ClassifyWitness\nopen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.NonRegression\nopen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.Witness (s11σ s11Lbls)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChainC (lcLbls)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.AbandonedGrant Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Protected\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\n\n/-- Decidability of `ProvCap` for a decidable provenance. -/\ninstance (st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (S : Nat → Prop) [DecidablePred S] (c l : Nat)\n    (m : Mode) : Decidable (ProvCap st S c l m) := by\n  unfold ProvCap; infer_instance\n\n/-- The three cases of the brief of the complement, task 5, for one step, at mode `Observe`: for\nevery entry live before and after the step and every leaf of `footprint(guarded)` in the final\nfootprint, no grant is impossible; an active grant `g` gives a capacity from `g` or a descendant\nof `g`; an inactive grant gives a capacity from the covering descendants. -/\ndef ThreeOK (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbl : Label)\n    (st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) : Prop :=\n  ∀ e ∈ st.2.1, e.Live st.1 → e.Live st'.1 → ∀ l ∈ st.1.flat.afp e.guarded,\n    TouchesF L st lbl l → OptP e.grant (fun g =>\n      (st.1.flat.Active g → ProvCap st (fun x => x = g ∨ g ∈ st.1.flat.ancs x) lbl.ctx l .observe) ∧\n      (¬ st.1.flat.Active g → ProvCap st (CoveringDesc st.1 e.guarded) lbl.ctx l .observe)) False\n\n/-- Decidability of `ThreeOK`. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbl : Label)\n    (st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) : Decidable (ThreeOK L st lbl st') := by\n  unfold ThreeOK; infer_instance\n\n/-- The three checks at every step of a run. -/\ndef SweepOK (L : MutexLayout) (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label) : Prop :=\n  ∀ i (h : i < lbls.length), ClosureStep (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i + 1)) ∧\n    ThreeOK L (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i + 1)) ∧ OtherCapFree (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i + 1))\n\n/-- Decidability of `SweepOK`. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label) :\n    Decidable (SweepOK L σ lbls) := by\n  unfold SweepOK; infer_instance\n\n/-- Brief of the complement, tasks 2, 3 and 5, on the `RunFull` traces of the repository: the 24\nfinal amended executions, the trace of legitimate uses, the twins of W-GI and W-RX, the four\nwitnesses of the exceptions of slice 3 (`ce` among the 24), W-AG, W-AG-J and W-AG′. -/\ntheorem sweep :\n    SweepOK L0 hoσ hoLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 ho2σ ho2Lbls ∧ SweepOK L0 ho3σ ho3Lbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 hojσ hojLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 ho3jσ ho3jLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 lcσ lcLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 rl0σ rl0Lbls ∧ SweepOK L0 rlσ rlLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 rljσ rljLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 trσ trLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 trjσ trjLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 s11σ s11Lbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 cvσ cvLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 ceσ ceLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 crσ crLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 gsTwinσ gsTwinLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 s3σ s3Lbls ∧ SweepOK L0 s10σ s10Lbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 AmendWitness.tsσ AmendWitness.tsLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 AmendWitness.tiσ AmendWitness.tiLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 AmendWitness.taσ AmendWitness.taLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 AmendWitness.tdtσ AmendWitness.tdtLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 FinalWitness.amσ FinalWitness.amLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 AmendWitness.tdσ AmendWitness.tdLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 FullEncap.NonRegression.lvσ FullEncap.NonRegression.lvLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 Witness.gtσ Witness.gtLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 Witness.rxbσ Witness.rxbLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 CapacityWitness.frσ CapacityWitness.frLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 CapacityWitness.exσ CapacityWitness.exLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 CapacityWitness.tmσ CapacityWitness.tmLbls ∧\n    SweepOK L0 agσ agLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 ajσ ajLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 apσ apLbls := by\n  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_,\n    ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> decide\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies W-AG, step 7 (`c1 : write3(T)` via `x`, index 9): entry\n`e` is live before and after, `T` is a protected leaf in the footprint, the recorded grant `g`\n(authority 5) is inactive: the step falls in the third case, the capacity of `c1` coming from `x`\n(authority 6), a covering descendant of `e`, at `Modify`. -/\ntheorem W_AG_7_third : (⟨3, some 5⟩ : SyncEntry).Live ab9 ∧ (⟨3, some 5⟩ : SyncEntry).Live ab8 ∧\n    TouchesF L0 (agσ 9) (.kernel 1 (.write 6 [3])) 3 ∧ ¬ ab8.flat.Active 5 ∧\n    CoveringDesc ab8 3 6 ∧ Attr5 ab8 abReg 1 6 .modify ∧ effective ab8.flat 6 3 = some .modify ∧\n    ProvCap (agσ 9) (CoveringDesc ab8 3) 1 3 .modify := by\n  decide\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Sweep\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}},"displayPath":"Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ComplementSweep.lean","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7adcd64d-5a9c-4447-9aa9-a3e1520d12a9","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:37:03.782Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/ComplementSweep.lean\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.LastAcquire\n2\timport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.AbandonedGrant\n3\timport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.NonRegression\n4\t\n5\t/-!\n6\t# Sweep of the complement on the `RunFull` traces\n7\t\n8\tBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, complement, tasks 2, 3 and 5: the closure (`ClosureStep`), the\n9\tthree cases of the protected data (`ThreeOK`, at mode `Observe`) and the absence of another\n10\tcontext's capacity on a dying leaf (`OtherCapFree`) are checked by `decide` at every step of the\n11\t`RunFull` traces of the repository, W-AG, W-AG-J and W-AG′ included. Step 7 of W-AG falls in the\n12\tthird case (`W_AG_7_third`).\n13\t-/\n14\t\n15\tset_option autoImplicit false\n16\t\n17\tnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Sweep\n18\t\n19\topen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\n20\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.HandoffEvents Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.MutexEdge\n21\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.ResetLockRight Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.ClassifyWitness\n22\topen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.NonRegression\n23\topen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.Witness (s11σ s11Lbls)\n24\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChainC (lcLbls)\n25\topen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.AbandonedGrant Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Protected\n26\topen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\n27\t\n28\t/-- Decidability of `ProvCap` for a decidable provenance. -/\n29\tinstance (st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (S : Nat → Prop) [DecidablePred S] (c l : Nat)\n30\t    (m : Mode) : Decidable (ProvCap st S c l m) := by\n31\t  unfold ProvCap; infer_instance\n32\t\n33\t/-- The three cases of the brief of the complement, task 5, for one step, at mode `Observe`: for\n34\tevery entry live before and after the step and every leaf of `footprint(guarded)` in the final\n35\tfootprint, no grant is impossible; an active grant `g` gives a capacity from `g` or a descendant\n36\tof `g`; an inactive grant gives a capacity from the covering descendants. -/\n37\tdef ThreeOK (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbl : Label)\n38\t    (st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) : Prop :=\n39\t  ∀ e ∈ st.2.1, e.Live st.1 → e.Live st'.1 → ∀ l ∈ st.1.flat.afp e.guarded,\n40\t    TouchesF L st lbl l → OptP e.grant (fun g =>\n41\t      (st.1.flat.Active g → ProvCap st (fun x => x = g ∨ g ∈ st.1.flat.ancs x) lbl.ctx l .observe) ∧\n42\t      (¬ st.1.flat.Active g → ProvCap st (CoveringDesc st.1 e.guarded) lbl.ctx l .observe)) False\n43\t\n44\t/-- Decidability of `ThreeOK`. -/\n45\tinstance (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbl : Label)\n46\t    (st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) : Decidable (ThreeOK L st lbl st') := by\n47\t  unfold ThreeOK; infer_instance\n48\t\n49\t/-- The three checks at every step of a run. -/\n50\tdef SweepOK (L : MutexLayout) (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label) : Prop :=\n51\t  ∀ i (h : i < lbls.length), ClosureStep (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i + 1)) ∧\n52\t    ThreeOK L (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i + 1)) ∧ OtherCapFree (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i + 1))\n53\t\n54\t/-- Decidability of `SweepOK`. -/\n55\tinstance (L : MutexLayout) (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label) :\n56\t    Decidable (SweepOK L σ lbls) := by\n57\t  unfold SweepOK; infer_instance\n58\t\n59\t/-- Brief of the complement, tasks 2, 3 and 5, on the `RunFull` traces of the repository: the 24\n60\tfinal amended executions, the trace of legitimate uses, the twins of W-GI and W-RX, the four\n61\twitnesses of the exceptions of slice 3 (`ce` among the 24), W-AG, W-AG-J and W-AG′. -/\n62\ttheorem sweep :\n63\t    SweepOK L0 hoσ hoLbls ∧ SweepOK L0 ho2σ ho2Lbls ∧ SweepOK L0 h