":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"c480a741-89bf-43c7-ac6e-83b6b93c01fc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Syk3VNUZ9SaFud2LVMSy1r","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.NonRegression\n2\timport Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedRead\n3\timport Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain\n4\timport Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.S10\n5\timport Ern.Concurrency.EncapTraces\n6\timport Ern.Concurrency.Traces\n7\t\n8\t/-!\n9\t# Traces replayed under the complete encapsulation\n10\t\n11\tBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, complement, task 6 (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies,\n12\t\"Traces rejouées\").\n13\t\n14\t* W-GR, W-GC, W-GS: the excluded step is a local verdict, `ok` at the kernel and outside the\n15\t  guard-free forms, on its starting state, reached from the initial state by an admitted prefix;\n16\t  the positive suite (the setup, then the remaining steps, without the excluded one) is a\n17\t  `RunFull` from the initial state.\n18\t* The traces that existed only under an older encapsulation (S2, S3 in full, S4, S9, S10, the\n19\t  traces of WC4 in `Traces` and `EncapTraces`) are `RunFull` traces.\n20\t-/\n21\t\n22\tset_option autoImplicit false\n23\t\n24\tnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Replay\n25\t\n26\topen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\n27\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus\n28\topen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Witness (instDecidableEncap5R)\n29\topen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\n30\topen Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)\n31\t\n32\t/-- A prefix of a `RunFull` is a `RunFull`. -/\n33\ttheorem RunFull.take {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\n34\t    {lbls : List Label} (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) (n : Nat) : RunFull k L σ (lbls.take n) :=\n35\t  fun i hi => by\n36\t    have hi' : i < lbls.length := by simp at hi; omega\n37\t    have e : (lbls.take n)[i] = lbls[i] := List.getElem_take\n38\t    rw [e]; exact h i hi'\n39\t\n40\t/-! ## W-GR -/\n41\t\n42\t/-- W-GR, suite without step 1: `c0 : acquire(e)` from `MX₄`, grant `g`, authority 5. -/\n43\tdef wr5 : SC := deriveSyncEff x4 0 3\n44\t/-- W-GR, suite: `c0 : write3(T)` via `g` (O10). -/\n45\tdef wr6 : SC := wr5.set (write3Eff (wr5.view 0) [3])\n46\t/-- The registry with `g` recorded. -/\n47\tdef wrReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 5⟩]\n48\t\n49\t/-- The labels of `MX₄`. -/\n50\tdef mx4Lbls : List Label :=\n51\t  [.kernel 0 (.derive 1 [3] .modify), .kernel 0 (.store 3 1), .newMutex 0 3,\n52\t   .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] []]\n53\t\n54\t/-- The labels of the positive suite of W-GR. -/\n55\tdef wrLbls : List Label := mx4Lbls ++ [.acquire 0 0, .kernel 0 (.write 5 [3])]\n56\t\n57\t/-- The named states of the positive suite of W-GR. -/\n58\tdef wrσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n59\t  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []),\n60\t    (wr5, wrReg, []), (wr6, wrReg, [])].getD i (wr6, wrReg, [])\n61\t\n62\t/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies, W-GR under the complete encapsulation. Local verdict:\n63\tstep 1, `c1 : read3(T)` with `access = guarded` from `MX₄`, is `ok` at the kernel (O9) and outside\n64\tthe guard-free forms (its access authority is the live `guarded`, WC5.2 C22 item 6), `MX₄` being\n65\treached by the admitted prefix of the suite. Suite: `MX₄`, then steps 2 and 3, is a `RunFull`\n66\tfrom the initial state; step 1 changes no state (O9), so the suite does not depend on it. -/\n67\ttheorem W_GR_full : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 x4 (.ok GuardedRead.gr1) ∧\n68\t    ¬ PremG KM L0 (x4, regX, []) (.kernel 1 (.read 3 [3])) ∧\n69\t    wrσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧ RunFull KM L0 wrσ wrLbls := by\n70\t  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []), (wr5, wrReg, []),\n71\t      (wr6, wrReg, [])]\n72\t      [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [], .acquire 0 0,\n73\t        .kernel 0 (.write 5 [3])] :=\n74\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n75\t    .cons (by decide) (.spawn ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n76\t    .cons (by decide) (.acquire ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n77\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) .nil\n78\t  exact ⟨GuardedRead.W_GR_1_ok, by decide, rfl,\n79\t    runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R ((ClassifyWitness.mx3_steps h).run _) (by decide))\n80\t      (by decide)⟩\n81\t\n82\t/-! ## W-GC -/\n83\t\n84\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain in\n85\t/-- W-GC, suite without step 1: `c0 : acquire(e)`, grant `g`, authority 6. -/\n86\tdef cg7 : SC := deriveSyncEff GuardedChain.gc6 0 4\n87\t/-- W-GC, suite: `c0 : write3(Y)` via `z` (O10). -/\n88\tdef cg8 : SC := cg7.set (write3Eff (cg7.view 0) [4])\n89\t/-- W-GC, suite: `c0 : read3(Y)` via `z` (O9). -/\n90\tdef cg9 : SC := cg8.set (cg8.view 0)\n91\t/-- The registry with `g` recorded. -/\n92\tdef cgReg : SyncReg := [⟨4, some 6⟩]\n93\t\n94\t/-- The labels of the positive suite of W-GC: the setup, then steps 2 to 4. -/\n95\tdef cgLbls : List Label :=\n96\t  GuardedChain.glbls.take 7 ++ [.acquire 0 0, .kernel 0 (.write 3 [4]), .kernel 0 (.read 3 [4])]\n97\t\n98\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain in\n99\t/-- The named states of the positive suite of W-GC. -/\n100\tdef cgσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n101\t  [(gc0, [], []), (gc1, [], []), (gc2, [], []), (gc3, [], []), (gc4, [], []), (gc4, greg, []),\n102\t    (gc5, greg, []), (gc6, greg, []), (cg7, cgReg, []), (cg8, cgReg, []), (cg9, cgReg, [])].getD i\n103\t    (cg9, cgReg, [])\n104\t\n105\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain in\n106\t/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies, W-GC under the complete encapsulation. Local verdict:\n107\tstep 1, `c1 : read3(Y)` via `z`, is `ok` at the kernel (O9, `gc_read`) and outside the\n108\tguard-free forms (`Exer5` of `z` passes through the live `guarded`), its state being reached by\n109\tthe admitted setup. Suite: the setup, then steps 2 to 4 (`c0 : acquire(e)`, `write3(Y)`,\n110\t`read3(Y)` via `z`, through the grant), is a `RunFull` from the initial state; step 1 changes no\n111\tstate (O9). -/\n112\ttheorem W_GC_full : opStepC KM (.read 3 [4]) 1 gc6 (.ok gc7) ∧\n113\t    ¬ PremG KM L0 (gc6, greg, []) (.kernel 1 (.read 3 [4])) ∧\n114\t    cgσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init zst), [], []) ∧ RunFull KM L0 cgσ cgLbls := by\n115\t  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(gc0, [], []), (gc1, [], []), (gc2, [], []), (gc3, [], []),\n116\t      (gc4, [], []), (gc4, greg, []), (gc5, greg, []), (gc6, greg, []), (cg7, cgReg, []),\n117\t      (cg8, cgReg, []), (cg9, cgReg, [])] cgLbls :=\n118\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n119\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n120\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n121\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n122\t    .cons (by decide) (.newMutex ⟨by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n123\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n124\t    .cons (by decide) (.spawn ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n125\t    .cons (by decide) (.acquire ⟨by decide, ⟨4, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n126\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n127\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) .nil\n128\t  exact ⟨gc_read.2, by decide, rfl,\n129\t    runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide)⟩\n130\t\n131\t/-! ## W-GS -/\n132\t\n133\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedStore in\n134\t/-- W-GS, suite without step 1: `c1 : acquire(e)` from the state before step 1, grant `g₁`,\n135\tauthority 6, held by frame 1. -/\n136\tdef sg6 : SC := deriveSyncEff gs5 1 3\n137\t/-- W-GS, suite: `c1 : read3(T)` via `g₁` (O9). -/\n138\tdef sg7 : SC := sg6.set (sg6.view 1)\n139\t\n140\t/-- The labels of the positive suite of W-GS. -/\n141\tdef sgLbls : List Label :=\n142\t  GuardedStore.setupLbls ++ [.acquire 1 0, .kernel 1 (.read 6 [3])]\n143\t\n144\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedStore in\n145\t/-- The named states of the positive suite of W-GS. -/\n146\tdef sgσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n147\t  [(gs0, [], []), (gs1, [], []), (gs2, [], []), (gs2, sreg, []), (gs3, sreg, []),\n148\t    (gs4, sreg, []), (gs5, sreg, []), (sg6, sregG, []), (sg7, sregG, [])].getD i\n149\t    (sg7, sregG, [])\n150\t\n151\topen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedStore in\n152\t/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies, W-GS under the complete encapsulation. Local verdict:\n153\tstep 1, `c0 : store(z2, T)` without the grant, is `ok` at the kernel (O8, `W_GS_1_ok`) and\n154\toutside the guard-free forms (the right on `T`, Spec 1 §65.2, holds only through `guarded`), its\n155\tstate being reached by the admitted setup. Suite: the setup, then steps 2 and 3 replayed from the\n156\tstate before step 1, is a `RunFull` from the initial state; there, unlike in W-GS, `z2` is still\n157\theld by `f0` (step 2 and 3 do not read it). The twin is a `RunFull` (`runAmF_traces_full`). -/\n158\ttheorem W_GS_full : opStepC KM (.store 4 3) 0 gs5 (.ok gs6) ∧\n159\t    ¬ PremG KM L0 (gs5, sreg, []) (.kernel 0 (.store 4 3)) ∧\n160\t    sgσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init GuardedChain.zst), [], []) ∧ RunFull KM L0 sgσ sgLbls := by\n161\t  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(gs0, [], []), (gs1, [], []), (gs2, [], []), (gs2, sreg, []),\n162\t      (gs3, sreg, []), (gs4, sreg, []), (gs5, sreg, []), (sg6, sregG, []), (sg7, sregG, [])]\n163\t      sgLbls :=\n164\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n165\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n166\t    .cons (by decide) (.newMutex ⟨by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n167\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n168\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n169\t    .cons (by decide) (.spawn ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n170\t    .cons (by decide) (.acquire ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n171\t    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) .nil\n172\t  exact ⟨W_GS_1_ok, by decide, rfl,\n173\t    runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide)⟩\n174\t\n175\t/-! ## Traces under an older encapsulation -/\n176\t\n177\t/-- The labels of S2 (`s2_trace`): `MX₄`, `c1 : acquire(e)`, `write3(T)`, `unlock(e)`. -/\n178\tdef s2Lbls : List Label := mx4Lbls ++ [.acquire 1 0, .kernel 1 (.write 5 [3]), .unlock 1 0]\n179\t\n180\t/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` §1 S2 (`s2_trace`, `cycle_trace5`) is a `RunFull` from the initial"}]},"uuid":"fd34b3eb-bd4b-420f-b1a2-88323f507457","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:38:36.618Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/Replay.lean","content":"import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.NonRegression\nimport Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedRead\nimport Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain\nimport Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.S10\nimport Ern.Concurrency.EncapTraces\nimport Ern.Concurrency.Traces\n\n/-!\n# Traces replayed under the complete encapsulation\n\nBrief of milestone 4, slice 3, complement, task 6 (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies,\n\"Traces rejouées\").\n\n* W-GR, W-GC, W-GS: the excluded step is a local verdict, `ok` at the kernel and outside the\n  guard-free forms, on its starting state, reached from the initial state by an admitted prefix;\n  the positive suite (the setup, then the remaining steps, without the excluded one) is a\n  `RunFull` from the initial state.\n* The traces that existed only under an older encapsulation (S2, S3 in full, S4, S9, S10, the\n  traces of WC4 in `Traces` and `EncapTraces`) are `RunFull` traces.\n-/\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Replay\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Witness (instDecidableEncap5R)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\nopen Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)\n\n/-- A prefix of a `RunFull` is a `RunFull`. -/\ntheorem RunFull.take {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\n    {lbls : List Label} (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) (n : Nat) : RunFull k L σ (lbls.take n) :=\n  fun i hi => by\n    have hi' : i < lbls.length := by simp at hi; omega\n    have e : (lbls.take n)[i] = lbls[i] := List.getElem_take\n    rw [e]; exact h i hi'\n\n/-! ## W-GR -/\n\n/-- W-GR, suite without step 1: `c0 : acquire(e)` from `MX₄`, grant `g`, authority 5. -/\ndef wr5 : SC := deriveSyncEff x4 0 3\n/-- W-GR, suite: `c0 : write3(T)` via `g` (O10). -/\ndef wr6 : SC := wr5.set (write3Eff (wr5.view 0) [3])\n/-- The registry with `g` recorded. -/\ndef wrReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 5⟩]\n\n/-- The labels of `MX₄`. -/\ndef mx4Lbls : List Label :=\n  [.kernel 0 (.derive 1 [3] .modify), .kernel 0 (.store 3 1), .newMutex 0 3,\n   .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] []]\n\n/-- The labels of the positive suite of W-GR. -/\ndef wrLbls : List Label := mx4Lbls ++ [.acquire 0 0, .kernel 0 (.write 5 [3])]\n\n/-- The named states of the positive suite of W-GR. -/\ndef wrσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []),\n    (wr5, wrReg, []), (wr6, wrReg, [])].getD i (wr6, wrReg, [])\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies, W-GR under the complete encapsulation. Local verdict:\nstep 1, `c1 : read3(T)` with `access = guarded` from `MX₄`, is `ok` at the kernel (O9) and outside\nthe guard-free forms (its access authority is the live `guarded`, WC5.2 C22 item 6), `MX₄` being\nreached by the admitted prefix of the suite. Suite: `MX₄`, then steps 2 and 3, is a `RunFull`\nfrom the initial state; step 1 changes no state (O9), so the suite does not depend on it. -/\ntheorem W_GR_full : opStepC KM (.read 3 [3]) 1 x4 (.ok GuardedRead.gr1) ∧\n    ¬ PremG KM L0 (x4, regX, []) (.kernel 1 (.read 3 [3])) ∧\n    wrσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧ RunFull KM L0 wrσ wrLbls := by\n  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []), (wr5, wrReg, []),\n      (wr6, wrReg, [])]\n      [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [], .acquire 0 0,\n        .kernel 0 (.write 5 [3])] :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.spawn ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.acquire ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) .nil\n  exact ⟨GuardedRead.W_GR_1_ok, by decide, rfl,\n    runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R ((ClassifyWitness.mx3_steps h).run _) (by decide))\n      (by decide)⟩\n\n/-! ## W-GC -/\n\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain in\n/-- W-GC, suite without step 1: `c0 : acquire(e)`, grant `g`, authority 6. -/\ndef cg7 : SC := deriveSyncEff GuardedChain.gc6 0 4\n/-- W-GC, suite: `c0 : write3(Y)` via `z` (O10). -/\ndef cg8 : SC := cg7.set (write3Eff (cg7.view 0) [4])\n/-- W-GC, suite: `c0 : read3(Y)` via `z` (O9). -/\ndef cg9 : SC := cg8.set (cg8.view 0)\n/-- The registry with `g` recorded. -/\ndef cgReg : SyncReg := [⟨4, some 6⟩]\n\n/-- The labels of the positive suite of W-GC: the setup, then steps 2 to 4. -/\ndef cgLbls : List Label :=\n  GuardedChain.glbls.take 7 ++ [.acquire 0 0, .kernel 0 (.write 3 [4]), .kernel 0 (.read 3 [4])]\n\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain in\n/-- The named states of the positive suite of W-GC. -/\ndef cgσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(gc0, [], []), (gc1, [], []), (gc2, [], []), (gc3, [], []), (gc4, [], []), (gc4, greg, []),\n    (gc5, greg, []), (gc6, greg, []), (cg7, cgReg, []), (cg8, cgReg, []), (cg9, cgReg, [])].getD i\n    (cg9, cgReg, [])\n\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChain in\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies, W-GC under the complete encapsulation. Local verdict:\nstep 1, `c1 : read3(Y)` via `z`, is `ok` at the kernel (O9, `gc_read`) and outside the\nguard-free forms (`Exer5` of `z` passes through the live `guarded`), its state being reached by\nthe admitted setup. Suite: the setup, then steps 2 to 4 (`c0 : acquire(e)`, `write3(Y)`,\n`read3(Y)` via `z`, through the grant), is a `RunFull` from the initial state; step 1 changes no\nstate (O9). -/\ntheorem W_GC_full : opStepC KM (.read 3 [4]) 1 gc6 (.ok gc7) ∧\n    ¬ PremG KM L0 (gc6, greg, []) (.kernel 1 (.read 3 [4])) ∧\n    cgσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init zst), [], []) ∧ RunFull KM L0 cgσ cgLbls := by\n  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(gc0, [], []), (gc1, [], []), (gc2, [], []), (gc3, [], []),\n      (gc4, [], []), (gc4, greg, []), (gc5, greg, []), (gc6, greg, []), (cg7, cgReg, []),\n      (cg8, cgReg, []), (cg9, cgReg, [])] cgLbls :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.newMutex ⟨by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.spawn ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.acquire ⟨by decide, ⟨4, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) .nil\n  exact ⟨gc_read.2, by decide, rfl,\n    runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-! ## W-GS -/\n\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedStore in\n/-- W-GS, suite without step 1: `c1 : acquire(e)` from the state before step 1, grant `g₁`,\nauthority 6, held by frame 1. -/\ndef sg6 : SC := deriveSyncEff gs5 1 3\n/-- W-GS, suite: `c1 : read3(T)` via `g₁` (O9). -/\ndef sg7 : SC := sg6.set (sg6.view 1)\n\n/-- The labels of the positive suite of W-GS. -/\ndef sgLbls : List Label :=\n  GuardedStore.setupLbls ++ [.acquire 1 0, .kernel 1 (.read 6 [3])]\n\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedStore in\n/-- The named states of the positive suite of W-GS. -/\ndef sgσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(gs0, [], []), (gs1, [], []), (gs2, [], []), (gs2, sreg, []), (gs3, sreg, []),\n    (gs4, sreg, []), (gs5, sreg, []), (sg6, sregG, []), (sg7, sregG, [])].getD i\n    (sg7, sregG, [])\n\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedStore in\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 §2 terdecies, W-GS under the complete encapsulation. Local verdict:\nstep 1, `c0 : store(z2, T)` without the grant, is `ok` at the kernel (O8, `W_GS_1_ok`) and\noutside the guard-free forms (the right on `T`, Spec 1 §65.2, holds only through `guarded`), its\nstate being reached by the admitted setup. Suite: the setup, then steps 2 and 3 replayed from the\nstate before step 1, is a `RunFull` from the initial state; there, unlike in W-GS, `z2` is still\nheld by `f0` (step 2 and 3 do not read it). The twin is a `RunFull` (`runAmF_traces_full`). -/\ntheorem W_GS_full : opStepC KM (.store 4 3) 0 gs5 (.ok gs6) ∧\n    ¬ PremG KM L0 (gs5, sreg, []) (.kernel 0 (.store 4 3)) ∧\n    sgσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init GuardedChain.zst), [], []) ∧ RunFull KM L0 sgσ sgLbls := by\n  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(gs0, [], []), (gs1, [], []), (gs2, [], []), (gs2, sreg, []),\n      (gs3, sreg, []), (gs4, sreg, []), (gs5, sreg, []), (sg6, sregG, []), (sg7, sregG, [])]\n      sgLbls :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.newMutex ⟨by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.spawn ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.acquire ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩) .nil\n  exact ⟨W_GS_1_ok, by decide, rfl,\n    runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-! ## Traces under an older encapsulation -/\n\n/-- The labels of S2 (`s2_trace`): `MX₄`, `c1 : acquire(e)`, `write3(T)`, `unlock(e)`. -/\ndef s2Lbls : List Label := mx4Lbls ++ [.acquire 1 0, .kernel 1 (.write 5 [3]), .unlock 1 0]\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` §1 S2 (`s2_trace`, `cycle_trace5`) is a `RunFull` from the initial","numLines":180,"startLine":1,"totalLines":346}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c480a741-89bf-43c7-ac6e-83b6b93c01fc","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
