{"parentUuid":"c416a688-984d-4c60-807f-1ef631facadb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011G4YgTK5kdQP58RRTZAofp","type":"tool_result","content":"    revert this; decide\n  · have := h ⟨1, none⟩ (List.mem_singleton_self _) (by decide)\n    revert this; decide\n\n/-- `c0 : transfer(M, M′)` (O4). -/\ndef w2 : SC := transferEffC w0 0 0 7\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` §2 W-C22.3 (b), twin, `ok`: in the same configuration (`slot = {a, b}`),\n`transfer(M, M′)` by context 0 is an `ok` step of Spec 1 §63 re-indexed that `Encap` admits; after\nit `SlotInit` holds. -/\ntheorem W_C22_3b_ok : opStepC KW (.transfer 0 7) 0 w0 (.ok w2) ∧\n    Encap L0 (w0, [⟨1, none⟩]) (.kernel 0 (.transfer 0 7)) ∧ SlotInit w2 [⟨1, none⟩] :=\n  ⟨⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩, (by decide : TransferExcl L0 (w0, [⟨1, none⟩]) 0),\n    fun e he _ => by rw [List.mem_singleton.1 he]; decide⟩\n\n/-! ## S17a, positive twin of the corpus (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` §1 S17a) -/\n\nopen Ern.Concurrency.EncapTraces in\n/-- `c0 : endUse(slot)` from `EncapTraces.e2` (`MX₃`) (O12). -/\ndef eS : SC := EncapTraces.e2.set (endUseEff (EncapTraces.e2.view 0) 1)\n/-- `c0 : endUse(lock)` (O12). -/\ndef eL : SC := eS.set (endUseEff (eS.view 0) 2)\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` §1 S17a, positive twin, `ok`: from `MX₃` (`EncapTraces.e2`, reached by\nthe encapsulated trace `EncapTraces.traceMutex`), `endUse(slot)` is an `ok` step admitted by\n`Encap` that kills the entry (§69 releases `guarded`); then `endUse(lock)` is an `ok` step\nadmitted by `Encap`, no entry being live. -/\ntheorem S17a_2_ok : opStepC K0 (.endUse 1) 0 EncapTraces.e2 (.ok eS) ∧\n    Encap L0 (EncapTraces.e2, EncapTraces.reg1) (.kernel 0 (.endUse 1)) ∧\n    ¬ (⟨4, none⟩ : SyncEntry).Live eS ∧ opStepC K0 (.endUse 2) 0 eS (.ok eL) ∧\n    Encap L0 (eS, EncapTraces.reg1) (.kernel 0 (.endUse 2)) := by\n  refine ⟨⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩, ?_, by decide, ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩,\n    fun e he hl => ?_⟩\n  · exact (by decide : ∀ e ∈ EncapTraces.reg1, e.Live EncapTraces.e2 →\n      ControlOf L0 EncapTraces.e2 e ≠ some 1 ∧\n      OptP (slotOf EncapTraces.e2 e.guarded) (fun q => partOf EncapTraces.e2.P 1 q → 1 = q) True)\n  · exact absurd hl (by rw [List.mem_singleton.1 he]; decide)\n\n/-! ## The separation of the registries is needed by theorem 4 (Spec 1 §56; WC4 C13.7) -/\n\n/-- An arena registry whose entry administers `T` with `internal = guarded` of the live entry of\n`MX₃`: excluded on reached states by the unified guard (`NewArenaPreC.guard`, `lstep_adminSep`). -/\ndef arBad : ArenaReg := [⟨3, 3, [3], []⟩]\n/-- `split(guarded, [T])` by context 0 (O2). -/\ndef xb1 : SC := x2.set (splitEff (x2.view 0) 3 [[3]])\nErn/Concurrency/RegIndex.lean:19:theorem reg_set_guarded {reg : SyncReg} {i : Nat} {e e' : SyncEntry} (he : reg[i]? = some e)\nErn/Concurrency/RegIndex.lean:32:theorem lstep_reg {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {lbl : Label} {st st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\nErn/Concurrency/RegIndex.lean:64:theorem reg_stable {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\nErn/Concurrency/RegIndex.lean:81:theorem reg_stable_run5C {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\nErn/Concurrency/EventsStrictProtocols.lean:24:theorem handoffOrdered_no_raceS {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics}\nErn/Concurrency/EventsStrictProtocols.lean:42:theorem spawn_ordersS {k : K} {L' L : MutexLayout}\nErn/Concurrency/EventsStrictProtocols.lean:61:theorem join_ordersS {k : K} {L' L : MutexLayout}\nErn/Concurrency/EventsStrictProtocols.lean:105:theorem lock_ordersS_gaps {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {L : MutexLayout}\nErn/Concurrency/EventsStrictProtocols.lean:149:theorem lock_ordersS {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {L : MutexLayout} {lbls : List Label}\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:12:* theorem 2 for every labelled step of the kernel with the synchronization and arena libraries,\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:14:* theorems 2, 4 and 7 together along an `EncapsulatedTrace` (WC4 C22, C23; Spec 1 §55, §56):\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:28:theorem lstep_kInvCA {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {lbl : Label} {st st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:59:/-- The library invariants carried along traces: `SyncState` (theorem 4, WC4 C21, C22), the\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:61:(theorem 7, Spec 1 §55). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:67:theorem libInv_nil {L : MutexLayout} {s : SC} {reg : SyncReg} :\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:75:theorem lstep_inv {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {lbl : Label} {st st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:87:theorem trace_inv {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {st st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbls : List Label}\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:98:theorem trace_preserves {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {st st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg}\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:105:theorem init_inv {k : K} {statics : Statics} (hdd : DDSound k) (hst : StaticsOK statics)\nErn/Concurrency/Reachable.lean:131:theorem encapsulated_inv {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {statics : Statics} {lbls : List Label}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5d16e42c-45bd-497a-8c5a-7c7ddf264daa","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:40:44.520Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"    revert this; decide\n  · have := h ⟨1, none⟩ (List.mem_singleton_self _) (by decide)\n    revert this; decide\n\n/-- `c0 : transfer(M, M′)` (O4). -/\ndef w2 : SC := transferEffC w0 0 0 7\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` §2 W-C22.3 (b), twin, `ok`: in the same configuration (`slot = {a, b}`),\n`transfer(M, M′)` by context 0 is an `ok` step of Spec 1 §63 re-indexed that `Encap` admits; after\nit `SlotInit` holds. -/\ntheorem W_C22_3b_ok : opStepC KW (.transfer 0 7) 0 w0 (.ok w2) ∧\n    Encap L0 (w0, [⟨1, none⟩]) (.kernel 0 (.transfer 0 7)) ∧ SlotInit w2 [⟨1, none⟩] :=\n  ⟨⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩, (by decide : TransferExcl L0 (w0, [⟨1, none⟩]) 0),\n    fun e he _