","type":"assistant","uuid":"f88a2f79-2eff-46b5-88db-d1e922510ceb","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:45:11.214Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"f88a2f79-2eff-46b5-88db-d1e922510ceb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015e1S4T9Yz4bxPko8yvRQDs","type":"tool_result","content":"or by a usable place whose terminal owner survives. -/\ndef Survives (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (x : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (s.A[x]?) (fun y => y.active = true ∧ HolderLive { s with F := F₀ } y.holder) False\n\n/-- Decidability of `Survives` (§73.4). -/\ninstance (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (x : Nat) : Decidable (Survives s F₀ x) := by\n  unfold Survives; infer_instance\n\n/-- First surviving authority of a list (§73.4). -/\ndef firstSurv (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (l : List Nat) : Option Nat :=\n  l.find? fun z => decide (Survives s F₀ z)\n\n/-- Authority `a` after the exit (§73, `ok` effect): released unless it survives; a surviving\nderived authority is reanchored to the first surviving active origin of its chain. -/\ndef exitG (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (a : Nat) (y : Authority) : Authority :=\n  if Survives s F₀ a then\n    match y.origin with\n    | none => y\n    | some _ => { y with origin := firstSurv s F₀ (s.ancs a) }\n  else { y with active := false }\n\n/-- Effect of `exitFrame` (§73, `ok` effect): the current frame is popped; authorities that do\nnot survive are released; surviving derived authorities and the anchors of `D` are reanchored to\nthe first surviving authority of their chains. -/\ndef exitEff (s : S3) : S3 :=\n  { s with\n    F := s.F.tail\n    D := fun q => (s.D q).map fun x => (firstSurv s s.F.tail (x :: s.ancs x)).getD x\n    A := mapI (exitG s s.F.tail) 0 s.A }\n\n/-- Preconditions of `exitFrame` (§73). The result clause of §73.2 is not represented. -/\nstructure ExitPre (k : K) (s : S3) : Prop where\n  /-- §73.1: the current frame is not the initial frame and has a surviving caller. -/\n  hasCaller : s.F.tail ≠ []\n  /-- §73.2, §73.4, §73.5: every anchor of a place usable after the exit has a surviving\n  authority among itself and its origins. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean:225:def exitEffC (s : SC) (c : Nat) : SC :=\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-226-  { s.set (exitEff (s.view c)) with\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-227-    C := reparent (s.C.modify c fun x => { x with stack := x.stack.tail })\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-228-      ((s.stk c).headD 0) ((s.stk c).tail.headD 0) }\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-229-\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-230-/-- Preconditions of `exitFrameC` executed by `c` (Spec 1 §73 re-indexed; WC4 C6, C6.1: O7.1\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-231-transposed, O7.2–O7.5 on the global state). The surviving frames are the other globally live\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-232-frames. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-233-structure ExitPreC (k : K) (s : SC) (c : Nat) : Prop where\n--\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean:353:def termEffC (s : SC) (c : Nat) : SC :=\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-354-  { s.set (exitEff (s.view c)) with\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-355-    C := reparent (s.C.modify c fun x => { x with stack := [], life := .done })\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-356-      ((s.stk c).headD 0) ((s.ctxParent c).getD 0) }\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-357-\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-358-/-- Preconditions of `terminate` executed by `c` (WC4 C7: the O7 validity requirements applied to\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-359-the initial frame of a terminating non-initial context, after its nested call frames have\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-360-ended). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-361-structure TermPre (k : K) (s : SC) (c : Nat) : Prop where","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e5978b09-2f8a-47d9-af49-c3aca8a462a4","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:45:12.010Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"or by a usable place whose terminal owner survives. -/\ndef Survives (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (x : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (s.A[x]?) (fun y => y.active = true ∧ HolderLive { s with F := F₀ } y.holder) False\n\n/-- Decidability of `Survives` (§73.4). -/\ninstance (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (x : Nat) : Decidable (Survives s F₀ x) := by\n  unfold Survives; infer_instance\n\n/-- First surviving authority of a list (§73.4). -/\ndef firstSurv (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (l : List Nat) : Option Nat :=\n  l.find? fun z => decide (Survives s F₀ z)\n\n/-- Authority `a` after the exit (§73, `ok` effect): released unless it survives; a surviving\nderived authority is reanchored to the first surviving active origin of its chain. -/\ndef exitG (s : S3) (F₀ : Frames) (a : Nat) (y : Authority) : Authority :=\n  if Survives s F₀ a then\n    match y.origin with\n    | none => y\n    | some _ => { y with origin := firstSurv s F₀ (s.ancs a) }\n  else { y with active := false }\n\n/-- Effect of `exitFrame` (§73, `ok` effect): the current frame is popped; authorities that do\nnot survive are released; surviving derived authorities and the anchors of `D` are reanchored to\nthe first surviving authority of their chains. -/\ndef exitEff (s : S3) : S3 :=\n  { s with\n    F := s.F.tail\n    D := fun q => (s.D q).map fun x => (firstSurv s s.F.tail (x :: s.ancs x)).getD x\n    A := mapI (exitG s s.F.tail) 0 s.A }\n\n/-- Preconditions of `exitFrame` (§73). The result clause of §73.2 is not represented. -/\nstructure ExitPre (k : K) (s : S3) : Prop where\n  /-- §73.1: the current frame is not the initial frame and has a surviving caller. -/\n  hasCaller : s.F.tail ≠ []\n  /-- §73.2, §73.4, §73.5: every anchor of a place usable after the exit has a surviving\n  authority among itself and its origins. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean:225:def exitEffC (s : SC) (c : Nat) : SC :=\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-226-  { s.set (exitEff (s.view c)) with\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-227-    C := reparent (s.C.modify c fun x => { x with stack := x.stack.tail })\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-228-      ((s.stk c).headD 0) ((s.stk c).tail.headD 0) }\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-229-\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-230-/-- Preconditions of `exitFrameC` executed by `c` (Spec 1 §73 re-indexed; WC4 C6, C6.1: O7.1\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-231-transposed, O7.2–O7.5 on the global state). The surviving frames are the other globally live\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-232-frames. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-233-structure ExitPreC (k : K) (s : SC) (c : Nat) : Prop where\n--\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean:353:def termEffC (s : SC) (c : Nat) : SC :=\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-354-  { s.set (exitEff (s.view c)) with\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-355-    C := reparent (s.C.modify c fun x => { x with stack := [], life := .done })\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-356-      ((s.stk c).headD 0) ((s.ctxParent c).getD 0) }\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-357-\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-358-/-- Preconditions of `terminate` executed by `c` (WC4 C7: the O7 validity requirements applied to\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-359-the initial frame of a terminating non-initial context, after its nested call frames have\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-360-ended). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-361-structure TermPre (k : K) (s : SC) (c : Nat) : Prop where","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8fba500b-83c6-4d45-8667-e21cdd4fd340","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f88a2f79-2eff-46b5-88db-d1e922510ceb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType"