{"parentUuid":"fcc9790f-3c1a-4df5-acb0-d0d14d0cf486","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013S6rAztRjnyZyi9hqtoAsV","type":"tool_result","content":"668:## 60. O1 — Derivation of an Authority\n679:## 61. O2 — Splitting Authorities\n  /-- WC4 C13.7, Spec 1 §56: `guarded` is not the identity of another live entry. -/\n  unique : ∀ e ∈ reg, e.Live s → e.guarded ≠ g\n  /-- WC4 C13.7, Spec 1 §56: `guarded` is not the `internal` identity of a live arena of the\n  arena registry. -/\n  otherAdmin : g ∉ Arena.liveInternals s.flat ar\n  /-- WC4 C13.8: no other live entry is associated with `ctl`. -/\n  ctlUnique : OptP (ControlOf L s ⟨g, none⟩) (fun ctl => ∀ e ∈ reg, e.Live s →\n    ControlOf L s e ≠ some ctl) False\n  /-- WC4 C13.9. -/\n  available : NoCoveringDesc s g\n\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v12 §2 undecies, `alloc`, provider containing the controller: from `MX₃`,\n`c0 : alloc(provider = M, owner = lock′)` is an `ok` kernel step, as expected (Spec 1 §71.2: the\nleaves of `M` are `Init`, `Modify` exercisable through `root_M`; §71.3), admitted by `Encap5R`, and\nthe trace is a `Run5R` from the initial state; entry `e` stays live. The final restriction refuses\nit (the provider metadata accesses may write the controller leaf: the provider counts by its\nleaves, `lock` among them); the trace is no `Run7`. -/\ntheorem alloc_provider_M_refused : pmσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧\n    opStepC KM (.alloc 0 6 [(none, 0)]) 0 x2 (.ok pm1) ∧ Run5R KM L0 pmσ pmLbls ∧\n    (⟨3, none⟩ : SyncEntry).Live pm1 ∧ TouchesF L0 (pmσ 3) (.kernel 0 (.alloc 0 6 [(none, 0)])) 2 ∧\n    ¬ CtlRestrF L0 (pmσ 3) (.kernel 0 (.alloc 0 6 [(none, 0)])) (pmσ 4) ∧\n    ¬ Run7 KM L0 pmσ pmLbls := by\n  have ha : opStepC KM (.alloc 0 6 [(none, 0)]) 0 x2 (.ok pm1) :=\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:32:theorem store_refusedF : ¬ CtlRestrF L0 (csσ 4) (.kernel 0 (.store 4 2)) (csσ 5) ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:40:theorem issue_refusedF : ¬ CtlRestrF L0 (ciσ 7) (.issue 0 0 [5] 2) (ciσ 8) ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:48:theorem alloc_refusedF :\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:68:theorem alloc_owner_M_admitted : amσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:95:theorem alloc_provider_M_refused : pmσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:113:theorem depend_admitted : Run7 KM L0 tdσ tdLbls :=\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:121:theorem twins_run7 : Run7 KM L0 tsσ tsLbls ∧ Run7 KA L0 tiσ tiLbls ∧ Run7 KM L0 taσ taLbls ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:134:theorem W_NC_3_amended_reject : (∀ st', ¬ NewMutexAmOk KM L0 [] rc2 [] 0 3 st') ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:141:theorem W_NC_twin_amended_ok : NewMutexAmOk KM L0 [] x2 [] 0 3 (x2, regX) :=\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/FinalWitness.lean:146:theorem W_NC_not_amendedF : Run7 KM L0 ncσ ncLbls ∧ ¬ RunAmF KM L0 ncσ ncLbls := by\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/AmendWitness.lean:27:theorem store_refused : ¬ CtlRestr L0 (csσ 4) (.kernel 0 (.store 4 2)) (csσ 5) ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/AmendWitness.lean:35:theorem alloc_refused : ¬ CtlRestr L0 (caσ 3) (.kernel 0 (.alloc 1 2 [(none, 0)])) (caσ 4) ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/AmendWitness.lean:43:theorem issue_refused : ¬ CtlRestr L0 (ciσ 7) (.issue 0 0 [5] 2) (ciσ 8) ∧\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/AmendWitness.lean:64:theorem store_twin : tsσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧ Run6 KM L0 tsσ tsLbls := by\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/AmendWitness.lean:86:theorem alloc_twin : taσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧ Run6 KM L0 taσ taLbls := by\nformal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/AmendWitness.lean:108:theorem issue_twin : tiσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init arst), [], []) ∧ Run6 KA L0 tiσ tiLbls 