ierRequest":"6ddb5469-01aa-4a41-beea-2a7e87c1593b","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cgyw9KtdNQHifZu9YQooH","requestRef":"a622f645-cd31-4a71-a7dc-77a1cc9e7b32","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"3911c04a-c1e2-4ed6-a681-5745b95f8348","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:55:11.925Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"3911c04a-c1e2-4ed6-a681-5745b95f8348","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0139DsT8342TV7p27U2zNKgc","type":"tool_result","content":"## 40. Logical Places, Leaves, and Ownership\n\nA place has an identity, optionally a structural parent, an abstract `kind`, an owner `owner : Frame | Place`, and a logical death marker. Structural parenthood `partOf(p,q)` describes the subplaces of a value; `owner` describes **who keeps the storage** of a root place valid. An owned place may lie outside its owner's direct footprint; ownership and composition are therefore distinct.\n\nA **leaf** is a place with no structural children. `footprint(p)` contains the leaves of `p`, and access rights over a place are evaluated on those leaves. Places transitively owned by a value are not automatically leaves of its `footprint`. A logical unit of the access discipline does not automatically constitute an additional allocation in the elementary memory machine.\n\nA place `p` is **usable** (`Usable(s,p)`) if and only if:\n\n1. `p` exists and is not marked dead;\n2. if its owner is a frame, that frame belongs to the stack;\n3. if its owner is a place `q`, then `q` is itself usable and the chain terminates at a frame in the stack.\n\nAn ownership cycle makes no place usable. `placeFrame(p)` is the terminal frame of this chain when `p` is usable. Structural parts share their parent's owner and death marker. A value may be logically ended by `endUse` without the place that contained it becoming unusable; the substorages it owned may, however, die.\n\nA **root place** has no structural parent. Every **usable** root place has a root authority of own mode `Modify`, with no origin, held exactly by that place's owner (`RootHeld`). This authority cannot be transferred in isolation; root ownership follows a legal transfer of the owning value when necessary.\n\n## 41. Leaf Initialization States\n\nEvery tracked leaf has exactly one of the states `Uninit`, `Init`, or `Moved`.\n\n- `Uninit`: no initialized value available in this leaf.\n- `Init`: initialized value, subject to type, representation, and storage obligations.\n- `Moved`: value consumed by transfer, inaccessible as its former value.\n\nAggregates may be partially initialized. Both `Uninit` and `Moved` prohibit ordinary reads, while remaining distinct states for diagnostics and end-of-use obligations. An initialization state creates no access permission.\n\n## 42. Authorities, Modes, Holders, and Origins\n\nAn authority conceptually has the following fields:\n\n```text\nAuthority {\n    id\n    mode: Observe | Modify\n    origin?: AuthorityId\n    footprint: Set<Leaf>\n    holder: Frame | Place\n    active: Bool\n}\n```\n\n`origin` links a derived authority to its current origin. Authorities have fresh identities and well-formed origin chains. A root authority has no origin; a derived authority has one. Creating derived rights does not increase the scope or permitted mode of the origin.\n\nThe **holder** (`holder`) is not the **owner** (`owner`). An authority derived by `derive` or `split` is initially held by the current frame; `store` or a permitted transfer may make it held by a place. The derived `issue` operation proceeds through `split` followed by `store`. `release` does not release a root. There is no persistent `Suspended` field: suspension of rights is inferred from active descendants and applies leaf by leaf.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"18e8b4b7-c313-420e-9ca5-6b753de92d15","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:55:12.111Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 40. Logical Places, Leaves, and Ownership\n\nA place has an identity, optionally a structural parent, an abstract `kind`, an owner `owner : Frame | Place`, and a logical death marker. Structural parenthood `partOf(p,q)` describes the subplaces of a value; `owner` describes **who keeps the storage** of a root place valid. An owned place may lie outside its owner's direct footprint; ownership and composition are therefore distinct.\n\nA **leaf** is a place with no structural children. `footprint(p)` contains the leaves of `p`, and access rights over a place are evaluated on those leaves. Places transitively owned by a value are not automatically leaves of its `footprint`. A logical unit of the access discipline does not automatically constitute an additional allocation in the elementary memory machine.\n\nA place `p` is **usable** (`Usable(s,p)`) if and only if:\n\n1. `p` exists and is not marked dead;\n2. if its owner is a frame, that frame belongs to the stack;\n3. if its owner is a place `q`, then `q` is itself usable and the chain terminates at a frame in the stack.\n\nAn ownership cycle makes no place usable. `placeFrame(p)` is the terminal frame of this chain when `p` is usable. Structural parts share their parent's owner and death marker. A value may be logically ended by `endUse` without the place that contained it becoming unusable; the substorages it owned may, however, die.\n\nA **root place** has no structural parent. Every **usable** root place has a root authority of own mode `Modify`, with no origin, held exactly by that place's owner (`RootHeld`). This authority cannot be transferred in isolation; root ownership follows a legal transfer of the owning value when necessary.\n\n## 41. Leaf Initialization States\n\nEvery tracked leaf has exactly one of the states `Uninit`, `Init`, or `Moved`.\n\n- `Uninit`: no initialized value available in this leaf.\n- `Init`: initialized value, subject to type, representation, and storage obligations.\n- `Moved`: value consumed by transfer, inaccessible as its former value.\n\nAggregates may be partially initialized. Both `Uninit` and `Moved` prohibit ordinary reads, while remaining distinct states for diagnostics and end-of-use obligations. An initialization state creates no access permission.\n\n## 42. Authorities, Modes, Holders, and Origins\n\nAn authority conceptually has the following fields:\n\n```text\nAuthority {\n    id\n    mode: Observe | Modify\n    origin?: AuthorityId\n    footprint: Set<Leaf>\n    holder: Frame | Place\n    active: Bool\n}\n```\n\n`origin` links a derived authority to its current origin. Authorities have fresh identities and well-formed origin chains. A root authority has no origin; a derived authority has one. Creating derived rights does not increase the scope or permitted mode of the origin.\n\nThe **holder** (`holder`) is not the **owner** (`owner`). An authority derived by `derive` or `split` is initially held by the current frame; `store` or a permitted transfer may make it held by a place. The derived `issue` operation proceeds through `split` followed by `store`. `release` does not release a root. There is no persistent `Suspended` field: suspension of rights is inferred from active descendants and applies leaf by leaf.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6ddb5469-01aa-4a41-beea-2a7e87c1593b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3911c04a-c1e2-4ed6-a681-5745b95f8348","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/