{"parentUuid":"f0b486b8-f3b8-460f-ae6d-95984cc6de45","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad10e2fd-52be-47f7-a4f7-932245537372","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CCTr9WVeSMN91cGJh1FGcn","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: ern-formal-mm02-exploration\ndescription: \"Conventions of the ERN formal/ exploratory passes (MM-02 and MM-03 branches, French briefs, reports/ never merged, spec kept outside the repo, lake path, axiom rule)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180\n  modified: 2026-11-10T21:38:57.914Z\n...\n**Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions.\n\n**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_l\n- Spec 1 v0.1 validated and frozen by the owner on 2026-11-06: file stays `specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md` (project convention: version in the file name; an unversioned rename in 3f9fee2 was reverted by 9b33c26 on 2026-11-07); v0 file deleted, owner tags `memory-model-v0` on main. PR ernlang/ern#2 ready for review, not merged. Inter-spec boundaries: KExt (§42), §86 typing → Spec 4, MM3-H H16 → Spec 3, MM23-H16 → Spec 8 (address) + Spec 11 (width/encoding); the lowest-address rule is a non-normative reference realization, not §82.3. Next-revision note: §81 omits Spec 8. \n\n- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23/J3/derivability, Spec 2 m1–m3 (WC2–WC4), m4 handoff (WC5, corpus v4–v6, ChainExcl, PlaceExcl), m4 event pass (WC5.1, corpus v8, po/sw/hb), m4 herd7/RC11 litmus pass, m4 strict mutex edge (corpus v9), m4 layer E event fragment (WC5.1 corrigé), m4 layer R mutex realization (corpus v10, 3 controller counterexamples) corrective pass (Run6, proposed C22.4/C18 amendments, W-NC) final pass (Run7, TouchesF, proposed C13.11) and slice 3 complete encapsulation (FullEncap, RunFull, task 5 refuted), reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule\n- [No Co-Authored-By trailer](feedback-no-coauthored-by.md) — never add the Claude co-author line to commits; main rewritten 2026-11-05","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5fbfe471-99fc-4688-8d22-b12adbddd228","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:56:00.781Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: ern-formal-mm02-exploration\ndescription: \"Conventions of the ERN formal/ exploratory passes (MM-02 and MM-03 branches, French briefs, reports/ never merged, spec kept outside the repo, lake path, axiom rule)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180\n  modified: 2026-11-10T21:38:57.914Z\n...\n**Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions.\n\n**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_l\n- Spec 1 v0.1 validated and frozen by the owner on 2026-11-06: file stays `specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md` (project convention: version in the file name; an unversioned rename in 3f9fee2 was reverted by 9b33c26 on 2026-11-07); v0 file deleted, owner tags `memory-model-v0` on main. PR ernlang/ern#2 ready for review, not merged. Inter-spec boundaries: KExt (§42), §86 typing → Spec 4, MM3-H H16 → Spec 3, MM23-H16 → Spec 8 (address) + Spec 11 (width/encoding); the lowest-address rule is a non-normative reference realization, not §82.3. Next-revision note: §81 omits Spec 8. \n\n- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23/J3/derivability, Spec 2 m1–m3 (WC2–WC4), m4 handoff (WC5, corpus v4–v6, ChainExcl, PlaceExcl), m4 event pass (WC5.1, corpus v8, po/sw/hb), m4 herd7/RC11 litmus pass, m4 strict mutex edge (corpus v9), m4 layer E event fragment (WC5.1 corrigé), m4 layer R mutex realization (corpus v10, 3 controller counterexamples) corrective pass (Run6, proposed C22.4/C18 amendments, W-NC) final pass (Run7, TouchesF, proposed C13.11) and slice 3 complete encapsulation (FullEncap, RunFull, task 5 refuted), reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule\n- [No Co-Authored-By trailer](feedback-no-coauthored-by.md) — never add the Claude co-author line to commits; main rewritten 2026-11-05","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"61df93c3-1168-4c7a-a838-41ce037a4bce","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean