{"parentUuid":"1b3b1fd0-37b4-4d55-965c-0a7bb74d0907","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"af17f01e-fb36-4c87-8f58-dbe0f151d425","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, SubagentHandback, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, advisor, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Current brief:** « Brief Claude Code — ERN Spec 2, jalon 4, tranche 3 : encapsulation complète, complément ».\n   - Branch `formal/spec2-m4`; exploratory and never merged.\n   - Attachments: corpus `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v14 (§2 terdecies) and `ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.2.md` (unchanged).\n   - Owner decisions:\n     1. Task 5 becomes a statement in three cases (a disjunction), with closure of the descendance.\n     2. Reanchoring (§73) is not an issuance under C22 point 1.\n     3. « Entrée vivante » means live before and after the step.\n     4. Open points are taken up in this pass.\n\n   **Tasks:**\n   1. Witnesses W-AG, W-AG-J, W-AG′ and the strict graph.\n   2. Closure of covering descendants: 28-kind table with three columns (creates an authority / changes a direct origin link / can make an authority enter, and by which case), plus a status; check (2′) for composites.\n   3. Dying leaves: (i) a protected leaf doesn't die; (ii) no other context has cap5 on a dying leaf; which kinds kill leaves; invariants; the exc_* witnesses.\n   4. spawnVal capacity before the step.\n   5. Empty set without grant, last acquire, three cases, and the corpus fact « Donnée protégée » as a separate theorem.\n   6. Replay W-GR, W-GC, W-GS (local verdict vs RunFull suite; if a remaining step depends on the excluded step's state, present it as a local verification), then S4, S9 and the WC4 traces.\n\n   **Report:** a French « Complément » section in `formal/reports/spec2-m4-encap.md`.\n\n   **Constraints (verbatim):**\n   - « Formalisation exploratoire, jamais mergée. Pas de push sur `main`, pas de PR. »\n   - « Ne modifie ni `specs/`, ni `AGENTS.md`, ni `CLAUDE.md`, ni `formal/DESIGN.md`, ni aucun fichier de `formal/Ern/MemoryModel/`. »\n   - « N'ajoute aucune hypothèse pour obtenir un énoncé. Les hypothèses admises sont celles de `capacity_run` : `DDSound`, `StaticsOK`, état initial, `RunFull`. Toute hypothèse de plus est un écart à rapporter, avec ce qui la rend nécessaire. »\n   - « Définitions existantes. Aucune n'est modifiée ni affaiblie … `protected_runFull_refuted` compris. Tout est ajouté à côté. »\n   - Lean rules:\n     - no sorry, admit, axiom, native_decide or noncomputable;\n     - axioms {propext, Quot.sound};\n     - `lake build` with no new warning;\n     - the AGENTS.md grep is empty;\n     - docstrings in English citing WC5.2, Spec 1, corpus v14 or the brief;\n     - verdicts come from the corpus or brief, never from the model;\n     - Conventional Commits **without Co-Authored-By** (the memory rule overrides the system reminder's attribution line).\n   - Out of scope: modifying WC5.2; forbidding a derivative to outlive the grant; D-C1 (reject vs non-habilité); OB-C20; realization conformance; a general race-freedom proof.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Toolchain: Lean 4 v4.35.0, no Mathlib. Build with `~/.elan/bin/lake build` in `formal/` (134 jobs); check one file with `lake env lean <file>`.\n   - `RunFull` = EncapFull (Encap7 ∧ PremG) ∧ LStep at each step. Prefix lemmas: `RunFull.take` (Replay) and `run5R_take` (DyingCap).\n   - L1, `cap5_drop_own (hdd) : Cap5DropOwn k L` (CapDrop:1332).\n     - Bridge: `run5R_trace` → `encapsulatedTrace5R_imp` → `encapsulatedTrace5C_imp`.\n     - Encap5 is built from Encap5C via `⟨he.1, chainExcl_guardedExcl he.2.1, he.2.2⟩`.\n   - Usable / dying:\n     - `Dying s s' l := isLeaf s.P l ∧ s.flat.Usable l ∧ ¬ s'.flat.Usable l` (Classify:32).\n     - Usable (Spec 1 §40) depends on dead, F and owners.\n     - `dead` is changed only by endUse (OwnedIn) and free (FreedPlace).\n     - Frames are removed only by exitEff (exitFrame, terminate).\n     - Owners change by transfer and spawnVal phases (to corr in dst).\n   - Origin: written only by `exitG` (§73.4 reanchor, used by exitFrame and terminate).\n     - Root creation (origin none): enterFrame, alloc, spawn, spawnVal.\n     - Derived creation: derive, split, issue (split of internal), reset (derive of internal, then released), acquire (deriveSync from guarded).\n   - `CoveringDesc` (SyncLib:158), `NoCoveringDesc` (:166), `GrantDiscipline` (:173); `available` is C13.9 (SyncLib:277).\n   - `runFull_inv` (Capacity:168) gives KInvCA ∧ LibInv via RunFull ⊆ Run7 ⊆ Run5R and `trace_inv`.\n   - Decide-based sweeps:\n     - `SweepOK` = ClosureStep ∧ ThreeOK (at Observe) ∧ OtherCapFree;\n     - `KillOK`.\n   - Index of corpus step k in W-AG = k+2. Identities: root_M = 0, guarded = 3, g = 5, x = 6, g′ = 7 / y = 7; places slot = 1, lock = 2, T = 3.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/DyingCap.lean** (new; commit 012921f; in Ern.lean after LastAcquire)\n     ```lean\n     theorem cap5_none_after {s s' : SC} {reg : SyncReg} {c l : Nat} (hP : PSkel s.P s'.P)\n         (hnd : NoDangling s'.flat) (hd : Dying s s' l) : cap5 s' reg c l = none\n     theorem run5R_take ... (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) (n : Nat) : Run5R k L σ (lbls.take n)\n     theorem other_cap_dying_run ... (hdd : DDSound k) (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], [])) (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {i : Nat} (hi : i < lbls.length) {c' l : Nat} (hc' : c' ≠ lbls[i].ctx) (hd : Dying (σ i).1 (σ (i + 1)).1 l) : cap5 (σ i).1 (σ i).2.1 c' l = none\n     theorem otherCapFree_run ... (hi) : OtherCapFree (σ i) lbls[i] (σ (i + 1)) :=\n       fun _ _ hc' _ _ hd => other_cap_dying_run hdd hstat h0 h hi hc' hd\n     ```\n     - Line numbers: cap5_none_after 26, run5R_take 43, other_cap_dying_run 55, otherCapFree_run 84.\n\n   - **ComplementSweep.lean** (commit 3477c4c)\n     - Adds `killKind : Label → Bool`: true for `.kernel _ (.endUse _)`, `.kernel _ (.free _ _)`, `.kernel _ .exit` and `.terminate _`.\n     - Adds `KillOK σ lbls`: ∀ i, ∀ l ∈ range P.length, Dying → killKind lbls[i] = true. It is decidable.\n     - Adds `sweep_kill` over the 33 traces.\n     - Line numbers: ThreeOK 37, SweepOK 50, sweep 62, killKind 87, KillOK 92, sweep_kill 102, W_AG_7_third 124.\n\n   - **Replay.lean** (commits 3477c4c, 2774cfe, 8ae69ee)\n     - Imports `Corpus.Witness` and `FullEncap.ComplementSweep`.\n     - `W_GR_full` (:72): `opStepC … x4 (.ok gr1) ∧ gr1 = x4 ∧ ¬PremG … ∧ wrσ 5 = (x4, regX, []) ∧ wrσ 0 = init ∧ RunFull`.\n     - `W_GC_full` (:117): adds `gc7 = gc6` and `cgσ 7 = (gc6, greg, [])`.\n     - `W_GS_full` (:145): `W_GS_1_ok ∧ ¬PremG (gs5, sreg) ∧ gsTwinσ 6 = (gs5, sreg, []) ∧ gsTwinσ 0 = init ∧ RunFull KM L0 gsTwinσ gsTwinLbls`. The proof uses `NonRegression.runAmF_traces_full.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1`. The old sg suite was removed.\n     - `W_GS_2_3_local` (:158): EncapFull ∧ LStep at (gs6, sreg) acquire 1 0 → (gs7, sregG), and at (gs7, sregG) read 6 [3] → (gs8, sregG). It is a local verification.\n     - Other theorems:\n       - S2_full :174, S10_full :180, S3_full :196, S4_full :232, S9_full :254;\n       - mutex_full :281 (mtσ, mtLbls, init mst), distinct_full :300 (dtσ, dtLbls, init mst3);\n       - wc4_full :324 (adds tAσ 0 = init est, tBσ 0 = tAσ 0);\n       - endUseM_full :362 (kmσ, kmLbls), endUseSlot_full :380 (ksσ, ksLbls, init sst);\n       - W_C22_3b_twin_full :400 (tbσ, tbLbls, KW, init wst), S17a_twin_full :423 (saσ, saLbls);\n       - sweep_replay :438 (SweepOK ∧ KillOK on 13 traces: wr, cg, s3f, s4, s9, mt, dt, tA, tB, km, ks, tb, sa).\n     - Citations use WC5.2 C13/C16/C17 and WC5.2 §V S18.\n\n   - **Other modules of this pass** (unchanged in this segment):\n     - AbandonedGrant: W_AG_run 81, W_AG_6_facts 93, W_AG_a 106, W_AG_b 118, W_AG_c 126, W_AG_d 135, W_AGJ_run 161, W_AG_strict 194, W_AGJ_strict 208, W_AGp_run 249, W_AGp_neg 278.\n     - Closure: GrantOf 178, ClosureStep 192, closure_step 282, closure_run 401.\n     - Dying: shape_step 53, protected_not_dying_run 174, OtherCapFree 190, exc_dying_facts 205.\n     - SpawnValCap: PhaseRel 72, spawnVal_cap_pre 342.\n     - LastAcquire: ProvCap 84, CapFrom 90, cov_of_attr 201, three_cases 236, protected_cap_run 275, empty_without_grant 295, last_acquire 371.\n\n   - **formal/reports/spec2-m4-encap.md**\n     - A pointer line was added under the title.\n     - The « Complément » section was inserted before « Annexe ». Its subsections:\n       - Sources (restricted to passages read);\n       - Commits;\n       - Définitions/écarts;\n       - Tâche 1 table, with the deviation: refusals b, c and the W-AG′ negative are « aucune issue ok », not reject;\n       - Tâche 2 (method; (2′) not needed; 28-kind table: 27 prouvés, 1 sans objet);\n       - Tâche 3 (kill-kinds **inachevé**, goal: `killKind lbls[i] = false → Usable (σ i) l → Usable (σ (i+1)) l`);\n       - Tâche 4;\n       - updated capacity table (12 prouvé / 2 / 2 / 12 / 0);\n       - Tâche 5 (GrantDiscipline via runFull_inv; frontiers C13.9, C17.2/C17.3, C18.2; provenance vs C46);\n       - Tâche 6 (local verdicts vs RunFull executions; trace census);\n       - refusals/counterexamples;\n       - spec problems (none new);\n       - OB-C28 open items;\n       - audit.\n     - Commits 415c498 and 1d53130 (amended; the row reads « `415c498` et le commit suivant »).\n\n   - **Memory**\n     - A « slice 3 complement » entry was added to `ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md`.\n     - The MEMORY.md index line was updated.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Fast compile times (0.4 s) looked suspicious; confirmed EXIT 0 and real elaboration.\n   - `SC` has no DecidableEq: used `rfl` for state equalities.\n   - Ambiguous `z2` (EncapTraces vs Corpus): qualified as `EncapTraces.z2`.\n   - `Witness.w0` resolved to the FullEncap.Witness namespace: used `Corpus.w0` etc. (namespace `Ern.Concurrency.Corpus`).\n   - BSD `sed` has no `\\|` in basic regex: used `sed -E` or python.\n   - EncapFull is not decidable directly: proved as `⟨⟨by decide, by decide⟩, by decide⟩`.\n   - zsh globbed `--include=*.lean`: quoted it.\n   - Docstring lines over 100 characters after edits: rewrapped.\n   - The amended commit hash invalidated a self-referencing table row: reworded the row.\n   - Advisor feedback applied:\n     - removed the unverified « aucun témoin ne le réalise »;\n     - marked kill-kinds inachevé with its goal;\n     - restricted sources to passages read (§40 and §42 read in full now);\n     - do not offer create_pr.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - All tasks 1–6 are done. Every statement of tasks 2–5 is proved, except the general kill-kinds lemma (inachevé; decide on 46 traces plus reading).\n   - No ok step refused, no positive trace refused, no counterexample.\n   - Audit: 2796 theorems / 1861 non-internal; 0 outside {propext, Quot.sound}; module sum 130 (94).\n   - lake build is clean; per-module warnings 0; grep empty.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Earlier in the session: the brief « tranche 3 : encapsulation complète » (completed), then the complement brief (quoted constraints in section 1).\n   - No new user messages in this segment. It resumed from the prior summary: « Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. »\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Write the French closing message. wrap_up was already called.\n   - The closing message must state these deviations:\n     - refusals b, c and the W-AG′ negative are « aucune issue ok », not reject;\n     - form (2′) was not needed;\n     - the W-GS positive suite is the twin, and steps 2–3 are a local verification;\n     - the kill-kinds list has no general theorem.\n   - It must end with one or two lines on what was not checked or is at risk (ponytail mode).\n   - Do not ask the wrap_up question again in the message.\n   - Do not offer a PR or push.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Everything is committed (last commit 1d53130). Memory is updated.\n   - `mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up` was called with:\n     - recap: « Le complément de la tranche 3 est terminé sur `formal/spec2-m4` : les tâches 1 à 6 sont prouvées ou vérifiées, et la section « Complément » du rapport est écrite. Un seul énoncé reste inachevé : la liste générale des genres qui font mourir des feuilles. Rien n'est poussé. »\n     - ask: « Je prouve ici le lemme général des genres qui font mourir des feuilles ? »\n     - buttons: « Oui, prouve-le » / « Non, on s'arrête ».\n   - The tool result said: « Your closing message is your answer to the user: write it now, in full … do not ask it again. »\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Write the final French closing message summarizing results:\n     - per task: proved theorems, the witnesses obtained, replays;\n     - the deviations listed above;\n     - the audit numbers;\n     - the report location;\n     - the last lines on what was not checked: the kill-kinds general lemma, and the L1 internals not re-read.\n   - Do not start the kill-kinds proof unless the user answers « Oui, prouve-le ».\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"4cd5a24c-1f6d-4374-9f92-1082860022c2","timestamp":"2026-11-13T00:51:19.699Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":27,"turnIndex":34},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["b722839c-e0f7-4fc2-8769-52bb652189d9"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
