{"parentUuid":"07f61e23-6b68-4d6a-91c4-0d0f3cfc56fe","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c6363317-3632-459e-8779-ebed992e8329","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, SubagentHandback, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, advisor, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Prior context.** Branch `formal/spec2-m4`, an exploratory ERN Spec 2 formalization in Lean that is never merged. The previous pass, « tranche 3 : encapsulation complète, complément », was completed. Its closing message was written at the start of this segment; it ended with the open kill-kinds lemma.\n\n   **Current request.** The user answered « Oui, prouve-le » via a pasted brief, then sent a refined pasted brief mid-turn. Its key content, verbatim:\n\n   - Scope: « Oui, prouve-le ici, sur `formal/spec2-m4`, dans les mêmes règles que le complément. »\n   - Statement: « Énoncé : le but écrit dans ton rapport (tâche 3, troisième ligne). Sur une `RunFull` depuis l'état initial, pour tout `i < |lbls|`, si `killKind lbls[i] = false`, alors `Usable (σ i) l → Usable (σ (i+1)) l`. Hypothèses : `DDSound`, `StaticsOK`, `σ 0` initial, `RunFull`, rien de plus. Donne aussi la forme par pas, sous les invariants atteints. »\n   - Method: « Prouve ou réfute. La propriété doit résulter de l'analyse des transitions `LStep` sur les états atteints par `RunFull`, pas d'une hypothèse qui déclarerait que seuls quatre genres tuent des feuilles. »\n   - Focus point: « Le point non prouvé est le changement de propriétaire par `transfer` et par les phases de `spawnVal` (§63, effet et précondition 9) : regarde le changement de propriétaire, les chaînes de propriété et l'effet de chaque phase. Le théorème porte sur `Usable`, pas sur l'état d'initialisation : une source laissée `Moved` n'est pas pour autant une place inutilisable. »\n   - Refutation format and restrictions: « Si une place peut devenir inutilisable : trace `RunFull` minimale, clause et état, sans correction. Ne modifie ni `Usable`, ni `killKind`, ni `KillOK`, ni aucune autre définition ou théorème existant. »\n   - Framing: « Ce résultat complète la caractérisation des effets des opérations. Ne le présente pas comme nécessaire aux propriétés déjà prouvées. »\n   - Report items for the « Complément » section:\n     - pass the third line of task 3 to « prouvé » or « réfuté », with the theorem (module:line) and its hypotheses; update the OB-C28 open list;\n     - identify the 13 replayed traces counted in the 46 of the sweep, distinguishing complete traces, prefixes and local verifications;\n     - give the exact path of the « fichier mémoire » updated at the end of the pass, plus the output of `git diff --stat main...HEAD -- specs AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md formal/DESIGN.md formal/Ern/MemoryModel` and of `git status --short` on the same paths, both expected empty;\n     - redo the axiom audit, with a count whose sum is exact.\n   - Closing: « Commit quand le module compile. Pas de push, pas de PR. »\n\n   **Standing constraints from the earlier briefs, still in force:**\n   - « Formalisation exploratoire, jamais mergée. Pas de push sur `main`, pas de PR. »\n   - « Ne modifie ni `specs/`, ni `AGENTS.md`, ni `CLAUDE.md`, ni `formal/DESIGN.md`, ni aucun fichier de `formal/Ern/MemoryModel/`. »\n   - « N'ajoute aucune hypothèse pour obtenir un énoncé. »\n   - Existing definitions are not modified; everything is added alongside.\n   - Lean rules:\n     - no sorry, admit, axiom, native_decide or noncomputable;\n     - axioms only {propext, Quot.sound};\n     - `lake build` with no new warning;\n     - the AGENTS.md grep is empty;\n     - docstrings in English citing WC5.2, Spec 1, corpus v14 or the brief.\n   - Conventional Commits **without Co-Authored-By**: the memory rule overrides the system reminder's attribution line.\n   - Do not offer create_pr in wrap_up.\n   - Ponytail mode: end replies with one or two lines on what was skipped or not checked, and any risk.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Toolchain.** Lean 4 v4.35.0, no Mathlib. Build with `~/.elan/bin/lake build` in `formal/` (now 135 jobs). Check one file with `lake env lean <file>`.\n   - **`S3.Usable`** (Spec 1 §40, Basic.lean:379). Inductive constructors:\n     - `.frame`: `P[q]? = some pl`, `dead q = false`, `owner = .frame f`, `f ∈ F`;\n     - `.place`: owner `.place o` and `Usable o`.\n   - **Flat state.** `SC.flat` has `F := s.frames`, the flatMap of the stacks of live contexts. `SC.view c` reorders F, so membership is equal (`SC.mem_view_F`).\n   - **Which effects touch Usable inputs:**\n     - `dead` changes only in endUse (§69) and free (§70);\n     - frames are removed only by exit (§73) and terminate (C7);\n     - owners change only in transfer (§63: places owned by part r go to `corr(r)` via `mvTo`) and in the spawnVal transfer phases;\n     - enter, alloc and spawn append places via `shapeP P hd ls = P ++ …`.\n   - **Transfer.** `transfer_usable_fwd` (Lemmas:1246) needs `WF3 s` and `(transferEff s src dst).Usable dst`, which is §63.9 `dstUsableAfter`. `WF3.places`: parts share owner and death marker.\n   - **spawnVal** is `yieldEff (transfersEff c (spawnCreate s c ls) vs) ps s.nF`:\n     - `ValTransfersPre` gives per-phase `dstUsable`;\n     - `FreshRootLocal` gives a frame-owned destination (`spawn_frameOwned`);\n     - transfers never change frame owners (`transfer_usable_frameOwned`);\n     - `KBase` carries WF3 per phase (`transfer_base`, `view_facts_base`);\n     - the C5.4 final check is not used.\n   - **Reached invariants.** `runFull_inv` (Capacity:168) gives `KInvCA` for `σ i`. `(h i hi).2 : LStep k L lbls[i] (σ i) (σ (i+1))`.\n   - **Sweep structure.** The 46 swept traces are the 33 of `sweep` (ComplementSweep:62) plus the 13 of `sweep_replay` (Replay:438).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/KillKinds.lean** (NEW, commit `a234683`)\n     - Imports `Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.ComplementSweep`.\n     - Namespace `Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap`. Opens include `SyncPreserveAux SyncInitAux TransferPreserveAux PreservationAux` and `Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Sweep (killKind KillOK)`.\n     - Theorems and line numbers:\n       - `flat_usable_fwd` :38\n       - `flat_usable_view` :51\n       - `enterC_usable_fwd` :56\n       - `spawn_usable_fwd` :71\n       - `transferC_usable_fwd` :86\n       - `opStepC_usable_fwd_base` :96\n       - `opStepC_usable_fwd` :156\n       - `transfers_usable_fwd` :176\n       - `spawnVal_usable_fwd` :193\n       - `usable_step` :210\n       - `usable_run` :247\n       - `killOK_run` :256\n     - Key code:\n     ```lean\n     theorem flat_usable_fwd {s s' : SC} (hP : ∀ q < s.P.length, s'.P[q]? = s.P[q]?)\n         (hd : ∀ q < s.P.length, s.dead q = false → s'.dead q = false)\n         (hF : ∀ f ∈ s.frames, f ∈ s'.frames) {q : Nat} (h : s.flat.Usable q) :\n         s'.flat.Usable q := by\n       induction h with\n       | @frame q f pl hpl hdq ho hf =>\n         have hq : q < s.P.length := lt_of_getElem? hpl\n         exact .frame (pl := pl) ((hP q hq).trans hpl) (hd q hq hdq) ho (hF f hf)\n       | @place q o pl hpl hdq ho _ ih =>\n         have hq : q < s.P.length := lt_of_getElem? hpl\n         exact .place (pl := pl) ((hP q hq).trans hpl) (hd q hq hdq) ho ih\n\n     theorem transferC_usable_fwd {t : SC} {c src dst : Nat} (hw : WF3 (t.view c))\n         (hd' : (transferEff (t.view c) src dst).Usable dst) {q : Nat} (h : t.flat.Usable q) :\n         (transferEffC t c src dst).flat.Usable q :=\n       (set_usable (s := t) (t := transferEff (t.view c) src dst)\n         fun _ => SC.mem_view_F (s := t) (c := c)).2 (transfer_usable_fwd hw hd' (flat_usable_view h))\n\n     theorem opStepC_usable_fwd ... (hk : KInvCA s) (h : opStepC k op c s (.ok s'))\n         (hkill : killKind (.kernel c op) = false) ... := by\n       cases op with\n       | transfer src dst =>\n         obtain ⟨-, h⟩ := h; obtain ⟨hpre, rfl⟩ := Guarded.ok_iff.1 h\n         exact transferC_usable_fwd (view_facts hk c).1 hpre.dstUsableAfter hq\n       | enter ps ls =>\n         obtain ⟨-, h⟩ := h; obtain ⟨hpre, rfl⟩ := Guarded.ok_iff.1 h\n         exact enterC_usable_fwd hk.1.1.1 hpre.callerLive hq\n       | _ =>\n         exact opStepC_usable_fwd_base h (fun _ _ e => by cases e) (fun _ _ e => by cases e) hkill hq\n\n     theorem transfers_usable_fwd {k : K} {fin : S3} {c : Nat} :\n         ∀ (t : SC) (vs : List (Nat × Nat)), ValTransfersPre k fin c t vs → KBase t →\n           (∀ v ∈ vs, FrameOwned t.P v.2) → ∀ (q : Nat), t.flat.Usable q →\n             (transfersEff c t vs).flat.Usable q\n       | _, [], _, _, _, _, h => h\n       | t, v :: vs, ⟨hpre, hrest⟩, hk, hown, q, h => by\n         have hd' := transfer_usable_frameOwned (src := v.1) (dst := v.2) hpre.dstUsable\n           (hown v (List.mem_cons_self ..))\n         have hk₁ := transfer_base hk hpre.srcUsable hpre.dstUsable hpre.depsValid hpre.sameShape\n           hpre.disjoint hd'\n         exact transfers_usable_fwd (transferEffC t c v.1 v.2) vs hrest hk₁\n           (fun w hw => transfer_frameOwned (hown w (List.mem_cons_of_mem _ hw))) q\n           (transferC_usable_fwd (view_facts_base hk c).1 hd' h)\n\n     theorem usable_step {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {st st' : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbl : Label}\n         (hk : KInvCA st.1) (hs : LStep k L lbl st st') (hkill : killKind lbl = false) {q : Nat}\n         (hq : st.1.flat.Usable q) : st'.1.flat.Usable q  -- cases on all 13 LStep constructors\n\n     theorem usable_run ... (hdd : DDSound k) (hstat : StaticsOK statics)\n         (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], [])) (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {i : Nat}\n         (hi : i < lbls.length) (hkill : killKind lbls[i] = false) {l : Nat}\n         (hu : (σ i).1.flat.Usable l) : (σ (i + 1)).1.flat.Usable l :=\n       usable_step (runFull_inv hdd hstat h0 h (Nat.le_of_lt hi)).1 (h i hi).2 hkill hu\n\n     theorem killOK_run ... : KillOK σ lbls := fun i hi _ _ hd => by\n       cases hb : killKind lbls[i] with\n       | true => rfl\n       | false => exact absurd (usable_run hdd hstat h0 h hi hb hd.2.1) hd.2.2\n     ```\n     - How the other `usable_step` cases are closed:\n       - spawn: `spawn_usable_fwd hk.1.1.1 hpre.creatorLive hq`;\n       - terminate: `simp [killKind] at hkill`;\n       - join: `cases h; exact hq`;\n       - deriveSync and acquire: `set_usable_iff rfl rfl`;\n       - newMutex, resetLock and newArena: the state is unchanged;\n       - unlock: `set_usable_iff (by unfold releaseEff; split <;> rfl) …`;\n       - spawnVal: `spawnVal_usable_fwd`;\n       - issue and reset: `opStepC_usable_fwd_base` applied twice, through `issueStepC_ok` and `resetStepC_ok`.\n\n   - **formal/Ern.lean**: `import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.KillKinds` added after ComplementSweep (commit `a234683`).\n\n   - **formal/reports/spec2-m4-encap.md** (commits `5a1bbed`, `6326fde`). Changes in the « Complément » section:\n     - Sources: a bullet for the kill-kinds lemma.\n       - Spec 1 read in full: §40, §63, §69–§75, and the part XIV intro.\n       - §60–§62, §64–§68 and §76–§78 were only searched for owner/owned/dead/usable.\n       - WC5.2 C4–C8 read in full; C2, C3, C13 and C15–C18 not re-read.\n     - Commits table: rows for `a234683` and « le commit qui suit `a234683` ».\n     - Line numbers are those of `a234683`; « Neuf modules ». `killKind` and `KillOK` are listed as unchanged.\n     - The « Genres qui tuent » row in Définitions now names `usable_run` (`KillKinds:247`) and `killOK_run` (`:256`).\n     - Task 3 table, third row: **prouvé**, with `usable_run` / `usable_step` / `killOK_run` and their hypotheses.\n     - New « Genres qui tuent, prouvé » paragraph:\n       - hypotheses; Usable read on the flat state, for all places;\n       - per-step form under KInvCA only;\n       - method in three groups: kept, appends, owner changes (transfer via §63.9; spawnVal via ValTransferPre.dstUsable plus C5 précondition additionnelle 2, with C5 phase 4 `SpawnValPre.dstUsableAfter` not used);\n       - the Moved remark;\n       - S4 contains a spawnVal transfer;\n       - « Aucune propriété prouvée plus haut n'en dépend ».\n     - « Pas attendus » bullet updated.\n     - OB-C28: the kill-kinds item moved to « Fermés »; open items renumbered 1–5.\n     - Task 6: new « Les 13 traces rejouées du balayage » table:\n       - 11 complete traces: s3f, s4, s9, mt, dt, tA, tB, km, ks, tb, sa;\n       - 2 corpus traces without the excluded step 1: wr, cg;\n       - other rows: the W-GS twin is among the 33; prefixes are S2 (rl0σ take 8), S10 (s10σ take 7) and traceMutex (tAσ take 3); local verifications are the excluded steps 1 and `W_GS_2_3_local`.\n     - Audit: 135 jobs; « neuf nouveaux modules »; new table, nature breakdown and sums (see section 5).\n     - New subsection « Fichiers protégés et fichier mémoire »:\n       - memory paths: `/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md` and its index `…/memory/MEMORY.md`, outside the repo, and not CLAUDE.md;\n       - main = `d0c2d87` (merge-base), HEAD = `a234683`;\n       - both git outputs empty, and still empty after the report commits.\n\n   - **Memory**: `ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md` and the `MEMORY.md` index line were updated to record that the kill-kinds lemma is proved (a234683, audit 2822/1878).\n\n   - **Scratchpad**: `AxKill.lean`, `Audit7.lean`, `names_kill.txt`, `build_final.txt`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `killKind` unknown identifier → it is in namespace `Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Sweep`; added `open Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Sweep (killKind KillOK)`.\n   - `if_neg` deprecation warning → replaced by `split` with `exact absurd ‹_› (Nat.not_le.2 hq)` and `exact hd`.\n   - « don't know how to synthesize implicit argument `dst` » in `transfer_usable_frameOwned` → added `(dst := v.2)`.\n   - `Classical.choice` in `opStepC_usable_fwd`, `usable_step`, `usable_run` and `killOK_run`, caused by `by_cases` on ∃ → replaced by `cases op with | transfer | enter | _`. All axioms are now within {propext, Quot.sound}.\n   - Advisor-flagged report overclaim (sources said the §72 effect was read when the grep had not shown it) → read §69–§75 in full and reworded. Ambiguous C5 citations made explicit.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Proved, not refuted.**\n     - `usable_run` has exactly the 4 admitted hypotheses.\n     - `usable_step` needs only `KInvCA`.\n     - `killOK_run` gives KillOK on every RunFull from init.\n     - No counterexample.\n   - **Audit.**\n     - Totals: 2796 + 26 = 2822 theorems; 1861 + 17 = 1878 non-internal; 0 outside {propext, Quot.sound}; `comm` shows 0 removed.\n     - The 26 are: 12 written; 5 `Sweep.killKind.eq_1..5` (non-internal); 2 `_sparseCasesOn_1/2.else_eq`, 5 private `killKind.match_1.eq_N` and 2 private `releaseEff.match_1.eq_N` (internal).\n     - Sums: 12 + 5 = 17; 2 + 5 + 2 = 9; 17 + 9 = 26. Modules: 130 (94) + 26 (17) = 156 (111).\n     - The 14 generated names are equation lemmas generated in `KillKinds`; `killKind` and `releaseEff` are not modified.\n   - **Checks.**\n     - Final `lake build`: 135 jobs, 0 warnings, 0 errors.\n     - AGENTS grep empty.\n     - `KillKinds.lean`: no line over 100 characters, no noncomputable.\n     - Protected-path git outputs empty at `a234683` and at `6326fde`. The working tree is clean.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - **The pasted brief, then its refined version sent mid-turn** (constraints quoted in section 1). The first version said, among other things:\n     - « Oui, prouve-le ici, sur `formal/spec2-m4`, dans les mêmes règles que le complément. »\n     - « N'ajoute aucune hypothèse, ne modifie aucune définition ni aucun théorème existant ; `k