{"parentUuid":"9d36296f-b49c-41b5-8cc0-b87033a8604f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c6363317-3632-459e-8779-ebed992e8329","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qs6HS1QUUAvMs4mWXYibBX","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# ERN — Concurrency Model Specification v0\n3:## Working Candidate 5.3 — Execution Contexts, Authority Transmission, and Concurrent Event Semantics **[WC5.3]**\n21:# I. Concurrent Execution Machine\n23:## C1. Execution Contexts\n33:## C2. Concurrent State and External Contracts\n53:## C3. Frame Ancestry — H1\n71:## C4. Context Creation — `spawn`\n96:## C5. Provisional By-Value Transmission at `spawn`\n124:## C6. Frame Exit and Reparenting\n141:## C7. Context Termination — `terminate`\n157:## C8. Reference Completion Operation — `join`\n169:## C9. Cross-Context Authorities and Dependencies\n185:## C10. External Contexts\n195:# II. Synchronized Authority Derivation\n197:## C11. Separation of Mechanisms\n209:## C12. Synchronization Registry\n230:## C13. Reference Construction — `newMutex`\n260:## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n282:## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\n303:## C16. Reference Acquisition — `acquire` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n329:## C17. Reference Unlock — `unlock` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n353:## C18. Abandoned Grants and Recovery **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n379:## C19. Synchronized Administration\n393:# III. Invariants and Correspondence\n395:## C20. Concurrent Frame and Authority Well-Formedness\n405:## C21. Synchronization Invariant — `SyncInv`\n433:## C22. Grant Discipline and Safe Abstraction Encapsulation **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C6 (item 4); WC5.1 (item 6); WC5.3 (item 1 clarification)]**\n502:## C23. Preservation of Ordinary and Concurrent Operations\n512:## C24. Sequential Conservativity\n526:## C25. Abstract-to-Concrete Realization Obligations\n538:# IV. Open Obligations\n575:# V. Adversarial Corpus — Corrected Seed Cases\n605:### Guarded-Chain and Transfer Witness