Loss Marker, L1 and L2 — Scoped Authority Proofs and Open Event Obligations **[WC5.1]**\n1073:## C46. HandoffOrdered — D-C10 **[WC5.1]**\n1089:# XI. Event Realization of Reference Protocols — Proposed Block D\n1091:## C47. Spawn, Completion, and Join Events\n1101:## C48. Reference Mutex: Acquire, Unlock, and Grant Events\n1115:## C49. LockOrder, Recovery, and Delegation\n1125:## C50. Realization, Visibility, and Physical Correspondence\n1135:# XII. Safe Executions and Data-Race Freedom — Proposed Block D\n1137:## C51. EncapsulatedTrace and SafeConcurrentTrace **[WC5.1]**\n1148:## C52. Candidate Data-Race-Freedom Theorem and Proof Partition **[WC5.1]**\n1167:## C53. Proof Boundary, Conservativity, and No Freeze\n1181:# Drafting choices\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cfe0b05e-72bb-4eb8-a5b2-c52683364da1","timestamp":"2026-11-14T07:52:23.736Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1:# ERN — Concurrency Model Specification v0\n3:## Working Candidate 5.3 — Execution Contexts, Authority Transmission, and Concurrent Event Semantics **[WC5.3]**\n21:# I. Concurrent Execution Machine\n23:## C1. Execution Contexts\n33:## C2. Concurrent State and External Contracts\n53:## C3. Frame Ancestry — H1\n71:## C4. Context Creation — `spawn`\n96:## C5. Provisional By-Value Transmission at `spawn`\n124:## C6. Frame Exit and Reparenting\n141:## C7. Context Termination — `terminate`\n157:## C8. Reference Completion Operation — `join`\n169:## C9. Cross-Context Authorities and Dependencies\n185:## C10. External Contexts\n195:# II. Synchronized Authority Derivation\n197:## C11. Separation of Mechanisms\n209:## C12. Synchronization Registry\n230:## C13. Reference Construction — `newMutex`\n260:## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n282:## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\n303:## C16. Reference Acquisition — `acquire` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n329:## C17. Reference Unlock — `unlock` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n353:## C