{"parentUuid":"e241f88e-633f-431e-98e1-8b965a162a10","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c6363317-3632-459e-8779-ebed992e8329","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YM2uXVpBpvoZapCEsqaDH8","type":"tool_result","content":"Ern/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean:49:structure WF3 (s : S3) : Prop where\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-50-  /-- §49.1: the stack is nonempty and duplicate-free, every frame below `nF`. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-51-  frames : s.F ≠ [] ∧ s.F.Nodup ∧ ∀ f ∈ s.F, f < s.nF\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-52-  /-- §49.2: parent links are valid and acyclic (the parent precedes the child); a part shares\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-53-  its parent's owner and death marker. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-54-  places : ∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (r : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.parent = some r →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-55-    ∃ pr : Place, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ r < q ∧ pr.owner = pl.owner ∧ s.dead r = s.dead q\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-56-  /-- §49.3: owner frames are below `nF`; owner places exist; the ownership chain of every usable\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-57-  place is finite and reaches a live frame. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-58-  owners : (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (f : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .frame f →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-59-      f < s.nF) ∧\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-60-    (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (o : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .place o →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-61-      o < s.P.length) ∧\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-62-    ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∃ f, FrameOf s q f ∧ f ∈ s.F\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-63-  /-- §49.4: footprints consist of leaves of existing places. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-64-  footprints : ∀ (a : Nat) (x : Authority), s.A[a]? = some x → ∀ l ∈ x.footprint,\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-65-    l < s.P.length ∧ isLeaf s.P l\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-66-  /-- §49.5: an existing origin precedes the authority, so origin chains are acyclic and end at a\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-67-  root authority. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-68-  origins : ∀ (b : Nat) (y : Authority) (a : Nat), s.A[b]? = some y → y.origin = some a → a < b\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-69-  /-- §49.6: `RootChain`. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-70-  rootChain : RootChain s\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-71-  /-- §49.7: `RootHeld`. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-72-  rootHeld : RootHeld s\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-73-  /-- §49.8: every active authority is held by a frame of the stack or by a usable place. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-74-  holders : ∀ (a : Nat) (y : Authority), s.A[a]? = some y → y.active = true →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-75-    HolderLive s y.holder\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-76-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-77-/-! ## `I1`–`I4`, `NoDangling`, `Inv3` (§50–§54, §57) -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-78-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-79-/-- `I1` (§50): two distinct active authorities unrelated by derivation covering a common leaf\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-80-both have own mode `Observe`. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-81-def I1 (s : S3) : Prop :=\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-82-  ∀ (a b : Nat) (x y : Authority) (p : Nat), a ≠ b → s.A[a]? = some x → s.A[b]? = some y →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-83-    x.active = true → y.active = true → p ∈ x.footprint → p ∈ y.footprint →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-84-    a ∉ s.ancs b → b ∉ s.ancs a → x.mode = .observe ∧ y.mode = .observe\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-85-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-86-/-- `I2` (§51): the origin of a derived authority exists; the derived mode does not exceed the\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-87-origin's, the derived footprint is within the origin's, and the origin of an active derived\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-88-authority is valid, that is, active. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-89-def I2 (s : S3) : Prop :=\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean:190:structure FramesC (s : SC) : Prop where\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-191-  /-- WC4 C3: the initial context, context 0, is live and its initial frame, the base frame of\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-192-  Spec 1 §39, has no parent. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-193-  initial : OptP (s.C[0]?) (fun x => x.life = .live ∧ x.parent = none) False\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-194-  /-- WC4 C3: every live context has a nonempty local stack. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-195-  nonempty : ∀ c, s.Live c → s.stk c ≠ []\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-196-  /-- WC4 C3: frame identities are globally unique; Spec 1 §49.1: duplicate-free. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-197-  nodup : s.frames.Nodup\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-198-  /-- Spec 1 §49.1: every frame has a valid identity (below `nF`). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-199-  bound : ∀ f ∈ s.frames, f < s.nF\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-200-  /-- WC4 C3: the initial frame of a non-initial live context has a parent (the frame that\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-201-  created the context, or its reparenting target, WC4 C6). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-202-  rooted : ∀ c, c ≠ 0 → s.Live c → s.ctxParent c ≠ none\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-203-  /-- Spec 1 §49.1 re-indexed, WC4 C3: the parent of a live frame is live; the parent precedes\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-204-  its child, which represents well-foundedness (Spec 1 §49, last paragraph). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-205-  parent : ∀ f ∈ s.frames, ∀ g, s.parC f = some g → g ∈ s.frames ∧ g < f\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-206-\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-207-/-- `ConcurrentWF` (WC4 C20): the frame structure of `FramesC` and `WF3` (Spec 1 §49.1–§49.8)\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-208-read with \"the stack\" as the globally live frames. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-209-def ConcurrentWF (s : SC) : Prop := FramesC s ∧ WF3 s.flat\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-210-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f3c37bfa-1311-4b0a-b0ad-18dfb6cea306","timestamp":"2026-11-14T07:56:03.223Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Ern/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean:49:structure WF3 (s : S3) : Prop where\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-50-  /-- §49.1: the stack is nonempty and duplicate-free, every frame below `nF`. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-51-  frames : s.F ≠ [] ∧ s.F.Nodup ∧ ∀ f ∈ s.F, f < s.nF\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-52-  /-- §49.2: parent links are valid and acyclic (the parent precedes the child); a part shares\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-53-  its parent's owner and death marker. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-54-  places : ∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (r : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.parent = some r →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-55-    ∃ pr : Place, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ r < q ∧ pr.owner = pl.owner ∧ s.dead r = s.dead q\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-56-  /-- §49.3: owner frames are below `nF`; owner places exist; the ownership chain of every usable\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-57-  place is finite and reaches a live frame. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-58-  owners : (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (f : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .frame f →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-59-      f < s.nF) ∧\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-60-    (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (o : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .place o →\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-61-      o < s.P.length) ∧\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-62-    ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∃ f, FrameOf s q f ∧ f ∈ s.F\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Invariants.lean-63-  /-- §49.4: footprints consist of leaves of existing places. -