{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","hash":"b60d5d037c0ea35936e3d2827f46b2f81a18f6115e08d2669822301e18760981","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I have enough context to design. Let me look at the transfer owner-change lemmas, since the \"never usable again\" statement needs the backward direction of `transfer_usable_fwd`."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015o7zXNw21CG1zRdLzekoye","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && grep -rn \"theorem transfer_usable_fwd\" Ern | head -2; f=$(grep -rln \"theorem transfer_usable_fwd\" Ern | head -1); n=$(grep -n \"theorem transfer_usable_fwd\" $f | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \"$((n-120)),$((n+40))p\" $f","description":"Read transfer_usable_fwd and surrounding lemmas"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
