ingLeaf (s : S3) (p l : Nat) : Prop :=\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-704-  l ∈ footprint s.P p ∨ (isLeaf s.P l ∧ s.Usable l ∧ ¬ (endUseS s p).Usable l)\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-705-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-706-/-- Decidability of `EndingLeaf` (§69). -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-707-instance (s : S3) (p l : Nat) : Decidable (EndingLeaf s p l) := by\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-708-  unfold EndingLeaf; infer_instance\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-709-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-710-/-- Root authority of the value at `p` (§69.3): an authority with no origin covering a leaf of\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-711-`p`. -/\n--\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean:812:def freeEff (s : S3) (p : Nat) : S3 := cleanup (freeS s p)\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-813-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-814-/-- Leaf of the released unit (§70.3, §70.4): a leaf of `p` or of storage that stops being\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-815-usable. -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-816-def FreedLeaf (s : S3) (p l : Nat) : Prop :=\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-817-  l ∈ footprint s.P p ∨ (isLeaf s.P l ∧ s.Usable l ∧ ¬ (freeS s p).Usable l)\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-818-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-819-/-- Decidability of `FreedLeaf` (§70). -/\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-820-instance (s : S3) (p l : Nat) : Decidable (FreedLeaf s p l) := by\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-821-  unfold FreedLeaf; infer_instance\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-822-\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-823-/-- Authority `j` does not block `free p` (§70.3): if it is an active derivative over the\nErn/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean-824-footprint being freed, it is held within `p` or its holder dies. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean:225:def exitEffC (s : SC) (c : Nat) : SC :=\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-226-  { s.set (exitEff (s.view c)) with\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-227-    C := reparent (s.C.modify c fun x => { x with stack := x.stack.tail })\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-228-      ((s.stk c).headD 0) ((s.stk c).tail.headD 0) }\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-229-\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-230-/-- Preconditions of `exitFrameC` executed by `c` (Spec 1 §73 re-indexed; WC4 C6, C6.1: O7.1\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-231-transposed, O7.2–O7.5 on the global state). The surviving frames are the other globally live\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-232-frames. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-233-structure ExitPreC (k : K) (s : SC) (c : Nat) : Prop where\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-234-  /-- Spec 1 §73.1 re-indexed (WC4 C6, first paragraph): the current frame of `c` is not the\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-235-  initial frame of its context and has a surviving caller in its stack. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-236-  hasCaller : (s.stk c).tail ≠ []\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-237-  /-- Spec 1 §73.2, §73.4, §73.5: every anchor of a place usable after the exit has a surviving\n--\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean:353:def termEffC (s : SC) (c : Nat) : SC :=\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-354-  { s.set (exitEff (s.view c)) with\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-355-    C := reparent (s.C.modify c fun x => { x with stack := [], life := .done })\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-356-      ((s.stk c).headD 0) ((s.ctxParent c).getD 0) }\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-357-\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-358-/-- Preconditions of `terminate` executed by `c` (WC4 C7: the O7 validity requirements applied to\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-359-the initial frame of a terminating non-initial context, after its nested call frames have\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-360-ended). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-361-structure TermPre (k : K) (s : SC) (c : Nat) : Prop where\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-362-  /-- WC4 C7: a non-initial context (WC4 C3: the base frame never exits). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-363-  nonInitial : c ≠ 0\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-364-  /-- WC4 C7: the nested call frames have ended; only the initial frame remains. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Frames.lean-365-  initialOnly : (s.stk c).length = 1","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8a33ebc6-b523-43cb-a3b5-401a8a80c1e2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f6e7d94-7e0b-4d1e-87a9-7a81ca202d38","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
