te` `ok` (WC5.1 C7),\n`c0 : join(c1)` `ok` (WC5.1 C8), then as W-TR: `transfer(M, M′)`, `acquire(e)`, `write3(T)`, all\n`ok`. -/\ntheorem W_TRJ_ok : TermStep KM p4 1 (.ok jq) ∧ JoinStep jq 0 1 (.ok jq) ∧\n    opStepC KM (.transfer 0 4) 0 jq (.ok uq) ∧ AcquireOk KM L0 uq regX 0 0 (uqa, [⟨3, some 6⟩]) ∧\n    opStepC KM (.write 6 [3]) 0 uqa (.ok uqw) :=\n  ⟨W_RLJ_ok.1, W_RLJ_ok.2.1, ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩,\n    ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩, ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩⟩\n\n/-- The labels of W-TR-J. -/\ndef trjLbls : List Label :=\n  pLbls ++ [.terminate 1, .join 0 1, .kernel 0 (.transfer 0 4), .acquire 0 0,\n    .kernel 0 (.write 6 [3])]\n\n/-- The named states of W-TR-J. -/\ndef trjσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []),\n    (x5, regG, []), (x6, regG, []), (x7, regX, []), (p4, regX, []), (jq, regX, []),\n    (jq, regX, []), (uq, regX, []), (uqa, [⟨3, some 6⟩], []), (uqw, [⟨3, some 6⟩], [])].getD i\n    (uqw, [⟨3, some 6⟩], [])\n\n/-- W-TR-J from the initial state is a `Run5R`. -/\ntheorem W_TRJ_run : trjσ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init mxst), [], []) ∧ Run5R KM L0 trjσ trjLbls := by\n  obtain ⟨ht, hj, htr, ha, hw⟩ := W_TRJ_ok\n  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(p4, regX, []), (jq, regX, []), (jq, regX, []), (uq, regX, []),\n      (uqa, [⟨3, some 6⟩], []), (uqw, [⟨3, some 6⟩], [])]\n      [.terminate 1, .join 0 1, .kernel 0 (.transfer 0 4), .acquire 0 0,\n        .kernel 0 (.write 6 [3])] :=\n    .cons ⟨⟨trivial, trivial, trivial⟩, trivial⟩ (.terminate ht) <|\n    .cons ⟨⟨trivial, trivial, trivial⟩, trivial⟩ (.join hj) <|\n    .cons ⟨⟨(by decide : TransferExcl L0 (jq, regX) 0), trivial, trivial⟩, by decide⟩\n      (.kernel htr) <|\n    .cons ⟨⟨trivial, trivial, trivial⟩, by decide⟩ (.acquire ha) <|\n    .cons ⟨⟨trivial, by decide, by decide⟩, trivial⟩ (.kernel hw) .nil\n  exact ⟨rfl, (prefix_steps h).run _⟩\n\n/-! ## The defect of the abstract mutex edge -/\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v9 §2 octies W-RL: the write of `T` by context 1 (step 6) and the write of\n`T` by context 0 (step 11) form an exclusive pair. -/\ntheorem W_RL_excl : ExclPair rlLbls 6 11 3 :=\n  ⟨by decide, by decide, 0, 1, .modify, .modify, by decide, ⟨rfl, by decide, rfl⟩,\n    ⟨rfl, by decide, rfl⟩, Or.inl rfl⟩\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v9 §2 octies W-RL, graph of §2 septies: the pair is ordered by the\nabstract mutex edge passing over the `resetLock` (step 9), write of context 1 →`po` `unlock(e)`\n(step 7) →`sw` `acquire(e)` of context 0 (step 10) →`po` write of context 0, and it satisfies\n`HandoffOrderedAt` (WC5.1 C46). This is the defect of the abstract edge, kept as a counterexample\n(WC5.1 C45, last paragraph). -/\ntheorem W_RL_defect : PO rlσ rlLbls (.step 6) (.step 7) ∧ SW rlLbls (.step 7) (.step 10) ∧\n    PO rlσ rlLbls (.step 10) (.step 11) ∧ HB rlσ rlLbls (.step 6) (.step 11) ∧\n    HandoffOrderedAt rlσ rlLbls 6 11 3 := by\n  decide\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v9 §2 octies W-TR: the write of `T` by context 1 (step 6) and the write of\n`T` by context 0 (step 11) form an exclusive pair. -/\ntheorem W_TR_excl : ExclPair trLbls 6 11 3 :=\n  ⟨by decide, by decide, 0, 1, .modify, .modify, by decide, ⟨rfl, by decide, rfl⟩,\n    ⟨rfl, by decide, rfl⟩, Or.inl rfl⟩\n\n/-- `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v9 §2 octies W-TR, graph of §2 septies: the pair is ordered by the abstract\nmutex edge although the controller moved from `lock` to `lock′` at step 9, and it satisfies\n`HandoffOrderedAt` (WC5.1 C46). Same defect, kept as a counterexample (WC5.1 C45, last\nparagraph). -/\ntheorem W_TR_defect : PO trσ trLbls (.step 6) (.step 7) ∧ SW trLbls (.step 7) (.step 10) ∧\n    PO trσ trLbls (.step 10) (.step 11) ∧ HB trσ trLbls (.step 6) (.step 11) ∧\n    HandoffOrderedAt trσ trLbls 6 11 3 := by\n  decide\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.MutexEdge","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dea1573a-4e57-4659-83f0-ed26e949f669","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8d3a6c67-054d-4471-b5dc-de71c0f38b4c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
