{"parentUuid":"4c312afd-6483-44fc-998f-124dd6e4a4be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2WjvVXoCSeEiV9MXVyW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5150,"cache_read_input_tokens":601481,"output_tokens":3315,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5150,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3315,"cache_read_input_tokens":601481,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5150},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":816,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"5b12c102-b0f8-4aae-afeb-6aa883c445eb","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch2Wjv9wBmjU3pS1Qs6QZ","requestRef":"47324e36-f115-4c51-aa4f-eec7a820e02b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"493b93b1-80b3-4d7e-97fe-52c241197b0d","timestamp":"2026-11-14T08:34:58.869Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"493b93b1-80b3-4d7e-97fe-52c241197b0d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2WjvVXoCSeEiV9MXVyW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VU74ffBMwm4t9FAXZtHqh6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nsrc=open('/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6/scratchpad/sweep_thms.lean').read()\n# rewrap table lines\nout=[]\nfor line in src.split('\\n'):\n    m=re.match(r'^(\\s+)\\[(.*)\\](.*)$',line)\n    if m and line.strip().startswith('[(') :\n        ind=m.group(1); entries=re.findall(r'\\([^()]*\\)',m.group(2)); tail=m.group(3)\n        cur=ind+'['\n        lines=[]\n        for k,e in enumerate(entries):\n            piece=e+(', ' if k<len(entries)-1 else '')\n            if len(cur)+len(piece.rstrip())>98:\n                lines.append(cur.rstrip())\n                cur=ind+' '+piece\n            else:\n                cur+=piece\n        cur=cur.rstrip()+']'+tail\n        lines.append(cur)\n        out.extend(lines)\n    elif line.strip()=='[]' or line.strip().startswith('[] '):\n        out.append(line)\n    else:\n        out.append(line)\nsrc='\\n'.join(out)\n# fix docstrings: rewrap first doc line\nsrc=src.replace(\"/-- Brief, task 5, sweep, \",\"/-- Brief, task 5, sweep, on \")\ndef wrapdoc(s):\n    res=[]\n    for blk in re.split(r'(/-- .*? -/)',s,flags=re.S):\n        if blk.startswith('/-- '):\n            words=blk[4:-3].split()\n            lines=[]; cur='/--'\n            for w in words:\n                if len(cur)+1+len(w)>100:\n                    lines.append(cur); cur=w\n                else:\n                    cur+=' '+w\n            cur+=' -/'\n            if len(cur)>100:\n                lines.append(cur[:-3].rstrip()); cur='-/'\n            lines.append(cur)\n            res.append('\\n'.join(lines))\n        else:\n            res.append(blk)\n    return ''.join(res)\nsrc=wrapdoc(src)\nheader='''import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtFrontier\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtWitness\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Protected\n\n/-!\n# Sweep of the extended handoff on the `RunFull` traces\n\nBrief of milestone 4, slice 4, task 5, \"Balayage\" (`formal/reports/spec2-m4-handoff-ext.md`). For\neach `RunFull` trace of the repository, the witnesses of this slice included, `SweepExt` lists\nthe extended exclusive pairs `(i, j, l)`, their frontier `r`, and whether strict `hb` holds from\n`r` to `j` (extended handoff order) and from `i` to `j` (no extended race). The list is complete\n(`sweepExt_complete`): every extended exclusive pair of the trace is in it. The facts of the\ncorpus (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v15 §2 quaterdecies) are the expected ones; for the other traces the\nlists are results of the model, decided by `decide`.\n-/\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.HandoffEvents Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.MutexEdge\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.ResetLockRight Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.ClassifyWitness\nopen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.NonRegression\nopen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.Witness (s11σ s11Lbls)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChainC (lcLbls)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.AbandonedGrant\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\nopen Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)\n\n/-- The sweep of a trace (brief, task 5): every extended exclusive pair with `i`, `j` steps of the\ntrace and `l` a place of its last state is in the list `T`; each entry `(i, j, l, r, a, b)` of `T`\nis an extended exclusive pair whose frontier is `r`, with strict `hb(r, j)` exactly when `a`\n(extended handoff order) and strict `hb(i, j)` exactly when `b` (no extended race). -/\ndef SweepExt (k : K) (L : MutexLayout) (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label)\n    (T : List (Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Bool × Bool)) : Prop :=\n  (∀ i ∈ List.range lbls.length, ∀ j ∈ List.range lbls.length,\n    ∀ l ∈ List.range (σ lbls.length).1.P.length,\n      ExtPair k L σ lbls i j l → (i, j, l) ∈ T.map fun e => (e.1, e.2.1, e.2.2.1)) ∧\n  ∀ e ∈ T, ExtPair k L σ lbls e.1 e.2.1 e.2.2.1 ∧\n    IsFrontier k σ lbls e.1 e.2.1 e.2.2.1 e.2.2.2.1 ∧\n    (HBS σ L lbls (.step e.2.2.2.1) (.step e.2.1) ↔ e.2.2.2.2.1 = true) ∧\n    (HBS σ L lbls (.step e.1) (.step e.2.1) ↔ e.2.2.2.2.2 = true)\n\n/-- Decidability of `SweepExt`. -/\ninstance (k : K) [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable] (L : MutexLayout)\n    (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label)\n    (T : List (Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Bool × Bool)) : Decidable (SweepExt k L σ lbls T) := by\n  unfold SweepExt; infer_instance\n\n/-- On a `RunFull` from the initial state, the list of `SweepExt` is complete: every extended\nexclusive pair is in it, its leaf being a place of the last state (`touch_lt_run`,\n`len_mono_run`). -/\ntheorem sweepExt_complete {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {statics : Statics}\n    {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbls : List Label} (hdd : DDSound k)\n    (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], []))\n    (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {T : List (Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Bool × Bool)}\n    (hs : SweepExt k L σ lbls T) {i j l : Nat} (hp : ExtPair k L σ lbls i j l) :\n    (i, j, l) ∈ T.map fun e => (e.1, e.2.1, e.2.2.1) := by\n  obtain ⟨hij, hj, -, -, htj, -⟩ := hp.out\n  have hl := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le (touch_lt_run hdd hstat h0 h hj htj)\n    (len_mono_run hdd hstat h0 h (Nat.succ_le_of_lt hj) (Nat.le_refl _))\n  exact hs.1 i (List.mem_range.2 (Nat.lt_trans hij hj)) j (List.mem_range.2 hj) l\n    (List.mem_range.2 hl) hp\n\n'''\nopen('Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSweep.lean','w').write(header+src+'\\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep\\n')\nEOF\nawk 'length > 100 {print FILENAME\": \"FNR\": \"length}' Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSweep.lean | head; sed -i '' 's/^import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtFrontier$/import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtFrontier\\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep/' Ern.lean; time ~/.elan/bin/lake build Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep 2>&1 | grep -v \"^✔\" | head -30","description":"Write the sweep module and build it","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5150,"cache_read_input_tokens":601481,"output_tokens":3315,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5150,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3315,"cache_read_input_tokens":601481,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5150},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":23227,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VU74ffBMwm4t9FAXZtHqh6":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nsrc=open('/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6/scratchpad/sweep_thms.lean').read()\n# rewrap table lines\nout=[]\nfor line in src.split('\\n'):\n    m=re.match(r'^(\\s+)\\[(.*)\\](.*)$',line)\n    if m and line.strip().startswith('[(') :\n        ind=m.group(1); entries=re.findall(r'\\([^()]*\\)',m.group(2)); tail=m.group(3)\n        cur=ind+'['\n        lines=[]\n        for k,e in enumerate(entries):\n            piece=e+(', ' if k<len(entries)-1 else '')\n            if len(cur)+len(piece.rstrip())>98:\n                lines.append(cur.rstrip())\n                cur=ind+' '+piece\n            else:\n                cur+=piece\n        cur=cur.rstrip()+']'+tail\n        lines.append(cur)\n        out.extend(lines)\n    elif line.strip()=='[]' or line.strip().startswith('[] '):\n        out.append(line)\n    else:\n        out.append(line)\nsrc='\\n'.join(out)\n# fix docstrings: rewrap first doc line\nsrc=src.replace(\"/-- Brief, task 5, sweep, \",\"/-- Brief, task 5, sweep, on \")\ndef wrapdoc(s):\n    res=[]\n    for blk in re.split(r'(/-- .*? -/)',s,flags=re.S):\n        if blk.startswith('/-- '):\n            words=blk[4:-3].split()\n            lines=[]; cur='/--'\n            for w in words:\n                if len(cur)+1+len(w)>100:\n                    lines.append(cur); cur=w\n                else:\n                    cur+=' '+w\n            cur+=' -/'\n            if len(cur)>100:\n                lines.append(cur[:-3].rstrip()); cur='-/'\n            lines.append(cur)\n            res.append('\\n'.join(lines))\n        else:\n            res.append(blk)\n    return ''.join(res)\nsrc=wrapdoc(src)\nheader='''import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtFrontier\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtWitness\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Protected\n\n/-!\n# Sweep of the extended handoff on the `RunFull` traces\n\nBrief of milestone 4, slice 4, task 5, \"Balayage\" (`formal/reports/spec2-m4-handoff-ext.md`). For\neach `RunFull` trace of the repository, the witnesses of this slice included, `SweepExt` lists\nthe extended exclusive pairs `(i, j, l)`, their frontier `r`, and whether strict `hb` holds from\n`r` to `j` (extended handoff order) and from `i` to `j` (no extended race). The list is complete\n(`sweepExt_complete`): every extended exclusive pair of the trace is in it. The facts of the\ncorpus (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v15 §2 quaterdecies) are the expected ones; for the other traces the\nlists are results of the model, decided by `decide`.\n-/\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.HandoffEvents Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.MutexEdge\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.ResetLockRight Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.ClassifyWitness\nopen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.NonRegression\nopen Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal.Witness (s11σ s11Lbls)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.GuardedChainC (lcLbls)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.AbandonedGrant\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\nopen Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)\n\n/-- The sweep of a trace (brief, task 5): every extended exclusive pair with `i`, `j` steps of the\ntrace and `l` a place of its last state is in the list `T`; each entry `(i, j, l, r, a, b)` of `T`\nis an extended exclusive pair whose frontier is `r`, with strict `hb(r, j)` exactly when `a`\n(extended handoff order) and strict `hb(i, j)` exactly when `b` (no extended race). -/\ndef SweepExt (k : K) (L : MutexLayout) (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label)\n    (T : List (Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Bool × Bool)) : Prop :=\n  (∀ i ∈ List.range lbls.length, ∀ j ∈ List.range lbls.length,\n    ∀ l ∈ List.range (σ lbls.length).1.P.length,\n      ExtPair k L σ lbls i j l → (i, j, l) ∈ T.map fun e => (e.1, e.2.1, e.2.2.1)) ∧\n  ∀ e ∈ T, ExtPair k L σ lbls e.1 e.2.1 e.2.2.1 ∧\n    IsFrontier k σ lbls e.1 e.2.1 e.2.2.1 e.2.2.2.1 ∧\n    (HBS σ L lbls (.step e.2.2.2.1) (.step e.2.1) ↔ e.2.2.2.2.1 = true) ∧\n    (HBS σ L lbls (.step e.1) (.step e.2.1) ↔ e.2.2.2.2.2 = true)\n\n/-- Decidability of `SweepExt`. -/\ninstance (k : K) [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable] (L : MutexLayout)\n    (σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg) (lbls : List Label)\n    (T : List (Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Bool × Bool)) : Decidable (SweepExt k L σ lbls T) := by\n  unfold SweepExt; infer_instance\n\n/-- On a `RunFull` from the initial state, the list of `SweepExt` is complete: every extended\nexclusive pair is in it, its leaf being a place of the last state (`touch_lt_run`,\n`len_mono_run`). -/\ntheorem sweepExt_complete {k : K} {L : MutexLayout} {statics : Statics}\n    {σ : Nat → SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg} {lbls : List Label} (hdd : DDSound k)\n    (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = (SC.ofS3 (S3.init statics), [], []))\n    (h : RunFull k L σ lbls) {T : List (Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Bool × Bool)}\n    (hs : SweepExt k L σ lbls T) {i j l : Nat} (hp : ExtPair k L σ lbls i j l) :\n    (i, j, l) ∈ T.map fun e => (e.1, e.2.1, e.2.2.1) := by\n  obtain ⟨hij, hj, -, -, htj, -⟩ := hp.out\n  have hl := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le (touch_lt_run hdd hstat h0 h hj htj)\n    (len_mono_run hdd hstat h0 h (Nat.succ_le_of_lt hj) (Nat.le_refl _))\n  exact hs.1 i (List.mem_range.2 (Nat.lt_trans hij hj)) j (List.mem_range.2 hj) l\n    (List.mem_range.2 hl) hp\n\n'''\nopen('Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSweep.lean','w').write(header+src+'\\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep\\n')\nEOF\nawk 'length > 100 {print FILENAME\": \"FNR\": \"length}' Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSweep.lean | head; sed -i '' 's/^import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtFrontier$/import Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtFrontier\\nimport Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep/' Ern.lean; time ~/.elan/bin/lake build Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSweep 2>&1 | grep -v \"^✔\" | head -30","description":"Write the sweep module and build it","timeout":1800000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01VU74ffBMwm4t9FAXZtHqh6":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5b12c102-b0f8-4aae-afeb-6aa883c445eb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch2Wjv9wBmjU3pS1Qs6QZ","requestRef":"47324e36-f115-4c51-aa4f-eec7a820e02b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"99a4ec3f-5358-4947-98a8-2e51923e2d56","timestamp":"2026-11-14T08:35:22.099Z","