{"parentUuid":"dc0500ae-c439-453b-85fb-500a4a9ecaf6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01QYvDpNovp2pywuTbAo52ak","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dc64375a-b74e-4ed0-92c9-d8ad047b50d9","timestamp":"2026-11-14T08:39:21.449Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"dc64375a-b74e-4ed0-92c9-d8ad047b50d9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2X32BKL6yA2Em3Zq4yf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012kTjCpW2s9zQRWXLW5Heox","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\ntail='end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\\n'\nassert s.endswith(tail)\ns=s[:-len(tail)]+tail.replace('end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\\n','')\nadd=r'''end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt Ern.Concurrency.Corpus\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Witness (instDecidableEncap5R)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\nopen Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)\n\n/-! ## Witnesses of `r = i` -/\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, couples where `r = i` occurs, on `RunFull` traces from the initial state:\n`(spawn, N)`: in the `terminate` witness of slice 3 (`CapacityWitness.tm`), the `spawn` of step 0\ncreates the locals of the child and the child stores into one of them at step 2; in S3\n(`MutexReal.NonRegression.s3`), the `spawn` of step 7 creates the local 8 of the child, which\n`issue`s into it at step 9. `(spawnVal, C)`: W-SV (`W_SV_graph`). The frontier is the creating\nstep; `hb(i, j)` holds by the creation edge. -/\ntheorem r_eq_i_witnesses :\n    ClassN L0 (CapacityWitness.tmσ 0) (CapacityWitness.tmσ 1) (.spawn 0 [] CapacityWitness.eLocals)\n      2 ∧\n    IsFrontier CapacityWitness.KE3 CapacityWitness.tmσ CapacityWitness.tmLbls 0 2 2 0 ∧\n    HBS CapacityWitness.tmσ L0 CapacityWitness.tmLbls (.step 0) (.step 2) ∧\n    ClassN L0 (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 7) (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 8)\n      (.spawn 0 [6] [(none, 0)]) 8 ∧\n    IsFrontier KA MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls 7 9 8 7 ∧\n    HBS MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ L0 MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls (.step 7) (.step 9) ∧\n    ClassC (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 4) (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 5) 4 ∧\n    IsFrontier K0 HandoffExtWitness.svσ HandoffExtWitness.svLbls 4 5 4 4 := by\n  decide\n\n/-- `(spawnVal, N)`: the by-value `spawn` of S4 with a second local of the child, which is no\ndestination (WC5.3 C5 phase 1: created `Uninit`). -/\ndef vn5 : SC := spawnValEff Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]\n/-- `c1 : write3(L)` via `root_L` (authority 5), `L` the second local of the child (O10). -/\ndef vn6 : SC := vn5.set (write3Eff (vn5.view 1) [5])\n\n/-- The labels of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/\ndef vnLbls : List Label :=\n  [.kernel 0 (.enter [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)]), .kernel 0 (.write 1 [1]),\n   .kernel 0 (.write 2 [2]), .kernel 0 (.alloc 2 1 [(none, 0)]),\n   .spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)], .kernel 1 (.write 5 [5])]\n\n/-- The named states of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/\ndef vnσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []), (Traces.q3, [], []),\n    (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])].getD i (vn6, [], [])\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, `(spawnVal, N)`: the trace is a `RunFull` from the initial state; the local `5`\nof the child is created `Uninit` by the by-value `spawn` (class N), the child writes it; the pair\n`(4, 5, 5)` is an extended exclusive pair whose frontier is the by-value `spawn` itself, ordered by\nthe creation edge. -/\ntheorem spawnVal_N_witness : RunFull K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls ∧\n    ClassN L0 (vnσ 4) (vnσ 5) (.spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]) 5 ∧\n    ExtPair K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 ∧ IsFrontier K0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 4 ∧\n    HBS vnσ L0 vnLbls (.step 4) (.step 5) := by\n  obtain ⟨e0, w1, w2, a3, -, -⟩ := Traces.s4_steps\n  have sv : SpawnValStep K0 Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)] (.ok vn5) :=\n    ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩\n  have s2 : opStepC K0 (.write 5 [5]) 1 vn5 (.ok vn6) := ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have h : Steps5R K0 L0 [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []),\n      (Traces.q3, [], []), (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])] vnLbls :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel e0) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel w1) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel w2) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel a3) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.spawnVal sv) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel s2) .nil\n  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide), by decide,\n    by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ## The suggested counterexample to `hb(i, j)` when `r = i` -/\n\n/-- From `MX₄`: `c0 : o2 := derive(root_M, Observe, {slot, lock})`, authority 5 (O1). -/\ndef hq5 : SC := x4.set (deriveEff (x4.view 0) 0 [1, 2] .observe)\n/-- `c0 : spawn c2` yielding `o2`, with a local `L` (place 7, root authority 6) in the initial\nframe 2 of `c2` (WC5.3 C4): the step `i` creating `l = L`. -/\ndef hq6 : SC := spawnEff hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)]\n/-- `c2 : z := derive(root_L, Modify, {L})`, authority 7 (O1). -/\ndef hq7 : SC := hq6.set (deriveEff (hq6.view 2) 6 [7] .modify)\n/-- `c2 : acquire(e)` (WC5.3 C16): grant 8, held by frame 2. -/\ndef hq8 : SC := deriveSyncEff hq7 2 3\n/-- The registry with the grant of `c2` recorded. -/\ndef hqReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 8⟩]\n\n/-- The labels of the suggested construction up to the acquisition by `c2`. -/\ndef hqLbls : List Label :=\n  [.kernel 0 (.derive 1 [3] .modify), .kernel 0 (.store 3 1), .newMutex 0 3,\n   .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [], .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe),\n   .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)], .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0]\n\n/-- The named states of the suggested construction. -/\ndef hqσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []),\n    (hq5, regX, []), (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])].getD i (hq8, hqReg, [])\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, \"Piste de contre-exemple\": the construction suggested by the brief, in which a\ncontext existing before step `i` would reach a leaf created by step `i` through an authority kept\nin data protected by a mutex, does not get past the kernel. From `MX₄`, `c0` spawns `c2` with a\nlocal `L` (step `i`), `c2` derives `z` over `L` and acquires the mutex: these steps form a\n`RunFull` from the initial state. Then `c2 : store(z, T)` is `reject`: the effective anchor of `z`\nis `root_L`, in the initial frame of `c2`, which is no ancestor of the frame of `T` (Spec 1 §65.4,\n`AnchorOrder`). -/\ntheorem hint_store_rejected : RunFull KM L0 hqσ hqLbls ∧\n    opStepC KM (.store 7 3) 2 hq8 .reject ∧ ¬ EffAnchorOKC hq8 7 ((hq8.view 2).pframe 3) := by\n  have d5 : opStepC KM (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe) 0 x4 (.ok hq5) :=\n    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have s6 : SpawnStep hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)] (.ok hq6) := ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩\n  have d7 : opStepC KM (.derive 6 [7] .modify) 2 hq6 (.ok hq7) :=\n    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have a8 : AcquireOk KM L0 hq7 regX 2 0 (hq8, hqReg) :=\n    ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩\n  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []), (hq5, regX, []),\n      (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])]\n      [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [],\n        .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)],\n        .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0] :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel mx_steps.2.2.2.2.1) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn mx_steps.2.2.2.2.2) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d5) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn s6) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d7) <| .cons (by decide) (.acquire a8) .nil\n  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R ((ClassifyWitness.mx3_steps h).run _) (by decide))\n    (by decide), ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide)⟩, by decide⟩\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame\n'''\ns=s+add\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean 2>&1 | head -40","description":"Add r = i witnesses and the hint attempt, compile","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4091,"cache_read_input_tokens":633077,"output_tokens":4520,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4091,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4520,"cache_read_input_tokens":633077,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4091},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":31707,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012kTjCpW2s9zQRWXLW5Heox":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\ntail='end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\\n'\nassert s.endswith(tail)\ns=s[:-len(tail)]+tail.replace('end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\\n','')\nadd=r'''end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt Ern.Concurrency.Corpus\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Witness (instDecidableEncap5R)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\nopen Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)\n\n/-! ## Witnesses of `r = i` -/\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, couples where `r = i` occurs, on `RunFull` traces from the initial state:\n`(spawn, N)`: in the `terminate` witness of slice 3 (`CapacityWitness.tm`), the `spawn` of step 0\ncreates the locals of the child and the child stores into one of them at step 2; in S3\n(`MutexReal.NonRegression.s3`), the `spawn` of step 7 creates the local 8 of the child, which\n`issue`s into it at step 9. `(spawnVal, C)`: W-SV (`W_SV_graph`). The frontier is the creating\nstep; `hb(i, j)` holds by the creation edge. -/\ntheorem r_eq_i_witnesses :\n    ClassN L0 (CapacityWitness.tmσ 0) (CapacityWitness.tmσ 1) (.spawn 0 [] CapacityWitness.eLocals)\n      2 ∧\n    IsFrontier CapacityWitness.KE3 CapacityWitness.tmσ CapacityWitness.tmLbls 0 2 2 0 ∧\n    HBS CapacityWitness.tmσ L0 CapacityWitness.tmLbls (.step 0) (.step 2) ∧\n    ClassN L0 (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 7) (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 8)\n      (.spawn 0 [6] [(none, 0)]) 8 ∧\n    IsFrontier KA MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls 7 9 8 7 ∧\n    HBS MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ L0 MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls (.step 7) (.step 9) ∧\n    ClassC (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 4) (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 5) 4 ∧\n    IsFrontier K0 HandoffExtWitness.svσ HandoffExtWitness.svLbls 4 5 4 4 := by\n  decide\n\n/-- `(spawnVal, N)`: the by-value `spawn` of S4 with a second local of the child, which is no\ndestination (WC5.3 C5 phase 1: created `Uninit`). -/\ndef vn5 : SC := spawnValEff Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]\n/-- `c1 : write3(L)` via `root_L` (authority 5), `L` the second local of the child (O10). -/\ndef vn6 : SC := vn5.set (write3Eff (vn5.view 1) [5])\n\n/-- The labels of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/\ndef vnLbls : List Label :=\n  [.kernel 0 (.enter [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)]), .kernel 0 (.write 1 [1]),\n   .kernel 0 (.write 2 [2]), .kernel 0 (.alloc 2 1 [(none, 0)]),\n   .spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)], .kernel 1 (.write 5 [5])]\n\n/-- The named states of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/\ndef vnσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []), (Traces.q3, [], []),\n    (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])].getD i (vn6, [], [])\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, `(spawnVal, N)`: the trace is a `RunFull` from the initial state; the local `5`\nof the child is created `Uninit` by the by-value `spawn` (class N), the child writes it; the pair\n`(4, 5, 5)` is an extended exclusive pair whose frontier is the by-value `spawn` itself, ordered by\nthe creation edge. -/\ntheorem spawnVal_N_witness : RunFull K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls ∧\n    ClassN L0 (vnσ 4) (vnσ 5) (.spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]) 5 ∧\n    ExtPair K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 ∧ IsFrontier K0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 4 ∧\n    HBS vnσ L0 vnLbls (.step 4) (.step 5) := by\n  obtain ⟨e0, w1, w2, a3, -, -⟩ := Traces.s4_steps\n  have sv : SpawnValStep K0 Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)] (.ok vn5) :=\n    ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩\n  have s2 : opStepC K0 (.write 5 [5]) 1 vn5 (.ok vn6) := ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have h : Steps5R K0 L0 [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []),\n      (Traces.q3, [], []), (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])] vnLbls :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel e0) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel w1) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel w2) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel a3) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.spawnVal sv) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel s2) .nil\n  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide), by decide,\n    by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ## The suggested counterexample to `hb(i, j)` when `r = i` -/\n\n/-- From `MX₄`: `c0 : o2 := derive(root_M, Observe, {slot, lock})`, authority 5 (O1). -/\ndef hq5 : SC := x4.set (deriveEff (x4.view 0) 0 [1, 2] .observe)\n/-- `c0 : spawn c2` yielding `o2`, with a local `L` (place 7, root authority 6) in the initial\nframe 2 of `c2` (WC5.3 C4): the step `i` creating `l = L`. -/\ndef hq6 : SC := spawnEff hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)]\n/-- `c2 : z := derive(root_L, Modify, {L})`, authority 7 (O1). -/\ndef hq7 : SC := hq6.set (deriveEff (hq6.view 2) 6 [7] .modify)\n/-- `c2 : acquire(e)` (WC5.3 C16): grant 8, held by frame 2. -/\ndef hq8 : SC := deriveSyncEff hq7 2 3\n/-- The registry with the grant of `c2` recorded. -/\ndef hqReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 8⟩]\n\n/-- The labels of the suggested construction up to the acquisition by `c2`. -/\ndef hqLbls : List Label :=\n  [.kernel 0 (.derive 1 [3] .modify), .kernel 0 (.store 3 1), .newMutex 0 3,\n   .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [], .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe),\n   .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)], .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0]\n\n/-- The named states of the suggested construction. -/\ndef hqσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []),\n    (hq5, regX, []), (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])].getD i (hq8, hqReg, [])\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, \"Piste de contre-exemple\": the construction suggested by the brief, in which a\ncontext existing before step `i` would reach a leaf created by step `i` through an authority kept\nin data protected by a mutex, does not get past the kernel. From `MX₄`, `c0` spawns `c2` with a\nlocal `L` (step `i`), `c2` derives `z` over `L` and acquires the mutex: these steps form a\n`RunFull` from the initial state. Then `c2 : store(z, T)` is `reject`: the effective anchor of `z`\nis `root_L`, in the initial frame of `c2`, which is no ancestor of the frame of `T` (Spec 1 §65.4,\n`AnchorOrder`). -/\ntheorem hint_store_rejected : RunFull KM L0 hqσ hqLbls ∧\n    opStepC KM (.store 7 3) 2 hq8 .reject ∧ ¬ EffAnchorOKC hq8 7 ((hq8.view 2).pframe 3) := by\n  have d5 : opStepC KM (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe) 0 x4 (.ok hq5) :=\n    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have s6 : SpawnStep hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)] (.ok hq6) := ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩\n  have d7 : opStepC KM (.derive 6 [7] .modify) 2 hq6 (.ok hq7) :=\n    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have a8 : AcquireOk KM L0 hq7 regX 2 0 (hq8, hqReg) :=\n    ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩\n  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []), (hq5, regX, []),\n      (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])]\n      [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [],\n        .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)],\n        .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0] :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel mx_steps.2.2.2.2.1) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn mx_steps.2.2.2.2.2) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d5) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn s6) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d7) <| .cons (by decide) (.acquire a8) .nil\n  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R ((ClassifyWitness.mx3_steps h).run _) (by decide))\n    (by decide), ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide)⟩, by decide⟩\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame\n'''\ns=s+add\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean 2>&1 | head -40","description":"Add r = i witnesses and the hint attempt, compile","timeout":900000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_012kTjCpW2s9zQRWXLW5Heox":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4d15ed2c-e159-464a-a0da-6b4c42b78c45","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch2X31xAaeHWsXCc3RkYA","requestRef":"84c87471-e4b4-49c7-82b7-cbc265977b2e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9a80c2f8-e571-409e-9a13-c2198536ad88","timestamp":"2026-11-14T08:39:21.448Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"9a80c2f8-e571-409e-9a13-c2198536ad88","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c6363317-3632-459e-8779-ebed992e8329","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012kTjCpW2s9zQRWXLW5Heox","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"87dab61e-2bdb-4311-9614-122de54a1b43","timestamp":"2026-11-14T08:39:22.627Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean","hunks":[{"oldStart":215,"oldLines":3,"newStart":215,"newLines":123,"lines":["   exact touchCompat_not_modify hfr"," "," end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt","+","+namespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame","+","+open Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal","+open Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt Ern.Concurrency.Corpus","+open Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Witness (instDecidableEncap5R)","+open Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)","+open Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)","+","+/-! ## Witnesses of `r = i` -/","+","+/-- Brief, task 4, couples where `r = i` occurs, on `RunFull` traces from the initial state:","+`(spawn, N)`: in the `terminate` witness of slice 3 (`CapacityWitness.tm`), the `spawn` of step 0","+creates the locals of the child and the child stores into one of them at step 2; in S3","+(`MutexReal.NonRegression.s3`), the `spawn` of step 7 creates the local 8 of the child, which","+`issue`s into it at step 9. `(spawnVal, C)`: W-SV (`W_SV_graph`). The frontier is the creating","+step; `hb(i, j)` holds by the creation edge. -/","+theorem r_eq_i_witnesses :","+    ClassN L0 (CapacityWitness.tmσ 0) (CapacityWitness.tmσ 1) (.spawn 0 [] CapacityWitness.eLocals)","+      2 ∧","+    IsFrontier CapacityWitness.KE3 CapacityWitness.tmσ CapacityWitness.tmLbls 0 2 2 0 ∧","+    HBS CapacityWitness.tmσ L0 CapacityWitness.tmLbls (.step 0) (.step 2) ∧","+    ClassN L0 (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 7) (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 8)","+      (.spawn 0 [6] [(none, 0)]) 8 ∧","+    IsFrontier KA MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls 7 9 8 7 ∧","+    HBS MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ L0 MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls (.step 7) (.step 9) ∧","+    ClassC (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 4) (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 5) 4 ∧","+    IsFrontier K0 HandoffExtWitness.svσ HandoffExtWitness.svLbls 4 5 4 4 := by","+  decide","+","+/-- `(spawnVal, N)`: the by-value `spawn` of S4 with a second local of the child, which is no","+destination (WC5.3 C5 phase 1: created `Uninit`). -/","+def vn5 : SC := spawnValEff Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]","+/-- `c1 : write3(L)` via `root_L` (authority 5), `L` the second local of the child (O10). -/","+def vn6 : SC := vn5.set (write3Eff (vn5.view 1) [5])","+","+/-- The labels of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/","+def vnLbls : List Label :=","+  [.kernel 0 (.enter [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)]), .kernel 0 (.write 1 [1]),","+   .kernel 0 (.write 2 [2]), .kernel 0 (.alloc 2 1 [(none, 0)]),","+   .spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)], .kernel 1 (.write 5 [5])]","+","+/-- The named states of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/","+def vnσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=","+  [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []), (Traces.q3, [], []),","+    (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])].getD i (vn6, [], [])","+","+/-- Brief, task 4, `(spawnVal, N)`: the trace is a `RunFull` from the initial state; the local `5`","+of the child is created `Uninit` by the by-value `spawn` (class N), the child writes it; the pair","+`(4, 5, 5)` is an extended exclusive pair whose frontier is the by-value `spawn` itself, ordered by","+the creation edge. -/","+theorem spawnVal_N_witness : RunFull K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls ∧","+    ClassN L0 (vnσ 4) (vnσ 5) (.spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]) 5 ∧","+    ExtPair K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 ∧ IsFrontier K0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 4 ∧","+    HBS vnσ L0 vnLbls (.step 4) (.step 5) := by","+  obtain ⟨e0, w1, w2, a3, -, -⟩ := Traces.s4_steps","+  have sv : SpawnValStep K0 Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)] (.ok vn5) :=","+    ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩","+  have s2 : opStepC K0 (.write 5 [5]) 1 vn5 (.ok vn6) := ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩","+  have h : Steps5R K0 L0 [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []),","+      (Traces.q3, [], []), (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])] vnLbls :=","+    .cons (by decide) (.kernel e0) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel w1) <|","+    .cons (by decide) (.kernel w2) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel a3) <|","+    .cons (by decide) (.spawnVal sv) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel s2) .nil","+  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide), by decide,","+    by decide, by decide, by decide⟩","+","+/-! ## The suggested counterexample to `hb(i, j)` when `r = i` -/","+","+/-- From `MX₄`: `c0 : o2 := derive(root_M, Observe, {slot, lock})`, authority 5 (O1). -/","+def hq5 : SC := x4.set (deriveEff (x4.view 0) 0 [1, 2] .observe)","+/-- `c0 : spawn c2` yielding `o2`, with a local `L` (place 7, root authority 6) in the initial","+frame 2 of `c2` (WC5.3 C4): the step `i` creating `l = L`. -/","+def hq6 : SC := spawnEff hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)]","+/-- `c2 : z := derive(root_L, Modify, {L})`, authority 7 (O1). -/","+def hq7 : SC := hq6.set (deriveEff (hq6.view 2) 6 [7] .modify)","+/-- `c2 : acquire(e)` (WC5.3 C16): grant 8, held by frame 2. -/","+def hq8 : SC := deriveSyncEff hq7 2 3","+/-- The registry with the grant of `c2` recorded. -/","+def hqReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 8⟩]","+","+/-- The labels of the suggested construction up to the acquisition by `c2`. -/","+def hqLbls : List Label :=","+  [.kernel 0 (.derive 1 [3] .modify), .kernel 0 (.store 3 1), .newMutex 0 3,","+   .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [], .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe),","+   .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)], .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0]","+","+/-- The named states of the suggested construction. -/","+def hqσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=","+  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []),","+    (hq5, regX, []), (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])].getD i (hq8, hqReg, [])","+","+/-- Brief, task 4, \"Piste de contre-exemple\": the construction suggested by the brief, in which a","+context existing before step `i` would reach a leaf created by step `i` through an authority kept","+in data protected by a mutex, does not get past the kernel. From `MX₄`, `c0` spawns `c2` with a","+local `L` (step `i`), `c2` derives `z` over `L` and acquires the mutex: these steps form a","+`RunFull` from the initial state. Then `c2 : store(z, T)` is `reject`: the effective anchor of `z`","+is `root_L`, in the initial frame of `c2`, which is no ancestor of the frame of `T` (Spec 1 §65.4,","+`AnchorOrder`). -/","+theorem hint_store_rejected : RunFull KM L0 hqσ hqLbls ∧","+    opStepC KM (.store 7 3) 2 hq8 .reject ∧ ¬ EffAnchorOKC hq8 7 ((hq8.view 2).pframe 3) := by","+  have d5 : opStepC KM (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe) 0 x4 (.ok hq5) :=","+    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩","+  have s6 : SpawnStep hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)] (.ok hq6) := ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩","+  have d7 : opStepC KM (.derive 6 [7] .modify) 2 hq6 (.ok hq7) :=","+    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩","+  have a8 : AcquireOk KM L0 hq7 regX 2 0 (hq8, hqReg) :=","+    ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩","+  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []), (hq5, regX, []),","+      (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])]","+      [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [],","+        .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)],","+        .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0] :=","+    .cons (by decide) (.kernel mx_steps.2.2.2.2.1) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn mx_steps.2.2.2.2.2) <|","+    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d5) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn s6) <|","+    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d7) <| .cons (by decide) (.acquire a8) .nil","+  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R ((ClassifyWitness.mx3_steps h).run _) (by decide))","+    (by decide), ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide)⟩, by decide⟩","+","+end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4d15ed2c-e159-464a-a0da-6b4c42b78c45","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9a80c2f8-e571-409e-9a13-c2198536ad88","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","hash":"12343dbf4f3ad6ea75ec2670d154bf923421c1f3bfb8d2a3f2bae2ccd0138e5c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012kTjCpW2s9zQRWXLW5Heox","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\ntail='end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\\n'\nassert s.endswith(tail)\ns=s[:-len(tail)]+tail.replace('end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\\n','')\nadd=r'''end Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access Ern.Concurrency Ern.Concurrency.MutexReal\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExt Ern.Concurrency.Corpus\nopen Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.Witness (instDecidableEncap5R)\nopen Ern.Concurrency.Traces (L0)\nopen Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Examples (K0)\n\n/-! ## Witnesses of `r = i` -/\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, couples where `r = i` occurs, on `RunFull` traces from the initial state:\n`(spawn, N)`: in the `terminate` witness of slice 3 (`CapacityWitness.tm`), the `spawn` of step 0\ncreates the locals of the child and the child stores into one of them at step 2; in S3\n(`MutexReal.NonRegression.s3`), the `spawn` of step 7 creates the local 8 of the child, which\n`issue`s into it at step 9. `(spawnVal, C)`: W-SV (`W_SV_graph`). The frontier is the creating\nstep; `hb(i, j)` holds by the creation edge. -/\ntheorem r_eq_i_witnesses :\n    ClassN L0 (CapacityWitness.tmσ 0) (CapacityWitness.tmσ 1) (.spawn 0 [] CapacityWitness.eLocals)\n      2 ∧\n    IsFrontier CapacityWitness.KE3 CapacityWitness.tmσ CapacityWitness.tmLbls 0 2 2 0 ∧\n    HBS CapacityWitness.tmσ L0 CapacityWitness.tmLbls (.step 0) (.step 2) ∧\n    ClassN L0 (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 7) (MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ 8)\n      (.spawn 0 [6] [(none, 0)]) 8 ∧\n    IsFrontier KA MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls 7 9 8 7 ∧\n    HBS MutexReal.NonRegression.s3σ L0 MutexReal.NonRegression.s3Lbls (.step 7) (.step 9) ∧\n    ClassC (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 4) (HandoffExtWitness.svσ 5) 4 ∧\n    IsFrontier K0 HandoffExtWitness.svσ HandoffExtWitness.svLbls 4 5 4 4 := by\n  decide\n\n/-- `(spawnVal, N)`: the by-value `spawn` of S4 with a second local of the child, which is no\ndestination (WC5.3 C5 phase 1: created `Uninit`). -/\ndef vn5 : SC := spawnValEff Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]\n/-- `c1 : write3(L)` via `root_L` (authority 5), `L` the second local of the child (O10). -/\ndef vn6 : SC := vn5.set (write3Eff (vn5.view 1) [5])\n\n/-- The labels of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/\ndef vnLbls : List Label :=\n  [.kernel 0 (.enter [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)]), .kernel 0 (.write 1 [1]),\n   .kernel 0 (.write 2 [2]), .kernel 0 (.alloc 2 1 [(none, 0)]),\n   .spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)], .kernel 1 (.write 5 [5])]\n\n/-- The named states of the `(spawnVal, N)` witness. -/\ndef vnσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []), (Traces.q3, [], []),\n    (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])].getD i (vn6, [], [])\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, `(spawnVal, N)`: the trace is a `RunFull` from the initial state; the local `5`\nof the child is created `Uninit` by the by-value `spawn` (class N), the child writes it; the pair\n`(4, 5, 5)` is an extended exclusive pair whose frontier is the by-value `spawn` itself, ordered by\nthe creation edge. -/\ntheorem spawnVal_N_witness : RunFull K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls ∧\n    ClassN L0 (vnσ 4) (vnσ 5) (.spawnVal 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)]) 5 ∧\n    ExtPair K0 L0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 ∧ IsFrontier K0 vnσ vnLbls 4 5 5 4 ∧\n    HBS vnσ L0 vnLbls (.step 4) (.step 5) := by\n  obtain ⟨e0, w1, w2, a3, -, -⟩ := Traces.s4_steps\n  have sv : SpawnValStep K0 Traces.q4 0 [] [(none, 0), (none, 0)] [(1, 4)] (.ok vn5) :=\n    ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩\n  have s2 : opStepC K0 (.write 5 [5]) 1 vn5 (.ok vn6) := ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have h : Steps5R K0 L0 [(Traces.q0, [], []), (Traces.q1, [], []), (Traces.q2, [], []),\n      (Traces.q3, [], []), (Traces.q4, [], []), (vn5, [], []), (vn6, [], [])] vnLbls :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel e0) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel w1) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel w2) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel a3) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.spawnVal sv) <| .cons (by decide) (.kernel s2) .nil\n  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R (h.run _) (by decide)) (by decide), by decide,\n    by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ## The suggested counterexample to `hb(i, j)` when `r = i` -/\n\n/-- From `MX₄`: `c0 : o2 := derive(root_M, Observe, {slot, lock})`, authority 5 (O1). -/\ndef hq5 : SC := x4.set (deriveEff (x4.view 0) 0 [1, 2] .observe)\n/-- `c0 : spawn c2` yielding `o2`, with a local `L` (place 7, root authority 6) in the initial\nframe 2 of `c2` (WC5.3 C4): the step `i` creating `l = L`. -/\ndef hq6 : SC := spawnEff hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)]\n/-- `c2 : z := derive(root_L, Modify, {L})`, authority 7 (O1). -/\ndef hq7 : SC := hq6.set (deriveEff (hq6.view 2) 6 [7] .modify)\n/-- `c2 : acquire(e)` (WC5.3 C16): grant 8, held by frame 2. -/\ndef hq8 : SC := deriveSyncEff hq7 2 3\n/-- The registry with the grant of `c2` recorded. -/\ndef hqReg : SyncReg := [⟨3, some 8⟩]\n\n/-- The labels of the suggested construction up to the acquisition by `c2`. -/\ndef hqLbls : List Label :=\n  [.kernel 0 (.derive 1 [3] .modify), .kernel 0 (.store 3 1), .newMutex 0 3,\n   .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [], .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe),\n   .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)], .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0]\n\n/-- The named states of the suggested construction. -/\ndef hqσ (i : Nat) : SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg :=\n  [(x0, [], []), (x1, [], []), (x2, [], []), (x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []),\n    (hq5, regX, []), (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])].getD i (hq8, hqReg, [])\n\n/-- Brief, task 4, \"Piste de contre-exemple\": the construction suggested by the brief, in which a\ncontext existing before step `i` would reach a leaf created by step `i` through an authority kept\nin data protected by a mutex, does not get past the kernel. From `MX₄`, `c0` spawns `c2` with a\nlocal `L` (step `i`), `c2` derives `z` over `L` and acquires the mutex: these steps form a\n`RunFull` from the initial state. Then `c2 : store(z, T)` is `reject`: the effective anchor of `z`\nis `root_L`, in the initial frame of `c2`, which is no ancestor of the frame of `T` (Spec 1 §65.4,\n`AnchorOrder`). -/\ntheorem hint_store_rejected : RunFull KM L0 hqσ hqLbls ∧\n    opStepC KM (.store 7 3) 2 hq8 .reject ∧ ¬ EffAnchorOKC hq8 7 ((hq8.view 2).pframe 3) := by\n  have d5 : opStepC KM (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe) 0 x4 (.ok hq5) :=\n    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have s6 : SpawnStep hq5 0 [5] [(none, 0)] (.ok hq6) := ⟨by decide, .ok (by decide)⟩\n  have d7 : opStepC KM (.derive 6 [7] .modify) 2 hq6 (.ok hq7) :=\n    ⟨by decide, _, .ok (by decide), rfl⟩\n  have a8 : AcquireOk KM L0 hq7 regX 2 0 (hq8, hqReg) :=\n    ⟨by decide, ⟨3, none⟩, rfl, by decide, by decide, rfl⟩\n  have h : Steps5R KM L0 [(x2, regX, []), (x3, regX, []), (x4, regX, []), (hq5, regX, []),\n      (hq6, regX, []), (hq7, regX, []), (hq8, hqReg, [])]\n      [.kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [4] [],\n        .kernel 0 (.derive 0 [1, 2] .observe), .spawn 0 [5] [(none, 0)],\n        .kernel 2 (.derive 6 [7] .modify), .acquire 2 0] :=\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel mx_steps.2.2.2.2.1) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn mx_steps.2.2.2.2.2) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d5) <| .cons (by decide) (.spawn s6) <|\n    .cons (by decide) (.kernel d7) <| .cons (by decide) (.acquire a8) .nil\n  exact ⟨runFull_of_run7 (run7_of_run5R ((ClassifyWitness.mx3_steps h).run _) (by decide))\n    (by decide), ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide)⟩, by decide⟩\n\nend Ern.Concurrency.FullEncap.HandoffExtSame\n'''\ns=s+add\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Concurrency/FullEncap/HandoffExtSame.lean 2>&1 | head -40","description":"Add r = i witnesses and the hint attempt, compile","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
