{"parentUuid":"48456c81-1724-44e7-846a-9f83bd651983","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"@AGENTS.md\n\n## Claude Code\n\nYou implement. The Review section applies to you only when asked.\nBefore coding, list the spec passages the task covers and read them in full."},{"path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nClaude Code implements. Codex reviews. Both follow this file.\n\n## Source of truth\n\n- `specs/` is normative and the only source of semantics. Before acting, read the spec text the task depends on. Never rely on memory, summaries, comments or earlier sessions.\n- Never restate spec content in code comments or agent files. Point to its location.\n- Spec beats code. If the spec is ambiguous, contradictory or silent on something the task needs: stop and report the exact passage with a concrete example of the problem. Never pick an interpretation yourself.\n- Representation choices (structure or inductive type, function or relation) are yours when they change no accepted program and no behavior. A choice that does is a semantic question: stop and report.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Do exactly the task. No unrequested features, generalization, refactoring or \"robustness\" additions. Put suggestions in the report.\n- Do not edit `specs/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` or `formal/DESIGN.md` unless the task says so.\n\n## Lean\n\n- The Lake project is in `formal/`. `formal/DESIGN.md` governs how to formalize, never what the semantics is. Propose design decisions it does not settle in your report; never take them silently.\n- Every definition or theorem that encodes a spec rule cites the rule's location in its docstring.\n- A definition says what its rule says. Never make a definition more permissive, add an unjustified hypothesis or narrow a theorem's domain to obtain a proof.\n- Never change a theorem statement, or a definition it depends on, to make a proof go through. If stuck, stop and report the goal state.\n- Never use `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` or `native_decide`.\n- Every `.lean` file under `formal/` is part of the build target.\n- Done means:\n  - `lake build` (in `formal/`) succeeds;\n  - this prints nothing: `grep -rnE '\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\b|^\\s*axiom\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake .`\n  - for each theorem completed by the task, `#print axioms` lists nothing beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.\n\n## Report\n\nSpec passages implemented (by location), what changed, what is unproven or open, spec problems found.\n\n## Review (Codex)\n\nAdversarial and read-only. For each change, check:\n\n- It says exactly what the spec says: not stronger, not weaker. Read definitions, hypotheses and quantifiers, not only proofs. A theorem that holds because a definition is too permissive or its hypotheses are unsatisfiable is blocking.\n- Each formalized rule cites its spec location.\n- No theorem statement or dependency was changed without the task allowing it.\n- No interpretation was chosen silently where the spec is unclear.\n- Nothing outside the task was added.\n\nWhen a milestone is declared complete, compare the rules in its announced scope with the spec locations cited in `formal/`, and list every rule left without a definition or theorem.\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a spec quote, a counterexample or command output. No evidence, no finding. Never ask for additions beyond the task.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity, location, cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence."},{"path":"/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem","content":"- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23/J3/derivability, Spec 2 m1–m3 (WC2–WC4), m4 handoff (WC5, corpus v4–v6, ChainExcl, PlaceExcl), m4 event pass (WC5.1, corpus v8, po/sw/hb), m4 herd7/RC11 litmus pass, m4 strict mutex edge (corpus v9), m4 layer E event fragment (WC5.1 corrigé), m4 layer R mutex realization (corpus v10, 3 controller counterexamples) corrective pass (Run6, proposed C22.4/C18 amendments, W-NC) final pass (Run7, TouchesF, proposed C13.11) and slice 3 complete encapsulation (FullEncap, RunFull, task 5 refuted) and its complement (corpus v14, three cases proved, closure, dying leaves via L1, kill-kinds lemma proved) and slice 4 extended handoff (HandoffExt*, OBC28Check, r = i ⇒ hb refuted by unlock), reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule\n- [No Co-Authored-By trailer](feedback-no-coauthored-by.md) — never add the Claude co-author line to commits; main rewritten 2026-11-05"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a97f8c1a-d32b-46f2-a85a-f749634289c5","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:22:11.001Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/CLAUDE.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n@AGENTS.md\n\n## Claude Code\n\nYou implement. The Review section applies to you only when asked.\nBefore coding, list the spec passages the task covers and read them in full.\n\nContents of /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# AGENTS.md\n\nClaude Code implements. Codex reviews. Both follow this file.\n\n## Source of truth\n\n- `specs/` is normative and the only source of semantics. Before acting, read the spec text the task depends on. Never rely on memory, summaries, comments or earlier sessions.\n- Never restate spec content in code comments or agent files. Point to its location.\n- Spec beats code. If the spec is ambiguous, contradictory or silent on something the task needs: stop and report the exact passage with a concrete example of the problem. Never pick an interpretation yourself.\n- Representation choices (structure or inductive type, function or relation) are yours when they change no accepted program and no behavior. A choice that does is a semantic question: stop and report.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Do exactly the task. No unrequested features, generalization, refactoring or \"robustness\" additions. Put suggestions in the report.\n- Do not edit `specs/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` or `formal/DESIGN.md` unless the task says so.\n\n## Lean\n\n- The Lake project is in `formal/`. `formal/DESIGN.md` governs how to formalize, never what the semantics is. Propose design decisions it does not settle in your report; never take them silently.\n- Every definition or theorem that encodes a spec rule cites the rule's location in its docstring.\n- A definition says what its rule says. Never make a definition more permissive, add an unjustified hypothesis or narrow a theorem's domain to obtain a proof.\n- Never change a theorem statement, or a definition it depends on, to make a proof go through. If stuck, stop and report the goal state.\n- Never use `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` or `native_decide`.\n- Every `.lean` file under `formal/` is part of the build target.\n- Done means:\n  - `lake build` (in `formal/`) succeeds;\n  - this prints nothing: `grep -rnE '\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\b|^\\s*axiom\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake .`\n  - for each theorem completed by the task, `#print axioms` lists nothing beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.\n\n## Report\n\nSpec passages implemented (by location), what changed, what is unproven or open, spec problems found.\n\n## Review (Codex)\n\nAdversarial and read-only. For each change, check:\n\n- It says exactly what the spec says: not stronger, not weaker. Read definitions, hypotheses and quantifiers, not only proofs. A theorem that holds because a definition is too permissive or its hypotheses are unsatisfiable is blocking.\n- Each formalized rule cites its spec location.\n- No theorem statement or dependency was changed without the task allowing it.\n- No interpretation was chosen silently where the spec is unclear.\n- Nothing outside the task was added.\n\nWhen a milestone is declared complete, compare the rules in its announced scope with the spec locations cited in `formal/`, and list every rule left without a definition or theorem.\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a spec quote, a counterexample or command output. No evidence, no finding. Never ask for additions beyond the task.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity, location, cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence.\n\nContents of /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23/J3/derivability, Spec 2 m1–m3 (WC2–WC4), m4 handoff (WC5, corpus v4–v6, ChainExcl, PlaceExcl), m4 event pass (WC5.1, corpus v8, po/sw/hb), m4 herd7/RC11 litmus pass, m4 strict mutex edge (corpus v9), m4 layer E event fragment (WC5.1 corrigé), m4 layer R mutex realization (corpus v10, 3 controller counterexamples) corrective pass (Run6, proposed C22.4/C18 amendments, W-NC) final pass (Run7, TouchesF, proposed C13.11) and slice 3 complete encapsulation (FullEncap, RunFull, task 5 refuted) and its complement (corpus v14, three cases proved, closure, dying leaves via L1, kill-kinds lemma proved) and slice 4 extended handoff (HandoffExt*, OBC28Check, r = i ⇒ hb refuted by unlock), reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule\n- [No Co-Authored-By trailer](feedback-no-coauthored-by.md) — never add the Claude co-author line to commits; main rewritten 2026-11-05\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","ent