{"parentUuid":"1280080a-f0b0-4503-8a6b-c1450d782809","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2p5Yi8UTT5uF4w2FUMy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KFZ6ukms3huLaans1hK3BC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/Downloads && grep -n -E '^#+ |^\\*\\*C17|C17' ERN_WC5_3_FINAL.md | head -80","description":"Locate C17 and headings in WC5.3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1926,"cache_read_input_tokens":87759,"output_tokens":134,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1926,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":134,"cache_read_input_tokens":87759,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1926},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":978,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KFZ6ukms3huLaans1hK3BC":{"command":"cd ~/Downloads && grep -n -E '^#+ |^\\*\\*C17|C17' ERN_WC5_3_FINAL.md | head -80","description":"Locate C17 and headings in WC5.3"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9de3db35-65e3-4df5-93f4-4ae20be600d9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch2p5YR2D34Wk9fytGAxQ","requestRef":"53a49783-16dc-4784-b415-3b330d38ae20","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"5025c527-c7b6-451e-a0ab-998a25d7b473","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:22:20.122Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"5025c527-c7b6-451e-a0ab-998a25d7b473","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0dd0571a-6379-45f8-954f-cbdecd0ea155","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KFZ6ukms3huLaans1hK3BC","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# ERN — Concurrency Model Specification v0\n3:## Working Candidate 5.3 — Execution Contexts, Authority Transmission, and Concurrent Event Semantics **[WC5.3]**\n21:# I. Concurrent Execution Machine\n23:## C1. Execution Contexts\n33:## C2. Concurrent State and External Contracts\n53:## C3. Frame Ancestry — H1\n71:## C4. Context Creation — `spawn`\n96:## C5. Provisional By-Value Transmission at `spawn`\n124:## C6. Frame Exit and Reparenting\n141:## C7. Context Termination — `terminate`\n157:## C8. Reference Completion Operation — `join`\n169:## C9. Cross-Context Authorities and Dependencies\n185:## C10. External Contexts\n195:# II. Synchronized Authority Derivation\n197:## C11. Separation of Mechanisms\n209:## C12. Synchronization Registry\n230:## C13. Reference Construction — `newMutex`\n260:## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n282:## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\n303:## C16. Reference Acquisition — `acquire` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n329:## C17. Reference Unlock — `unlock` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n345:This candidate defines no waiting outcome for `unlock` on a failed C17 precondition. A physical implementation may impose its own internal progress protocol, but it may not report an invalid request as a successful abstract unlock.\n353:## C18. Abandoned Grants and Recovery **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n379:## C19. Synchronized Administration\n393:# III. Invariants and Correspondence\n395:## C20. Concurrent Frame and Authority Well-Formedness\n405:## C21. Synchronization Invariant — `SyncInv`\n433:## C22. Grant Discipline and Safe Abstraction Encapsulation **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C6 (item 4); WC5.1 (item 6); WC5.3 (item 1 clarification)]**\n502:## C23. Preservation of Ordinary and Concurrent Operations\n512:## C24. Sequential Conservativity\n526:## C25. Abstract-to-Concrete Realization Obligations\n538:# IV. Open Obligations\n558:| `OB-C17` | **[WC5.1 — M4] L1, scoped exploratory proof:** `cap5_drop_own` covers all 28 modeled step kinds under `DDSound` and reachable encapsulated authority traces. `lossStep_own` further establishes for eligible direct-access conflicting pairs a first own-context loss step `r` strictly between the two accesses; with one event per abstract step, `po(e1,r)` follows. Internal composite-step ordering and physical access coverage remain open (`OB-C19`, `OB-C20`). Raw `cap` still fails L1 (W-GR). |\n575:# V. Adversarial Corpus — Corrected Seed Cases\n605:### Guarded-Chain and Transfer Witnesses — Corpus §§ 2 ter–2 sexies and S10b **[WC5.1]**\n616:### Handoff Witnesses — Corpus §§ 2 bis and 2 septies (authority and abstract-event verdicts proved) **[WC5.1 — M4]**\n641:### Finite Event-Model Witnesses — G1–G19 **[WC5.2 — M4]**\n661:### Controller Realization and Encapsulation Witnesses **[WC5.2 — M4]**\n676:### Full Encapsulation and Abandoned-Grant Witnesses — Corpus v14 **[WC5.3 — M4]**\n698:# VI. Exploratory Verification Requirements\n702:## Milestone 1 — Abstract Model\n717:## Milestone 2 — Refinement\n723:## Milestone 3 — Adversarial Validation\n731:## Milestone 4 — Event Model, Handoff, and Data-Race-Freedom Validation\n771:# VII. Concurrent Event Model — Proposed Block C\n775:## C26. Executions, Abstract Steps, and Event Graphs\n791:## C27. Event Attributes and Realization Origin\n805:## C28. Program Order, Lifecycle Markers, and Within-Step Order\n826:## C29. Pure-Authority Erasure and Concrete-Access Coverage\n838:# VIII. Conflicts, Ordering, and Consistency — Proposed Block C\n840:## C30. Byte-Level Conflicts and Access Pairs\n848:## C31. Reads-From and Modification Order\n859:## C32. Synchronizes-With — `sw`\n871:## C33. Happens-Before and Data Races\n892:## C34. Admissible Event Graphs and Reference Memory Models\n921:# IX. Shared-Mutation Disciplines and Atomics — Proposed Block D\n923:## C35. Companion Shared-Mutation Contract — `SharedDiscipline`\n939:## C36. Classification of Inherited Accesses — D-C2\n951:## C37. Concurrent Atomic Read — `readShared`\n968:## C38. Atomic Units, Concrete Layouts, and Multi-Leaf Writes — D-C5\n978:## C39. Atomic Shared Writes and RMWs\n986:## C40. Memory Orders and Operation Legality — D-C7\n1008:## C41. Atomic Protocol Obligations and Failure Paths\n1014:The reference `unlock` and `resetLock` must prove their own controller-update correspondence. Their logical atomicity in C17/C18 does **not** establish physical release semantics. Failure to discharge a realization obligation means the corresponding protocol is not yet justified as safe, not that an additional unchecked primitive is implicitly available.\n1016:## C42. Exclusive Ordinary Access to Atomic Storage — D-C9\n1026:# X. Inter-Context Authority Handoff — Proposed Block D\n1028:## C43. Context Capability and Current-Frame Exercise **[WC5.1]**\n1042:## C44. Scope of Exclusive Handoff Ordering\n1057:## C45. Loss Marker, L1 and L2 — Scoped Authority Proofs and Open Event Obligations **[WC5.1]**\n1073:## C46. HandoffOrdered — D-C10 **[WC5.1]**\n1089:# XI. Event Realization of Reference Protocols — Proposed Block D\n1091:## C47. Spawn, Completion, and Join Events\n1101:## C48. Reference Mutex: Acquire, Unlock, and Grant Events\n1115:## C49. LockOrder, Recovery, and Delegation\n1125:## C50. Realization, Visibility, and Physical Correspondence\n1135:# XII. Safe Executions and Data-Race Freedom — Proposed Block D\n1137:## C51. EncapsulatedTrace and SafeConcurrentTrace **[WC5.1]**\n1148:## C52. Candidate Data-Race-Freedom Theorem and Proof Partition **[WC5.1]**\n1167:## C53. Proof Boundary, Conservativity, and No Freeze\n1181:# Drafting choices\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ca95d5f7-4087-4c56-a518-15f8566467b0","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:22:20.838Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1:# ERN — Concurrency Model Specification v0\n3:## Working Candidate 5.3 — Execution Contexts, Authority Transmission, and Concurrent Event Semantics **[WC5.3]**\n21:# I. Concurrent Execution Machine\n23:## C1. Execution Contexts\n33:## C2. Concurrent State and External Contracts\n53:## C3. Frame Ancestry — H1\n71:## C4. Context Creation — `spawn`\n96:## C5. Provisional By-Value Transmission at `spawn`\n124:## C6. Frame Exit and Reparenting\n141:## C7. Context Termination — `terminate`\n157:## C8. Reference Completion Operation — `join`\n169:## C9. Cross-Context Authorities and Dependencies\n185:## C10. External Contexts\n195:# II. Synchronized Authority Derivation\n197:## C11. Separation of Mechanisms\n209:## C12. Synchronization Registry\n230:## C13. Reference Construction — `newMutex`\n260:## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n282:## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\n303:## C16. Reference Acquisition — `acquire` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n329:## C17. Reference Unlock — `unlock` **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n345:This candidate defines no waiting outcome for `unlock` on a failed C17 precondition. A physical implementation may impose its own internal progress protocol, but it may not report an invalid request as a successful abstract unlock.\n353:## C18. Abandoned Grants and Recovery **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C1]**\n379:## C19. Synchronized Administration\n393:# III. Invariants and Correspondence\n395:## C20. Concurrent Frame and Authority Well-Formedness\n405:## C21. Synchronization Invariant — `SyncInv`\n433:## C22. Grant Discipline and Safe Abstraction Encapsulation **[WC5 MODIFIED — D-C6 (item 4); WC5.1 (item 6); WC5.3 (item 1 clarification)]**\n502:## C23. Preservation of Ordinary and Concurrent Operations\n512:## C24. Sequential Conservativity\n526:## C25. Abstract-to-Concrete Realization Obligations\n538:# IV. Open Obligations\n558:| `OB-C17` | **[WC5.1 — M4] L1, scoped exploratory proof:** `cap5_drop_own` covers all 28 modeled step kinds under `DDSound` and reachable encapsulated authority traces. `lossStep_own` further establishes for eligible direct-access conflicting pairs a first own-context loss step `r` strictly between the two accesses; with one event per abstract step, `po(e1,r)` follows. Internal composite-step ordering and physical access coverage remain open (`OB-C19`, `OB-C20`). Raw `cap` still fails L1 (W-GR). |\n575:# V. Adversarial Corpus — Corrected Seed Cases\n605:### Guarded-Chain and Transfer Witnesses — Corpus §§ 2 ter–2 sexies and S10b **[WC5.1]**\n616:### Handoff Witnesses — Corpus §§ 2 bis and 2 septies (authority and abstract-event verdicts proved) **[WC5.1 — M4]**\n641:### Finite Event-Model Witnesses — G1–G19 **[WC5.2 — M4]**\n661:### Controller Realization and Encapsulation Witnesses **[WC5.2 — M4]**\n676:### Full Encapsulation and Abandoned-Grant Witnesses — Corpus v14 **[WC5.3 — M4]**\n698:# VI. Exploratory Verification Requirements\n702:## Milestone 1 — Abstract Model\n717:## Milestone 2 — Refinement\n723:## Milestone 3 — Adversarial Validation\n731:## Milestone 4 — Event Model, Handoff, and Data-Race-Freedom Validation\n771:# VII. Concurrent Event Model — Proposed Block C\n775:## C26. Executions, Abstract Steps, and Event Graphs\n791:## C27. Event Attributes and Realization Origin\n805:## C28. Program Order, Lifecycle Markers, and Within-Step Order\n826:## C29. Pure-Authority Erasure and Concrete-Access Coverage\n838:# VIII. Conflicts, Ordering, and Consistency — Proposed Block C\n840:## C30. Byte-Level Conflicts and Access Pairs\n848:## C31. Reads-From and Modification Order\n859:## C32. Synchronizes-With — `sw`\n871:## C33. Happens-Before and Data Races\n892:## C34. Admissible Event Graphs and Reference Memory Models\n921:# IX. Shared-Mutation Disciplines and Atomics — Proposed Block D\n923:## C35. Companion Shared-Mutation Contract — `SharedDiscipline`\n939:## C36. Classification of Inherited Accesses — D-C2\n951:## C37. Concurrent Atomic Read — `readShared`\n968:## C38. Atomic Units, Concrete Layouts, and Multi-Leaf Writes — D-C5\n978:## C39. Atomic Shared Writes and RMWs\n986:## C40. Memory Orders and Operation Legality — D-C7\n1008:## C41. Atomic Protocol Obligations and Failure Paths\n1014:The reference `unlock` and `resetLock` must prove their own controller-update correspondence. Their logical atomicity in C17/C18 does **not** establish physical release semantics. Failure to discharge a realization obligation means the corresponding protocol is not yet justified as safe, not that an additional unchecked primitive is implicitly available.\n1016:## C42. Exclusive Ordinary Access to Atomic Storage — D-C9\n1026:# X. Inter-Context Authority Handoff — Proposed Block D\n1028:## C43. Context Capability and Current-Frame Exercise **[WC5.1]**\n1042:## C44. Scope of Exclusive Handoff Ordering\n1057:## C45. Loss Marker, L1 and L2 — Scoped Authority Proofs and Open Event Obligations **[WC5.1]**\n1073:## C46. HandoffOrdered — D-C10 **[WC5.1]**\n1089:# XI. Event Realization of Reference Protocols — Proposed Block D\n1091:## C47. Spawn, Completion, and Join Events\n1101:## C48. Reference Mutex: Acquire, Unlock, and Grant Events\n1115:## C49. LockOrder, Recovery, and Delegation\n1125:## C50. Realization, Visibility, and Physical Correspondence\n1135:# XII. Safe Executions and Data-Race Freedom — Proposed Block D\n1137:## C51. EncapsulatedTrace and SafeConcurrentTrace **[WC5.1]**\n1148:## C52. Candidate Data-Race-Freedom Theorem and Proof Partition **[WC5.1]**\n1167:## C53. Proof Boundary, Conservativity, and No Freeze\n1181:# Drafting choices","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9de3db35-65e3-4df5-93f4-4ae20be600d9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","defa