{"parentUuid":"5b412eb0-4192-485c-ba95-3dee3be84b35","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2p6s5TVPGfDywonSxfN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W4asASmzrtrA4qs1Gvjwpf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 60,100p Ern/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean; sed -n 1,80p Ern/Concurrency/Encap5R.lean","description":"Read CtrlRight and CtrlRight5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4343,"cache_read_input_tokens":105401,"output_tokens":232,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":67},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4343,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":105401,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4343},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":913,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W4asASmzrtrA4qs1Gvjwpf":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && sed -n 60,100p Ern/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean; sed -n 1,80p Ern/Concurrency/Encap5R.lean","description":"Read CtrlRight and CtrlRight5"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01W4asASmzrtrA4qs1Gvjwpf":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a530e201-3a09-4478-9e21-18b2b6d54124","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch2p6rp5hU2XwwxphhvhM","requestRef":"59249d0e-90ad-44c5-8798-c53436484d58","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c97b96d-8e13-4119-b4b4-dbf0f5e30019","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:22:38.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"9c97b96d-8e13-4119-b4b4-dbf0f5e30019","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0dd0571a-6379-45f8-954f-cbdecd0ea155","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4asASmzrtrA4qs1Gvjwpf","type":"tool_result","content":"of `m` at position `controlField`. -/\ndef ControlOf (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) : Option Nat :=\n  match (s.A[e.guarded]?).map (·.holder) with\n  | some (Holder.place h) =>\n    match parentOf s.P h with\n    | some m =>\n      if (kids s.P m)[L.guardedField]? = some h then (kids s.P m)[L.controlField]? else none\n    | none => none\n  | _ => none\n\n/-- The `S3` whose current frame is `f` (WC4 C14: `SyncAuthorized` names the requesting frame;\nSpec 1 §43 reads the stack only through its top and membership). -/\ndef SC.viewAt (s : SC) (f : Nat) : S3 :=\n  { s.flat with F := f :: s.frames.filter fun g => decide (g ≠ f) }\n\n/-- WC4 C14.3: the frame `f` has effective and exercisable access to `ControlOf(e)` under the\ncondition of Spec 1 §68.2: some authority exercisable by `f` in a mode at least `Observe` has a\npresent effective mode on the controller. -/\ndef CtrlRight (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (ControlOf L s e) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range s.A.length,\n    (s.viewAt f).ExercisableAt a .observe ∧ effective s.flat a ctl ≠ none) False\n\n/-- Decidability of the controller fact. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Decidable (CtrlRight L s e f) := by\n  unfold CtrlRight; infer_instance\n\n/-- The authorization facts of WC4 C14 for an entry: C14.1 (live), C14.2 (`grant = none`), C14.3\n(`CtrlRight`). -/\ndef EntryAuth (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Prop :=\n  e.Live s ∧ e.grant = none ∧ CtrlRight L s e f\n\n/-- Decidability of the library authorization of an entry. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Decidable (EntryAuth L s e f) := by\n  unfold EntryAuth; infer_instance\n\n/-- Instantiation of `K_C.SyncAuthorized(state, sync_registry, guarded, requesting_frame)` by the\nlibrary (WC4 C14, C25): an entry of the registry with the requested `guarded` identity satisfies\nthe authorization facts C14.1–C14.3. -/\ndef LibSyncAuthorized (L : MutexLayout) (reg : SyncReg) (s : SC) (g f : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∃ e ∈ reg, e.guarded = g ∧ EntryAuth L s e f\n\nimport Ern.Concurrency.Encap5C\n\n/-!\n# Exclusion extended to the rights over places\n\nBrief of milestone 4, \"étendre l'exclusion aux droits sur les places\". `ChainExcl`\n(`Ern.Concurrency.Encap5C`) reads the authority argument of `derive`, `split`, `read`, `write` and\n`writeShared`; it does not read the right over a place (`HasRight`, Spec 1 §43) of the other\noperations, and W-GS (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v6 §2 sexies) writes the protected data without the lock\nthrough such a right. `PlaceExcl` requires the right premises of the preconditions to hold without\na live `guarded` on the holder chain (`HasRight5`). It is a proposition of the brief, tested here\nand not decided; the existing definitions, `ChainExcl` and `Encap5C` included, are unchanged.\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access\n\n/-! ## Rights over places without a live `guarded` -/\n\n/-- `HasRight(s, m, q)` (Spec 1 §43) read from the current frame of `c`, with `Exer5` in place of\n`ExercisableAt` (brief of milestone 4, task 2): some authority exercisable by a holder chain without\na live `guarded` has, over every leaf of `q`'s footprint, an effective mode permitting `m`. -/\ndef HasRight5 (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (m : Mode) (q : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∃ a ∈ List.range st.1.A.length, Exer5 st.1 st.2 c a m ∧\n    ∀ l ∈ footprint st.1.P q, Allows (effective st.1.flat a l) m\n\n/-- Decidability of `HasRight5`. -/\ninstance (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (m : Mode) (q : Nat) : Decidable (HasRight5 st c m q) := by\n  unfold HasRight5; infer_instance\n\n/-- `HolderRight` (Spec 1 §62.2) with `HasRight5` in its place case. -/\ndef HolderRight5 (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) : Holder → Prop\n  | .frame _ => True\n  | .place p => HasRight5 st c .modify p\n\n/-- Decidability of `HolderRight5`. -/\ninstance (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (h : Holder) : Decidable (HolderRight5 st c h) := by\n  cases h <;> unfold HolderRight5 <;> infer_instance\n\n/-- `CtrlRight` (WC5 C14.3, read with the access condition of Spec 1 §68.2) from the current frame\nof `c`, with `Exer5` in place of `ExercisableAt`. -/\ndef CtrlRight5 (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg) (e : SyncEntry) (c : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (ControlOf L st.1 e) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range st.1.A.length,\n    Exer5 st.1 st.2 c a .observe ∧ effective st.1.flat a ctl ≠ none) False\n\n/-- Decidability of `CtrlRight5`. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg) (e : SyncEntry) (c : Nat) :\n    Decidable (CtrlRight5 L st e c) := by\n  unfold CtrlRight5; infer_instance\n\n/-- `MetaRight` (Spec 1 §36, §77.1, §78.1) with `HasRight5` over the arena value, when the arena\nvalue exists. -/\ndef MetaRight5 (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (E : Arena.ArenaEntry) : Prop :=\n  OptP (Arena.arenaValue st.1.flat E) (fun v => HasRight5 st c .modify v) True\n\n/-- Decidability of `MetaRight5`. -/\ninstance (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (E : Arena.ArenaEntry) : Decidable (MetaRight5 st c E) := by\n  unfold MetaRight5; infer_instance\n\n/-- The right premise of each transfer phase of the by-value composite (WC5 C5.2, C5 item 1, Spec 1\n§63.1: `ValTransferPre.srcRight`) as `HasRight5`, each on the state produced by the earlier\ntransfers, in the declared order. -/\ndef ValRights5 (reg : SyncReg) (c : Nat) : SC → List (Nat × Nat) → Prop\n  | _, [] => True\n  | t, v :: vs => HasRight5 (t, reg) c .modify v.1 ∧ ValRights5 reg c (transferEffC t c v.1 v.2) vs\n\n/-- Decidability of `ValRights5`. -/\ninstance instDecidableValRights5 (reg : SyncReg) (c : Nat) :\n    (t : SC) → (vs : List (Nat × Nat)) → Decidable (ValRights5 reg c t vs)\n  | _, [] => isTrue trivial\n  | t, v :: vs =>\n    haveI := instDecidableValRights5 reg c (transferEffC t c v.1 v.2) vs\n    inferInstanceAs (Decidable (HasRight5 (t, reg) c .modify v.1 ∧ _))\n\n/-! ## The extended exclusion -/\n\n/-- `PlaceExcl` (brief of milestone 4, task 2): each right premise over a place of the precondition\nholds as `HasRight5` on the same place, in the state where the premise is read:\n`release` (Spec 1 §62.2, place-held case), `transfer` (§63.1, source and destination), `depend`","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"302b33a3-502d-40be-adfa-746c0cf57569","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:22:38.619Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"of `m` at position `controlField`. -/\ndef ControlOf (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) : Option Nat :=\n  match (s.A[e.guarded]?).map (·.holder) with\n  | some (Holder.place h) =>\n    match parentOf s.P h with\n    | some m =>\n      if (kids s.P m)[L.guardedField]? = some h then (kids s.P m)[L.controlField]? else none\n    | none => none\n  | _ => none\n\n/-- The `S3` whose current frame is `f` (WC4 C14: `SyncAuthorized` names the requesting frame;\nSpec 1 §43 reads the stack only through its top and membership). -/\ndef SC.viewAt (s : SC) (f : Nat) : S3 :=\n  { s.flat with F := f :: s.frames.filter fun g => decide (g ≠ f) }\n\n/-- WC4 C14.3: the frame `f` has effective and exercisable access to `ControlOf(e)` under the\ncondition of Spec 1 §68.2: some authority exercisable by `f` in a mode at least `Observe` has a\npresent effective mode on the controller. -/\ndef CtrlRight (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (ControlOf L s e) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range s.A.length,\n    (s.viewAt f).ExercisableAt a .observe ∧ effective s.flat a ctl ≠ none) False\n\n/-- Decidability of the controller fact. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Decidable (CtrlRight L s e f) := by\n  unfold CtrlRight; infer_instance\n\n/-- The authorization facts of WC4 C14 for an entry: C14.1 (live), C14.2 (`grant = none`), C14.3\n(`CtrlRight`). -/\ndef EntryAuth (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Prop :=\n  e.Live s ∧ e.grant = none ∧ CtrlRight L s e f\n\n/-- Decidability of the library authorization of an entry. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Decidable (EntryAuth L s e f) := by\n  unfold EntryAuth; infer_instance\n\n/-- Instantiation of `K_C.SyncAuthorized(state, sync_registry, guarded, requesting_frame)` by the\nlibrary (WC4 C14, C25): an entry of the registry with the requested `guarded` identity satisfies\nthe authorization facts C14.1–C14.3. -/\ndef LibSyncAuthorized (L : MutexLayout) (reg : SyncReg) (s : SC) (g f : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∃ e ∈ reg, e.guarded = g ∧ EntryAuth L s e f\n\nimport Ern.Concurrency.Encap5C\n\n/-!\n# Exclusion extended to the rights over places\n\nBrief of milestone 4, \"étendre l'exclusion aux droits sur les places\". `ChainExcl`\n(`Ern.Concurrency.Encap5C`) reads the authority argument of `derive`, `split`, `read`, `write` and\n`writeShared`; it does not read the right over a place (`HasRight`, Spec 1 §43) of the other\noperations, and W-GS (`corpus-spec2-m3.md` v6 §2 sexies) writes the protected data without the lock\nthrough such a right. `PlaceExcl` requires the right premises of the preconditions to hold without\na live `guarded` on the holder chain (`HasRight5`). It is a proposition of the brief, tested here\nand not decided; the existing definitions, `ChainExcl` and `Encap5C` included, are unchanged.\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.Concurrency\n\nopen Ern.MemoryModel Ern.MemoryModel.Access\n\n/-! ## Rights over places without a live `guarded` -/\n\n/-- `HasRight(s, m, q)` (Spec 1 §43) read from the current frame of `c`, with `Exer5` in place of\n`ExercisableAt` (brief of milestone 4, task 2): some authority exercisable by a holder chain without\na live `guarded` has, over every leaf of `q`'s footprint, an effective mode permitting `m`. -/\ndef HasRight5 (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (m : Mode) (q : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∃ a ∈ List.range st.1.A.length, Exer5 st.1 st.2 c a m ∧\n    ∀ l ∈ footprint st.1.P q, Allows (effective st.1.flat a l) m\n\n/-- Decidability of `HasRight5`. -/\ninstance (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (m : Mode) (q : Nat) : Decidable (HasRight5 st c m q) := by\n  unfold HasRight5; infer_instance\n\n/-- `HolderRight` (Spec 1 §62.2) with `HasRight5` in its place case. -/\ndef HolderRight5 (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) : Holder → Prop\n  | .frame _ => True\n  | .place p => HasRight5 st c .modify p\n\n/-- Decidability of `HolderRight5`. -/\ninstance (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (h : Holder) : Decidable (HolderRight5 st c h) := by\n  cases h <;> unfold HolderRight5 <;> infer_instance\n\n/-- `CtrlRight` (WC5 C14.3, read with the access condition of Spec 1 §68.2) from the current frame\nof `c`, with `Exer5` in place of `ExercisableAt`. -/\ndef CtrlRight5 (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg) (e : SyncEntry) (c : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (ControlOf L st.1 e) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range st.1.A.length,\n    Exer5 st.1 st.2 c a .observe ∧ effective st.1.flat a ctl ≠ none) False\n\n/-- Decidability of `CtrlRight5`. -/\ninstance (L : MutexLayout) (st : SC × SyncReg) (e : SyncEntry) (c : Nat) :\n    Decidable (CtrlRight5 L st e c) := by\n  unfold CtrlRight5; infer_instance\n\n/-- `MetaRight` (Spec 1 §36, §77.1, §78.1) with `HasRight5` over the arena value, when the arena\nvalue exists. -/\ndef MetaRight5 (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (E : Arena.ArenaEntry) : Prop :=\n  OptP (Arena.arenaValue st.1.flat E) (fun v => HasRight5 st c .modify v) True\n\n/-- Decidability of `MetaRight5`. -/\ninstance (st : SC × SyncReg) (c : Nat) (E : Arena.ArenaEntry) : Decidable (MetaRight5 st c E) := by\n  unfold MetaRight5; infer_instance\n\n/-- The right premise of each transfer phase of the by-value composite (WC5 C5.2, C5 item 1, Spec 1\n§63.1: `ValTransferPre.srcRight`) as `HasRight5`, each on the state produced by the earlier\ntransfers, in the declared order. -/\ndef ValRights5 (reg : SyncReg) (c : Nat) : SC → List (Nat × Nat) → Prop\n  | _, [] => True\n  | t, v :: vs => HasRight5 (t, reg) c .modify v.1 ∧ ValRights5 reg c (transferEffC t c v.1 v.2) vs\n\n/-- Decidability of `ValRights5`. -/\ninstance instDecidableValRights5 (reg : SyncReg) (c : Nat) :\n    (t : SC) → (vs : List (Nat × Nat)) → Decidable (ValRights5 reg c t vs)\n  | _, [] => isTrue trivial\n  | t, v :: vs =>\n    haveI := instDecidableValRights5 reg c (transferEffC t c v.1 v.2) vs\n    inferInstanceAs (Decidable (HasRight5 (t, reg) c .modify v.1 ∧ _))\n\n/-! ## The extended exclusion -/\n\n/-- `PlaceExcl` (brief of milestone 4, task 2): each right premise over a place of the precondition\nholds as `HasRight5` on the same place, in the state where the premise is read:\n`release` (Spec 1 §62.2, place-held case), `transfer` (§63.1, source and destination), `depend`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a530e201-3a09-4478-9e21-18b2b6d54124","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9c97b96d-8e13-4119-b4b4-dbf0f5e30019","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"e64