{"parentUuid":"ed8175c1-465a-4a54-bebe-9a9251a4e336","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0dd0571a-6379-45f8-954f-cbdecd0ea155","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ubzacqzkqk4ytb1V9BgYUj","type":"tool_result","content":"Ern/Concurrency/Context.lean:63:def SC.stk (s : SC) (c : Nat) : List Nat :=\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-64-  match s.C[c]? with\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-65-  | some x => if x.life = .live then x.stack else []\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-66-  | none => []\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-67-\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-68-/-- Parent of the initial frame of context `c` (WC4 C3). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-69-def SC.ctxParent (s : SC) (c : Nat) : Option Nat := (s.C[c]?).bind (·.parent)\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-70-\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-71-/-- Globally live frames: the frames of the stacks of live contexts (WC4 C2). -/\n--\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean:76:def SC.flat (s : SC) : S3 :=\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-77-  { F := s.frames, nF := s.nF, P := s.P, I := s.I, A := s.A, D := s.D, dead := s.dead,\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-78-    pins := s.pins }\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-79-\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-80-/-- The `S3` seen by executing context `c` (WC4 C2): the stack of `c` first, so that the current\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-81-frame is the top of its local stack, followed by the other globally live frames. It is the `S₃`\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-82-view of WC4 C2 (candidate P1) on which `K.Satisfiable` of an `alloc` executed by `c` is evaluated\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-83-(`alloc_ok_satisfiable`, `alloc_fail_unsatisfiable`). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean:84:def SC.view (s : SC) (c : Nat) : S3 :=\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-85-  { s.flat with F := s.stk c ++ s.frames.filter fun f => decide (f ∉ s.stk c) }\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-86-\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-87-/-- Kernel components of an `S3` written back into `s`; contexts unchanged (WC4 C2). -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean:88:def SC.set (s : SC) (t : S3) : SC :=\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-89-  { s with nF := t.nF, P := t.P, I := t.I, A := t.A, D := t.D, dead := t.dead, pins := t.pins }\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-90-\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-91-/-! ## Single-context states (WC4 C24) -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-92-\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-93-/-- Single-context state (WC4 C24): exactly one context, the initial one, live, without\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-94-parent. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-95-def SC.Single (s : SC) : Prop := ∃ stk, s.C = [⟨stk, .live, none⟩]\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-96-\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean:72:def SC.viewAt (s : SC) (f : Nat) : S3 :=\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-73-  { s.flat with F := f :: s.frames.filter fun g => decide (g ≠ f) }\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-74-\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-75-/-- WC4 C14.3: the frame `f` has effective and exercisable access to `ControlOf(e)` under the\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-76-condition of Spec 1 §68.2: some authority exercisable by `f` in a mode at least `Observe` has a\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-77-present effective mode on the controller. -/\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-78-def CtrlRight (L : MutexLayout) (s : SC) (e : SyncEntry) (f : Nat) : Prop :=\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-79-  OptP (ControlOf L s e) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range s.A.length,\nErn/Concurrency/SyncLib.lean-80-    (s.viewAt f).ExercisableAt a .observe ∧ effective s.flat a ctl ≠ none) False\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean:190:structure FramesC (s : SC) : Prop where\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-191-  /-- WC4 C3: the initial context, context 0, is live and its initial frame, the base frame of\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-192-  Spec 1 §39, has no parent. -/\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-193-  initial : OptP (s.C[0]?) (fun x => x.life = .live ∧ x.parent = none) False\nErn/Concurrency/Context.lean-194-  /-- WC4 C3: every live context has a nonempty local stack. -/\nErn/Concurrency/C