{"parentUuid":"10b1fe29-81d6-4d86-bdce-26b961191d21","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2pfZAcuk2yCFynzFAiD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DfRa5CEC9h1neLpsnf6CXG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/Downloads && sed -n 260,282p ERN_WC5_3_FINAL.md; sed -n 1028,1042p ERN_WC5_3_FINAL.md","description":"Read WC5.3 C14 and C43"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3781,"cache_read_input_tokens":196585,"output_tokens":178,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":34},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3781,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":178,"cache_read_input_tokens":196585,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3781},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":649,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DfRa5CEC9h1neLpsnf6CXG":{"command":"cd ~/Downloads && sed -n 260,282p ERN_WC5_3_FINAL.md; sed -n 1028,1042p ERN_WC5_3_FINAL.md","description":"Read WC5.3 C14 and C43"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"72656dfc-734e-4b13-9a99-9cd871444aa6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch2pfYskDeuh1GcQV8h2y","requestRef":"1587fb53-30ac-425d-86ce-f2cf2e1db775","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a8ebba4-03ac-47c4-8ada-ba588932395c","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:30:02.072Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"3a8ebba4-03ac-47c4-8ada-ba588932395c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0dd0571a-6379-45f8-954f-cbdecd0ea155","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DfRa5CEC9h1neLpsnf6CXG","type":"tool_result","content":"## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n\n`K_C` extends the unchanged Spec 1 contract `K`. The proposed concurrent authorization predicate accepts the **current logical synchronization registry as an explicit external argument**:\n\n```\nK_C.SyncAuthorized(state, sync_registry, guarded, requesting_frame)\n```\n\nThe registry is supplied by the library contract and is not part of the kernel state `S_C`. It must refer to the same logical registry state used for the candidate library transition.\n\nFor the reference mutex, the library's **authorization facts**, and only these facts, are:\n\n1. There exists a live registered entry with the requested `guarded` identity.\n2. That entry has `grant = none`.\n3. The requesting frame has the required effective and exercisable access to `ControlOf(entry)` under the controller-access obligation corresponding to Spec 1 §68.2.\n\nThe library must prove, under `ConcurrentWF`, the applicable Spec 1 invariants, `SyncInv`, `GrantDiscipline`, and the abstraction's encapsulation contract, that these facts imply the remaining authority prerequisites for `deriveSync`, including origin-chain validity, sufficient effective mode, absence of blocking descendants and I1 conservation.\n\nThe opaque authorization predicate must not be defined by simply conjoining the conclusions the library is required to prove. Its instantiation is state-dependent, and correctness must be reestablished for every enabled acquisition.\n\n`SyncAuthorized` does not create an authority, does not introduce ambient context rights, and cannot be used outside the corresponding valid synchronization contract. The precise synchronized physical realization remains deferred under `OB-C05`.\n\n## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\n## C43. Context Capability and Current-Frame Exercise **[WC5.1]**\n\nDefine, provisionally, for state `s`, execution context `c`, and logical leaf `l`:\n\n```\ncap(s, c, l) ∈ { none, Observe, Modify }\n```\n\nFor the safe-handoff proof, it is the greatest **effective** mode on `l` attributable to `c` through active authorities held by its live frames, **including suspended frames**, or held in a place through a valid holder chain, **provided the attributing chain does not pass through the `guarded` authority of any live synchronization entry** **[WC5.1]**. This guarded-chain-excluding capability is `cap5` in the exploratory Lean model. Its `Attr5` attribution relation deliberately treats live `guarded` authorities as unavailable for attribution but permits a valid frame-held grant and its legally held descendants. It does not change the rights of any authority in the frozen Spec 1.\n\n`cap` is **not** `ExercisableAt`. The latter applies the frozen §43 rules to the executing context's **current frame** and is used to decide **kernel** operation preconditions; C22.6 separately restricts which successful kernel operations the **safe interface** may expose. `cap` summarizes guarded-chain-excluding contextual entitlement across the context's frames and relevant held places, including rights not currently exercisable from the top frame. Derivation, reborrowing and frame changes need not terminate a context's `cap` merely because an individual authority becomes inactive or non-exercisable. **[WC5.1]** The unrestricted contextual capability (`cap` in the earlier Lean exploration) is distinguished here as **raw contextual capability**, not the quantity used by L1/L2: W-GR refutes raw capability-loss locality.\n\nFor two distinct contexts, present `cap` values on a leaf are **incompatible** when at least one is `Modify`; for `Confined`, any two present capabilities are incompatible under the additional safe-storage contract. This is a proposed abstraction for L1/L2, not a new sequential mode or authority identity.\n\n## C44. Scope of Exclusive Handoff Ordering\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"840fc0d5-d634-4b2a-bc12-a23f1c8c8371","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:30:02.321Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n\n`K_C` extends the unchanged Spec 1 contract `K`. The proposed concurrent authorization predicate accepts the **current logical synchronization registry as an explicit external argument**:\n\n```\nK_C.SyncAuthorized(state, sync_registry, guarded, requesting_frame)\n```\n\nThe registry is supplied by the library contract and is not part of the kernel state `S_C`. It must refer to the same logical registry state used for the candidate library transition.\n\nFor the reference mutex, the library's **authorization facts**, and only these facts, are:\n\n1. There exists a live registered entry with the requested `guarded` identity.\n2. That entry has `grant = none`.\n3. The requesting frame has the required effective and exercisable access to `ControlOf(entry)` under the controller-access obligation corresponding to Spec 1 §68.2.\n\nThe library must prove, under `ConcurrentWF`, the applicable Spec 1 invariants, `SyncInv`, `GrantDiscipline`, and the abstraction's encapsulation contract, that these facts imply the remaining authority prerequisites for `deriveSync`, including origin-chain validity, sufficient effective mode, absence of blocking descendants and I1 conservation.\n\nThe opaque authorization predicate must not be defined by simply conjoining the conclusions the library is required to prove. Its instantiation is state-dependent, and correctness must be reestablished for every enabled acquisition.\n\n`SyncAuthorized` does not create an authority, does not introduce ambient context rights, and cannot be used outside the corresponding valid synchronization contract. The precise synchronized physical realization remains deferred under `OB-C05`.\n\n## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\n## C43. Context Capability and Current-Frame Exercise **[WC5.1]**\n\nDefine, provisionally, for state `s`, execution context `c`, and logical leaf `l`:\n\n```\ncap(s, c, l) ∈ { none, Observe, Modify }\n```\n\nFor the safe-handoff proof, it is the greatest **effective** mode on `l` attributable to `c` through active authorities held by its live frames, **including suspended frames**, or held in a place through a valid holder chain, **provided the attributing chain does not pass through the `guarded` authority of any live synchronization entry** **[WC5.1]**. This guarded-chain-excluding capability is `cap5` in the exploratory Lean model. Its `Attr5` attribution relation deliberately treats live `guarded` authorities as unavailable for attribution but permits a valid frame-held grant and its legally held descendants. It does not change the rights of any authority in the frozen Spec 1.\n\n`cap` is **not** `ExercisableAt`. The latter applies the frozen §43 rules to the executing context's **current frame** and is used to decide **kernel** operation preconditions; C22.6 separately restricts which successful kernel operations the **safe interface** may expose. `cap` summarizes guarded-chain-excluding contextual entitlement across the context's frames and relevant held places, including rights not currently exercisable from the top frame. Derivation, reborrowing and frame changes need not terminate a context's `cap` merely because an individual authority becomes inactive or non-exercisable. **[WC5.1]** The unrestricted contextual capability (`cap` in the earlier Lean exploration) is distinguished here as **raw contextual capability**, not the quantity used by L1/L2: W-GR refutes raw capability-loss locality.\n\nFor two distinct contexts, present `cap` values on a leaf are **incompatible** when at least one is `Modify`; for `Confined`, any two present capabilities are incompatible under the additional safe-storage contract. This is a proposed abstraction for L1/L2, not a new sequential mode or authority identity.\n\n## C44. Scope of Exclusive Handoff Ordering","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"72656dfc-734e-4b13-9a99-9cd871444aa6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3a8ebba4-03ac-47c4-8ada-ba588932395c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
